TURATH_CHUNK(0,[{"num":-1,"demo":true,"sanad":"حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو النُّعْمَانِ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنَا حَمَّادُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنَا","matn":["أَنَسُ بْنُ سِيرِينَ ، قَالَ : قُلْتُ لِابْنِ عُمَرَ : أَرَأَيْتَ الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ قَبْلَ صَلاَةِ الغَدَاةِ أُطِيلُ فِيهِمَا القِرَاءَةَ ، فَقَالَ : كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وسَلَّمَ يُصَلِّي مِنَ اللَّيْلِ مَثْنَى مَثْنَى ، وَيُوتِرُ بِرَكْعَةٍ ، وَيُصَلِّي الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ قَبْلَ صَلاَةِ الغَدَاةِ ، وَكَأَنَّ الأَذَانَ بِأُذُنَيْهِ قَالَ حَمَّادٌ : أَيْ سُرْعَةً"],"takhrij":"","grade":"","chapter_ar":"","chapter_ur":"نمونہ: سند اور متن کے دو رنگ","part_ar":"","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"","chapter_en":"","part_en":"","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":0,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":0,"content":{},"tuhfa":{}},{"num":1,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّمَا الْأَعْمَالُ بِالنِّيَّةِ، وَإِنَّمَا لِامْرِئٍ مَا نَوَى، فَمَنْ كَانَتْ هِجْرَتُهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، فَهِجْرَتُهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، وَمَنْ كَانَتْ هِجْرَتُهُ لِدُنْيَا يُصِيبُهَا أَوِ امْرَأَةٍ يَتَزَوَّجُهَا، فَهِجْرَتُهُ إِلَى مَا هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في كتاب كيف بدء الوحي (1) عن الحميدي عبدالله بن الزبير قال: حدثنا سفيان، قال: حدثنا يحيى بن سعيد الأنصاري، قال: أخبرني محمد بن إبراهيم التيمي، أنه سمع علقمة بن وقاص الليثي يقول: سمعت عمر بن الخطاب على المنبر قال: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إنما الأعمال بالنيات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1, 5070) and Muslim (1907).","chapter_en":"Actions Are Only by Intentions","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Actions are only by intentions, and every person will have only what he intended. Whoever’s migration was to Allah and His Messenger, then his migration was to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever’s migration was for some worldly gain he sought or for a woman he wished to marry, then his migration was to that for which he migrated.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1542],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1، 5070)، ومسلم (1907)."},{"num":2,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنَّهَا قَالَتْ: أَوَّلُ مَا بُدِئَ بِهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْوَحْيِ الرُّؤْيَا الصَّالِحَةُ فِي النَّوْمِ، فَكَانَ لَا يَرَى رُؤْيَا إِلَّا جَاءَتْ مِثْلَ فَلَقِ الصُّبْحِ، ثُمَّ حُبِّبَ إِلَيْهِ الْخَلَاءُ وَكَانَ يَخْلُو بِغَارِ حِرَاءٍ، فَيَتَحَنَّثُ فِيهِ وَهُوَ التَّعَبُّدُ اللَّيَالِيَ ذَوَاتِ الْعَدَدِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَنْزِعَ إِلَى أَهْلِهِ وَيَتَزَوَّدُ لِذَلِكَ، ثُمَّ يَرْجِعُ إِلَى خَدِيجَةَ فَيَتَزَوَّدُ لِمِثْلِهَا حَتَّى جَاءَهُ الْحَقُّ وَهُوَ فِي غَارِ حِرَاءٍ، فَجَاءَهُ الْمَلَكُ، فَقَالَ: اقْرَأْ، قَالَ: مَا أَنَا بِقَارِئٍ، قَالَ: فَأَخَذَنِي فَغَطَّنِي حَتَّى بَلَغَ مِنِّي الْجَهْدَ، ثُمَّ أَرْسَلَنِي، فَقَالَ: اقْرَأْ، قُلْتُ: مَا أَنَا بِقَارِئٍ، فَأَخَذَنِي فَغَطَّنِي الثَّانِيَةَ حَتَّى بَلَغَ مِنِّي الْجَهْدَ، ثُمَّ أَرْسَلَنِي، فَقَالَ: اقْرَأْ، فَقُلْتُ مَا أَنَا بِقَارِئٍ، فَأَخَذَنِي فَغَطَّنِي الثَّالِثَةَ، ثُمَّ أَرْسَلَنِي فَقَالَ: ﴿اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ (1) خَلَقَ الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ (2) اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ (3) الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ (4) عَلَّمَ الْإِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ (5)﴾ [سورة العلق: 1، 5]. فَرَجَعَ بِهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْجُفُ فُؤَادُهُ، فَدَخَلَ عَلَى خَدِيجَةَ بِنْتِ خُوَيْلِدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا، فَقَالَ: زَمِّلُونِي زَمِّلُونِي، فَزَمَّلُوهُ حَتَّى ذَهَبَ عَنْهُ الرَّوْعُ، فَقَالَ لِخَدِيجَةَ، وَأَخْبَرَهَا الْخَبَرَ: لَقَدْ خَشِيتُ عَلَى نَفْسِي، فَقَالَتْ خَدِيجَةُ: كَلَّا وَاللَّهِ مَا يُخْزِيكَ اللَّهُ أَبَدًا، إِنَّكَ لَتَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ، وَتَحْمِلُ الْكَلَّ، وَتَكْسِبُ الْمَعْدُومَ، وَتَقْرِي الضَّيْفَ، وَتُعِينُ عَلَى نَوَائِبِ الْحَقِّ.","فَانْطَلَقَتْ بِهِ خَدِيجَةُ حَتَّى أَتَتْ بِهِ وَرَقَةَ بْنَ نَوْفَلِ بْنِ أَسَدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الْعُزَّى ابْنَ عَمِّ خَدِيجَةَ، وَكَانَ امْرَأً تَنَصَّرَ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، وَكَانَ يَكْتُبُ الْكِتَابَ الْعِبْرَانِيَّ، فَيَكْتُبُ مِنَ الْإِنْجِيلِ بِالْعِبْرَانِيَّةِ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَنْ يَكْتُبَ، وَكَانَ شَيْخًا كَبِيرًا قَدْ عَمِيَ، فَقَالَتْ لَهُ خَدِيجَةُ: يَا ابْنَ عَمِّ، اسْمَعْ مِنَ ابْنِ أَخِيكَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ وَرَقَةُ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، مَاذَا تَرَى، فَأَخْبَرَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَبَرَ مَا رَأَى، فَقَالَ لَهُ وَرَقَةُ: هَذَا النَّامُوسُ الَّذِي نَزَّلَ اللَّهُ عَلَى مُوسَى صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، يَا لَيْتَنِي فِيهَا جَذَعًا، لَيْتَنِي أَكُونُ حَيًّا إِذْ يُخْرِجُكَ قَوْمُكَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَوَمُخْرِجِيَّ هُمْ، قَالَ: نَعَمْ، لَمْ يَأْتِ رَجُلٌ قَطُّ بِمِثْلِ مَا جِئْتَ بِهِ إِلَّا عُودِيَ، وَإِنْ يُدْرِكْنِي يَوْمُكَ أَنْصُرْكَ نَصْرًا مُؤَزَّرًا، ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْشَبْ وَرَقَةُ أَنْ تُوُفِّيَ وَفَتَرَ الْوَحْيُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (3)، ومسلم في الإيمان (160) كلاهما من حديث الليث بن سعد عن عُقيل بن خالد عن ابن شهاب عن عروة يقول: سمعت عائشة، فذكرت الحديث. واللفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بدء الوحي إلى رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3) and Muslim (160), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"The Beginning of Revelation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers may Allah be pleased with her, said: The first form in which revelation began to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was through true and righteous dreams during sleep. He would not see a dream except that it came true as clearly as the break of dawn. Then solitude was made beloved to him. He would seclude himself in the Cave of Ḥirāʾ and devote himself there to worship for a number of nights before returning to his family. He would take provisions for that period, then return to Khadījah and take provisions for another similar period, until the truth came to him while he was in the Cave of Ḥirāʾ. The angel came to him and said, “Read.” He replied, “I am not a reader.” He said, “He seized me and pressed me until I reached the limit of my endurance, then released me and said, ‘Read.’ I replied, ‘I am not a reader.’ He seized me and pressed me a second time until I reached the limit of my endurance, then released me and said, ‘Read.’ I replied, ‘I am not a reader.’ He seized me and pressed me a third time, then released me and said: ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created; created the human being from a clinging substance. Read, and your Lord is the Most Generous, who taught by the pen, taught the human being what he did not know.’” [Sūrat al-ʿAlaq 96:1–5] The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned with these verses, his heart trembling. He entered upon Khadījah bint Khuwaylid may Allah be pleased with her and said, “Cover me! Cover me!” They covered him until his fear subsided. He then informed Khadījah of what had happened and said, “I feared for myself.” Khadījah replied, “Never! By Allah, Allah will never disgrace you. You maintain ties of kinship, bear the burdens of those unable to bear them themselves, assist the destitute, honor the guest, and help people through the calamities that befall them in the cause of truth.”","Khadījah then took him to Waraqah ibn Nawfal ibn Asad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā, a cousin of Khadījah. He had embraced Christianity during the pre-Islamic period and used to write in Hebrew. He would write from the Gospel in Hebrew whatever Allah willed him to write. He had become an elderly man and had lost his sight. Khadījah said to him, “O son of my uncle, listen to your nephew.” Waraqah asked him, “O my nephew, what have you seen?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told him what he had seen. Waraqah said, “This is the Nāmūs whom Allah sent down to Moses. If only I were a young man! If only I were alive when your people drive you out!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, “Will they drive me out?” He replied, “Yes. No man has ever brought what you have brought except that he was opposed. If I live to see your day, I will support you with mighty support.” Not long afterward, Waraqah died, and revelation ceased for a period."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ كَمَا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَى نُوحٍ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ﴾","[النساء: ١٦٣]"],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“Indeed, We have revealed to you as We revealed to Noah and the prophets after him.”","[Sūrat al-Nisāʾ 4:163]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3)، ومسلم (160)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":3,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ :مَا مِنَ الْأَنْبِيَاءِ نَبِيٌّ إِلَّا أُعْطِيَ مَا مِثْلهُ آمَنَ عَلَيْهِ الْبَشَرُ، وَإِنَّمَا كَانَ الَّذِي أُوتِيتُ وَحْيًا أَوْحَاهُ اللَّهُ إِلَيَّ فَأَرْجُو أَنْ أَكُونَ أَكْثَرَهُمْ تَابِعًا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في فضائل القرآن (4981)، ومسلم في الإيمان (152) كلاهما من حديث الليث، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبريّ، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره، واللّفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الوحي الذي أوحاه الله إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4981) and Muslim (152), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"The Revelation Allah Gave to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There was no prophet among the prophets except that he was given signs by which people came to believe. What I have been given is revelation that Allah revealed to me, so I hope that I will have the greatest number of followers on the Day of Resurrection.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In Muslim’s wording:","“There was no prophet except that he was given signs by which people believed,” followed by wording with a similar meaning.","That is, every prophet was given signs and miracles sufficient to establish his truth and cause people to believe in him. As for the Prophet’s great and manifest miracle, it is the Qurʾān, the like of which was given to no one else."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[733,9658,11819,11895,12747],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4981)، ومسلم (152)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":4,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنَّ الْحَارِثَ بْنَ هِشَامٍ سَأَل رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، كَيْفَ يَأْتِيكَ الْوَحْيُ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَحْيَانًا يَأْتِينِي مِثْلَ صَلْصَلَةِ الْجَرَسِ، وَهُوَ أَشَدُّهُ عَلَيَّ فَيُفْصَمُ عَنِّي، وَقَدْ وَعَيْتُ عَنْهُ مَا قَالَ، وَأَحْيَانًا يَتَمَثَّلُ لِي الْمَلَكُ رَجُلًا فَيُكَلِّمُنِي فَأَعِي مَا يَقُولُ، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: وَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُهُ يَنْزِلُ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ فِي الْيَوْمِ الشَّدِيدِ الْبَرْدِ فَيَفْصِمُ عَنْهُ، وَإِنَّ جَبِينَهُ لَيَتَفَصَّدُ عَرَقًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في القرآن (7) عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرتْه. ورواه البخاريّ في كتاب بدأ الوحي (2) من طريق مالك به.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب كيف كان ينزل الوحي على رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ (7), al-Bukhārī (2), and Muslim (2333).","chapter_en":"How Revelation Used to Descend Upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers may Allah be pleased with her, reported that al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, how does revelation come to you?” He replied: “Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and that is the most difficult form for me. Then it ceases, and I have fully grasped what was said. At other times, the angel appears to me in the form of a man, speaks to me, and I understand what he says.” ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her said: “I saw revelation descend upon him on an intensely cold day, and when it ceased, his forehead was streaming with sweat.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression «فيفصم» means that it breaks off and departs from him, so that what had overwhelmed him during revelation is lifted."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13229],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (7)، والبخاري (2)، ومسلم (2333)."},{"num":5,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ صَفْوَانَ بْنِ يَعْلَى بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ بِالْجِعْرَانَةِ عَلَيْهِ جُبَّةٌ وَعَلَيْهَا خَلُوقٌ، أَوَ قَالَ: أَثَرُ صُفْرَةٍ، فَقَالَ: كَيْفَ تَأْمُرُنِي أَنْ أَصْنَعَ فِي عُمْرَتِي؟ قَالَ: وَأُنْزِلَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْوَحْيُ، فَسُتِرَ بِثَوْبٍ وَكَانَ يَعْلَى، يَقُولُ: وَدِدْتُ أَنِّي أَرَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ نَزَلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَيَسُرُّكَ أَنْ تَنْظُرَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ، قَالَ: فَرَفَعَ عُمَرُ طَرَفَ الثَّوْبِ فَنَظَرْتُ إِلَيْهِ، لَهُ غَطِيطٌ، قَالَ: وَأَحْسَبُهُ قَالَ: كَغَطِيطِ الْبَكْرِ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا سُرِّيَ عَنْهُ، قَالَ: أَيْنَ السَّائِلُ عَنِ الْعُمْرَةِ؟ اغْسِلْ عَنْكَ أَثَرَ الصُّفْرَةِ، أَوَ قَالَ: أَثَرَ الْخَلُوقِ، وَاخْلَعْ عَنْكَ جُبَّتَكَ، وَاصْنَعْ فِي عُمْرَتِكَ مَا أَنْتَ صَانِعٌ فِي حَجِّكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل القرآن (4985)، ومسلم في الحج (1180: 6) كلاهما من حديث همام، حدثنا عطاء بن أبي رباح، قال: أخبرني صفوان بن يعلى فذكره. واللفظ لمسلم ولفظ البخاري نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب كيف كان ينزل الوحي على رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4985) and Muslim (1180).","chapter_en":"How Revelation Used to Descend Upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṣafwān ibn Yaʿlā ibn Umayyah narrated from his father may Allah be pleased with him: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Jiʿrānah. The man was wearing a cloak upon which there was khalūq perfume, or traces of yellow coloring. He asked: “What do you command me to do regarding my ʿumrah?” Revelation then descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he was covered with a cloth. Yaʿlā used to say, “I wished that I could see the Prophet ﷺ while revelation was descending upon him.” ʿUmar said, “Would you like to see the Prophet ﷺ while revelation is descending upon him?” He lifted the edge of the cloth, and I looked at him. He was making a heavy breathing sound—and I think he said, “like the breathing sound of a young camel.” When the state of revelation had passed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Where is the man who asked about ʿumrah? Wash the traces of yellow coloring off yourself” — or he said, “the traces of khalūq” — “remove your cloak, and do during your ʿumrah what you would do during your ḥajj.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word «غطيط» refers to a sound resembling the heavy breathing or snoring of a sleeping person. «كغطيط البكر» means like the breathing sound of a young camel."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4985)، ومسلم (1180)."},{"num":6,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَادَةَ بْنِ الصَّامِتِ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيِّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِذَا أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ، كُرِبَ لِذَلِكَ، وَتَرَبَّدَ وَجْهُهُ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةِ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِذَا أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ، نَكَسَ رَأْسَهُ، وَنَكَسَ أَصْحَابُهُ رُءُوسَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا أُتْلِيَ عَنْهُ، رَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2334) من طريقين عن قتادة، عن الحسن، عن حطّان بن عبدالله، عن عبادة بن الصّامت، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كيف كان ينزل الوحي على رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (2334).","chapter_en":"How Revelation Used to Descend Upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit may Allah be pleased with him reported: Whenever revelation descended upon the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, it caused him distress, and the color of his face would change.","In another narration: Whenever revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would lower his head, and his Companions would lower their heads. When revelation was lifted from him, he would raise his head."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2334)."},{"num":7,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ فِي حَدِيثِ الْإِفْكِ الطَوِيلٍ قَالَتْ: وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ أَنِّي حِينَئِذٍ بَرِيئَةٌ، وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ مُبَرِّئِي بِبَرَاءَتِي، وَلَكِنْ وَاللَّهِ مَا كُنْتُ أَظُنُّ أَنَّ اللَّهَ مُنْزِلٌ فِي شَأْنِي وَحْيًا يُتْلَى لَشَأْنِي فِي نَفْسِي كَانَ أَحْقَرَ مِنْ أَنْ يَتَكَلَّمَ اللَّهُ فِيَّ بِأَمْرٍ، وَلَكِنْ كُنْتُ أَرْجُو أَنْ يَرَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي النَّوْمِ رُؤْيَا يُبَرِّئُنِي اللَّهُ بِهَا، فَوَاللَّهِ مَا رَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَجْلِسَهُ وَلَا خَرَجَ أَحَدٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَيْتِ حَتَّى أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ، فَأَخَذَهُ مَا كَانَ يَأْخُذُهُ مِنَ الْبُرَحَاءِ حَتَّى إِنَّهُ لَيَتَحَدَّرُ مِنْهُ مِنَ الْعَرَقِ مِثْلُ الْجُمَانِ، وَهُوَ فِي يَوْمٍ شَاتٍ مِنْ ثِقَلِ الْقَوْلِ الَّذِي أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازي (4141)، ومسلم في التوبة (2770) كلاهما من حديث إبراهيم بن سعد، عن صالح، عن ابن شهاب، قال: حدثني عروة ابن الزّبير وسعيد بن المسيب وعلقمة بن وقاص وعبيد الله بن عبدالله بن عتبة بن مسعود، عن عائشة، فذكرته في قصة الإفك.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثقل الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4141) and Muslim (2770).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Heaviness of Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her said in the lengthy ḥadīth of the slander: Allah knows that I was innocent and that Allah would declare my innocence. Yet, by Allah, I never imagined that Allah would reveal concerning me a revelation that would be recited. In my own estimation, my affair was too insignificant for Allah to speak concerning me through revelation. Rather, I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might see a dream through which Allah would establish my innocence. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave his seat, nor did anyone leave the household, before revelation descended upon him. He was overtaken by the intense hardship that used to seize him during revelation, until drops of sweat like pearls flowed from him even though it was a cold winter day, because of the heaviness of the words being revealed to him."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿إِنَّا سَنُلْقِي عَلَيْكَ قَوْلًا ثَقِيلًا﴾","[المزمل: ٥]"],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“Indeed, We will cast upon you a weighty word.”","[Sūrat al-Muzzammil 73:5]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4141)، ومسلم (2770)."},{"num":8,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ ثَابِتٍ قَالَ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْلَى عَلَيْهِ: ﴿لَا يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ وَالْمُجَاهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ﴾ [سورة النساء: 95] قَالَ: فَجَاءَهُ ابْنُ أُمِّ مَكْتُومٍ وَهُوَ يُمِلُّهَا عَلَيَّ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّه! لَوْ أَسْتَطِيعُ الْجِهَادَ لَجَاهَدْتُ، وَكَانَ رَجُلًا أَعْمَى فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى عَلَى رَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَفَخِذُهُ عَلَى فَخِذِي، فَثَقُلَتْ عَلَيَّ حَتَّى خِفْتُ أَنَّ تَرُضَّ فَخِذِي، ثُمَّ سُرِّيَ عَنْهُ فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ﴾."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الجهاد (2832)، وفي التفسير bukhari(4592) من طريقين عن إبراهيم بن سعد الزّهريّ، قال: حدّثني صالح بن كيسان، عن ابن شهاب، عن سهل بن سعد السّاعديّ، أنّه قال: رأيتُ مروان بن الحكم جالساً في المسجد، فأقبلتُ حتى جلستُ إلى جنبه، فأخبرنا أنّ زيد بن ثابت أخبره، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثقل الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4592, 2832).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Heaviness of Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Thābit may Allah be pleased with him reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated to me: “Not equal are those believers who remain behind and those who strive in the way of Allah.” [Sūrat al-Nisāʾ 4:95] Then Ibn Umm Maktūm came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, if I were able to perform jihād, I would certainly do so.” He was blind. Revelation then descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his thigh was resting upon my thigh. It became so heavy upon me that I feared my thigh would be crushed. Then it was lifted from him, and Allah revealed: “Except those who are disabled.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4592، 2832)."},{"num":9,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَادَةَ بْنِ الصَّامِتِ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِذَا أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ نَكَسَ رَأْسَهُ، وَنَكَسَ أَصْحَابُهُ رُءُوسَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا أُتْلِيَ عَنْهُ رَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةِ: إِذَا أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الْوَحْيُ كُرِبَ لِذَلِكَ وَتَرَبَّدَ وَجْهُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2335) من طريقين عن قتادة، عن الحسن، عن حطّان بن عبدالله الرّقاشيّ، عن عبادة بن الصّامت، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثقل الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (2335).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Heaviness of Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit may Allah be pleased with him reported: Whenever revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would lower his head, and his Companions would lower their heads. When it was lifted from him, he would raise his head. In another narration:","Whenever revelation descended upon him, it caused him distress, and the color of his face would change."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2335)."},{"num":10,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: إِنْ كَانَ لَيُوحَى إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ، فَتَضْرِبُ بِجِرَانِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (24868) عن سليمان بن داود، قال: أخبرنا عبدالرحمن، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثقل الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (24868), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (2/505).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Heaviness of Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her said: Revelation would sometimes descend upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding his animal, and the animal would lower the underside of its neck to the ground."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her expression «فتضرب بجرانها» refers to the camel lowering its jirān, the underside of its neck. When a camel rests, it stretches its neck toward the ground."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (24868)، وصححه الحاكم (2/505)."},{"num":11,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الْأَنْصَارِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ يُحَدِّثُ عَنْ فَتْرَةِ الْوَحْيِ: فَبَيْنَا أَنَا أَمْشِي، سَمِعْتُ صَوْتًا مِنَ السَّمَاءِ، فَرَفَعْتُ رَأْسِي، فَإِذَا الْمَلَكُ الَّذِي جَاءَنِي بِحِرَاءٍ، جَالِسًا عَلَى كُرْسِيٍّ بَيْنَ السَّمَاءِ وَالأَرْضِ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَجُئِثْتُ مِنْهُ فَرَقًا، فَرَجَعْتُ، فَقُلْتُ: زَمِّلُونِي، زَمِّلُونِي، فَدَثَّرُونِي، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ (1) قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ (2) وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ (3) وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ (4) وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ (5)﴾ [سورة المدثّر: 1، 5] وَهِيَ الأَوْثَانُ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ تَتَابَعَ الْوَحْيُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في بدء الخلق (3238)، ومسلم في الإيمان (161) كلاهما من حديث اللّيث قال: حدثني عُقيل، عن ابن شهاب، قال: أخبرني أبو سلمة بن عبدالرحمن، أنّ جابر بن عبدالله قال: فذكره. واللّفظ لمسلم، ولفظ البخاريّ سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فترة الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in Badʾ al-Khalq (3238) and Muslim in al-Īmān (161).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Pause in Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while speaking about the pause in revelation, said: “While I was walking, I heard a voice from the sky. I raised my head, and there was the angel who had come to me at Ḥirāʾ, seated upon a chair between heaven and earth.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was overcome with fear of him, so I returned and said, ‘Wrap me up! Wrap me up!’ They covered me, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ‘O you who are covered! Arise and warn. Magnify your Lord. Purify your garments. And shun al-rujz.’ [Sūrat al-Muddaththir 74:1–5] Al-rujz here refers to the idols.” He said: “Then revelation continued in succession.” In another narration found in both collections: “Then revelation became intense and continued in succession.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3238)، ومسلم (161)."},{"num":12,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَحْيَى بْنِ أَبِي كَثِيرٍ يَقُولُ: سَأَلْتُ أَبَا سَلَمَةَ بْنُ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ: أَيُّ الْقُرْآنِ أُنْزِلَ قَبْلُ؟ قَالَ: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ﴾. فَقُلْتُ: أَوْ ﴿اقْرَأْ﴾؟ فقَالَ: سَأَلْتُ جَابِرَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ :أَيُّ الْقُرْآنِ أُنْزِلَ قَبْلُ؟ قَالَ:﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ﴾ فَقُلْتُ: أَوْ ﴿اقْرَأْ﴾؟ قَالَ جَابِرٌ: أُحَدِّثُكُمْ مَا حَدَّثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: جَاوَرْتُ بِحِرَاءَ شَهْرًا، فَلَمَّا قَضَيْتُ جِوَارِي نَزَلْتُ، فَاسْتَبْطَنْتُ بَطْنَ الْوَادِي، فَنُودِيتُ فَنَظَرْتُ أَمَامِي، وَخَلْفِي، وَعَنْ يَمِينِي، وَعَنْ شِمَالِي، فَلَمْ أَرَ أَحَدًا، ثُمَّ نُودِيتُ فَنَظَرْتُ، فَلَمْ أَرَ أَحَدًا، ثُمَّ نُودِيتُ فَرَفَعْتُ رَأْسِي، فَإِذَا هُوَ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ فِي الْهَوَاءِ (يعني جبريل) فَأَخَذَتْنِي رَجْفَةٌ شَدِيدَةٌ، فَأَتَيْتُ خَدِيجَةَ فَقُلْتُ: دَثِّرُونِي، فَدَثَّرُونِي، وَصَبُّوا عَلَيَّ مَاءً فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَاالْمُدَّثِّرُ(1) قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ(2) وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ(3) وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ(4) ﴾ [سورة المدثر: 1، 4].","وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: عَلِيُّ بْنُ الْمُبَارَكِ عَنْ يَحْيَى: فَإِذَا هُوَ جَالِسٌ عَلَى عَرْشٍ بَيْنَ السَّمَاءِ وَالأَرْضِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4922)، ومسلم في الإيمان (257، 161) كلاهما من حديث علي بن المبارك، عن يحيى بإسناده مثله، واللفظ لمسلم، وليس في هذه الرواية عند البخاريّ: فإذا هو على العرش في الهواء أو فإذا هو جالس على عرش بين السماء والأرض، ولكن ذكره في رواية حرب، عن يحيى (4924) كما ذكره في رواية ابن شهاب، عن أبي سلمة.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فترة الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tafsīr (4922) with similar wording, and Muslim in al-Īmān (161); the wording here is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Pause in Revelation","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr said: I asked Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, “Which portion of the Qurʾān was revealed first?” He replied: “O you who are covered!” I said, “Or was it ‘Read’?” He replied, “I asked Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, ‘Which portion of the Qurʾān was revealed first?’” He said: “O you who are covered!” I said, “Or was it ‘Read’?” Jābir said, “I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. He said: “I remained in devotional seclusion at Ḥirāʾ for a month. When I completed my period of seclusion, I descended and entered the middle of the valley. I was called, so I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right, and to my left, but I saw no one. Then I was called again, and I looked but saw no one. Then I was called again, so I raised my head, and there he was upon the throne in the air — meaning Jibrīl. A severe trembling seized me. I went to Khadījah and said, ‘Cover me!’ So they covered me and poured water over me. Then Allah Almighty revealed: ‘O you who are covered! Arise and warn. Magnify your Lord. And purify your garments.’ [Sūrat al-Muddaththir 74:1–4]” In the narration of ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak from Yaḥyā: “There he was, seated upon a throne between the heaven and the earth.”","His expression “When I completed my period of jiwār” means his period of devotional seclusion and retreat."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4922) بنحوه، ومسلم (161)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":13,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ فِي قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى:﴿لَا تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ ﴾ [القيامة: 16] قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُعَالِجُ مِنَ التَّنْزِيلِ شِدَّةً وَكَانَ مِمَّا يُحَرِّكُ شَفَتَيْهِ، فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: فَأَنَا أُحَرِّكُهُمَا لَكُمْ كَمَا كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُحَرِّكُهُمَا،وَقَالَ سَعِيدٌ: أَنَا أُحَرِّكُهُمَا كَمَا رَأَيْتُ ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ يُحَرِّكُهُمَا، فَحَرَّكَ شَفَتَيْهِ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿لَا تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ (16) إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهُ وَقُرْآنَهُ (17)﴾ [سورة القيامة: 16، 17] قَالَ: جَمْعُهُ لَهُ فِي صَدْرِكَ وَتَقْرَأَهُ ﴿فَإِذَا قَرَأْنَاهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْآنَهُ﴾ قَالَ: فَاسْتَمِعْ لَهُ وَأَنْصِتْ ﴿ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا بَيَانَهُ﴾ ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا أَنْ تَقْرَأَهُ، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ إِذَا أَتَاهُ جِبْرِيلُ اسْتَمَعَ، فَإِذَا انْطَلَقَ جِبْرِيلُ قَرَأَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَمَا قَرَأَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في بدء الوحي (5)، ومسلم في الصّلاة (448) كلاهما من حديث أبي عوانة، عن موسى بن أبي عائشة، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس، فذكره، واللفظ للبخاريّ، ومسلم لم يذكر تحريك ابن عباس شفتيه ومن بعده.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استعجال النبي ﷺ في تلقف الوحي عند نزوله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in Badʾ al-Waḥy (5) and Muslim in al-Ṣalāh (448).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Hastening to Receive the Revelation as It Descended","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them said concerning Allah Most High’s statement: “Do not move your tongue with it in haste.” [Sūrat al-Qiyāmah 75:16] said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to experience great difficulty when revelation descended upon him, and because of this he would move his lips. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “I will move my lips for you just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to move his.” Saʿīd said: “I will move them just as I saw Ibn ʿAbbās move them.” He then moved his lips. Allah Most High revealed: “Do not move your tongue with it in haste. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation.” [Sūrat al-Qiyāmah 75:16–17] He explained: That is, Allah would gather it for you within your chest so that you would be able to recite it. “So when We have recited it, follow its recitation.” He said: Listen to it attentively and remain silent. “Then indeed, upon Us is its explanation.” That is, it is then upon Allah to enable you to recite it. Thereafter, whenever Jibrīl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would listen attentively. When Jibrīl departed, the Prophet ﷺ would recite it exactly as Jibrīl had recited it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5)، ومسلم (448)."},{"num":14,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: انْطَلَقَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي طَائِفَةٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ عَامِدِينَ إِلَى سُوقِ عُكَاظٍ، وَقَدْ حِيلَ بَيْنَ الشَّيَاطِينِ وَبَيْنَ خَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ، وَأُرْسِلَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الشُّهُبُ فَرَجَعَتِ الشَّيَاطِينُ إِلَى قَوْمِهِمْ فَقَالُوا: مَا لَكُمْ؟ فَقَالُوا:حِيلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ خَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ وَأُرْسِلَتْ عَلَيْنَا الشُّهُبُ، قَالُوا: مَا حَالَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَ خَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ إِلَّا شَيْءٌ حَدَثَ فَاضْرِبُوا مَشَارِقَ الْأَرْضِ وَمَغَارِبَهَا، فَانْظُرُوا مَا هَذَا الَّذِي حَالَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَ خَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ، فَانْصَرَفَ أُولَئِكَ الَّذِينَ تَوَجَّهُوا نَحْوَ تِهَامَةَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ بِنَخْلَةَ عَامِدِينَ إِلَى سُوقِ عُكَاظٍ وَهُوَ يُصَلِّي بِأَصْحَابِهِ صَلَاةَ الْفَجْرِ، فَلَمَّا سَمِعُوا الْقُرْآنَ اسْتَمَعُوا لَهُ، فَقَالُوا: هَذَا وَاللَّهِ الَّذِي حَالَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَ خَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ، فَهُنَالِكَ حِينَ رَجَعُوا إِلَى قَوْمِهِمْ وَقَالُوا: يَا قَوْمَنَا ﴿إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْآنًا عَجَبًا (1) يَهْدِي إِلَى الرُّشْدِ فَآمَنَّا بِهِ وَلَنْ نُشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَا أَحَدًا (2)﴾ [سورة الجن 1، 2]. فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَى نَبِيِّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ﴿قُلْ أُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ﴾ وَإِنَّمَا أُوحِيَ إِلَيْهِ قَوْلُ الْجِنِّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الصّلاة (773)، ومسلم في الصّلاة (449) كلاهما من حديث أبي عوانة، عن أبي بشر، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس فذكره، واللّفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم قريب منه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما أوحي إلى النبي ﷺ من قول الجن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣalāh (773) and Muslim in al-Ṣalāh (449).","chapter_en":"What Was Revealed to the Prophet ﷺ Concerning the Words of the Jinn","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them reported: The Prophet ﷺ set out with a group of his Companions heading toward the market of ʿUkāẓ. Meanwhile, the devils had been prevented from obtaining news from heaven, and shooting stars had been sent against them. The devils returned to their people, who asked: “What has happened to you?” They replied: “We have been prevented from obtaining news from the heaven, and shooting stars have been sent against us.” They said: “Nothing could have prevented you from obtaining news from the heaven except something new that has occurred. Travel throughout the eastern and western regions of the earth and discover what has come between you and news of heaven.” Those who had gone toward Tihāmah came upon the Prophet ﷺ at Nakhlah while he and his Companions were heading toward the market of ʿUkāẓ. He was leading his Companions in the dawn prayer. When they heard the Qurʾān, they listened attentively and said: “By Allah, this is what has come between you and the news of heaven.” When they returned to their people, they said: “Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Qurʾān. It guides to right guidance, so we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.” [Sūrat al-Jinn 72:1–2] Allah then revealed to His Prophet ﷺ, “Say: It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened.” [Sūrat al-Jinn 72:1] What was revealed to him was the statement of the jinn."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[12931],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (773)، ومسلم (449)."},{"num":15,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:مَنْ حَدَّثَكَ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَتَمَ شَيْئًا مِنَ الْوَحْيِ فَلَا تُصَدِّقْهُ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى يَقُولُ:﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الرَّسُولُ بَلِّغْ مَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَبِّكَ وَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلْ فَمَا بَلَّغْتَ رِسَالَتَهُ﴾ [سورة المائدة: 67]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في التوحيد (7531) عن محمد بن يوسف، حدثنا سفيان، عن إسماعيل، عن الشعبيّ، عن مسروق، عن عائشة، فذكرت مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في إبلاغ الوحي كاملاً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7531).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning Conveying the Revelation Completely","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her said: “Whoever tells you that Muḥammad ﷺ concealed anything of the revelation, do not believe him. Allah Most High says: ‘O Messenger, convey what has been revealed to you from your Lord; and if you do not, then you have not conveyed His message.’” [Sūrat al-Māʾidah 5:67]"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الرَّسُولُ بَلِّغْ مَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَبِّكَ وَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلْ فَمَا بَلَّغْتَ رِسَالَتَهُ﴾","[المائدة: ٦٧]","قال الزهري:","من الله الرسالة، وعلى رسول الله البلاغ، وعلينا التسليم."],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“O Messenger, convey what has been revealed to you from your Lord; and if you do not, then you have not conveyed His message.”","[Sūrat al-Māʾidah 5:67]","Al-Zuhrī said:","“The message is from Allah, upon the Messenger is its conveyance, and upon us is submission.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (7531)."},{"num":16,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِذَا قَضَى اللَّهُ الْأَمْرَ فِي السَّمَاءِ ضَرَبَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ بِأَجْنِحَتِهَا خُضْعَانًا لِقَوْلِهِ كَالسِّلْسِلَةِ عَلَى صَفْوَانٍ، قَالَ عَلِيٌّ: وَقَالَ غَيْرُهُ: صَفْوَانٍ يَنْفُذُهُمْ ذَلِكَ، فَإِذَا فُزِّعَ عَنْ قُلُوبِهِمْ قَالُوا: مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ؟ قَالُوا: لِلَّذِي قَالَ الْحَقَّ وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْكَبِيرُ، فَيَسْمَعُهَا مُسْتَرِقُو السَّمْعِ وَمُسْتَرِقُو السَّمْعِ هَكَذَا وَاحِدٌ فَوْقَ آخَرَ، وَوَصَفَ سُفْيَانُ بِيَدِهِ وَفَرَّجَ بَيْنَ أَصَابِعِ يَدِهِ الْيُمْنَى نَصَبَهَا بَعْضَهَا فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ، فَرُبَّمَا أَدْرَكَ الشِّهَابُ الْمُسْتَمِعَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَرْمِيَ بِهَا إِلَى صَاحِبِهِ فَيُحْرِقَهُ، وَرُبَّمَا لَمْ يُدْرِكْهُ حَتَّى يَرْمِيَ بِهَا إِلَى الَّذِي يَلِيهِ إِلَى الَّذِي هُوَ أَسْفَلَ مِنْهُ حَتَّى يُلْقُوهَا إِلَى الْأَرْضِ، وَرُبَّمَا قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: حَتَّى تَنْتَهِيَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ، فَتُلْقَى عَلَى فَمْ السَّاحِرِ فَيَكْذِبُ مَعَهَا مِائَةَ كَذْبَةٍ فَيُصَدَّقُ فَيَقُولُونَ: أَلَمْ يُخْبِرْنَا يَوْمَ كَذَا وَكَذَا يَكُونُ كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَوَجَدْنَاهُ حَقًّا لِلْكَلِمَةِ الَّتِي سُمِعَتْ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ. حَدَّثَنَا عَلِيُّ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، حَدَّثَنَا سُفْيَانُ، حَدَّثَنَا عَمْرٌو، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ: إِذَا قَضَى اللَّهُ الْأَمْرَ وَزَادَ وَالْكَاهِنِ، وحَدَّثَنَا سُفْيَانُ، فَقَالَ عَمْرٌو: سَمِعْتُ عِكْرِمَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: إِذَا قَضَى اللَّهُ الْأَمْرَ، وَقَالَ: عَلَى فَمْ السَّاحِرِ.","قُلْتُ لِسُفْيَانَ: أَ أَنْتَ سَمِعْتَ عَمْرًا؟ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عِكْرِمَةَ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قُلْتُ لِسُفْيَانَ: إِنَّ إِنْسَانًا رَوَى عَنك، عَنْ عَمْرٍو، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ وَيَرْفَعُهُ أَنَّهُ قَرَأَ: ﴿فُزِّعَ﴾؟ قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: هَكَذَا قَرَأَ عَمْرٌو، فَلَا أَدْرِي سَمِعَهُ هَكَذَا أَمْ لَا قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: وَهِيَ قِرَاءَتُنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4701) عن علي بن عبدالله، حدثنا سفيان، عن عمرو، عن عكرمة، عن أبي هريرة، عن النّبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وصف أهل السماء عند نزول الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tafsīr (4701).","chapter_en":"The State of the Inhabitants of the Heavens When Revelation Descends","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When Allah decrees a matter in the heaven, the angels strike their wings in submission to His statement, producing a sound like a chain being dragged over a smooth rock.” ʿAlī said that another narrator added: “Over a smooth rock, and that sound penetrates them.” “When terror is removed from their hearts, they say, ‘What did your Lord say?’ They answer the one who asked, ‘The truth, and He is the Most High, the Most Great.’” Those who stealthily listen then hear it, and the stealthy listeners are positioned one above another like this.” Sufyān demonstrated with his hand, spreading the fingers of his right hand and placing them one above another. “Sometimes a shooting star reaches the listener before he can pass the word to his companion and burns him. At other times it does not reach him until he has passed it to the one below him, then that one passes it to the one below him, until they cast it down to the earth” — and Sufyān sometimes said, “until it reaches the earth.” “It is then placed upon the mouth of the sorcerer, who mixes one hundred lies with it, yet he is believed. People say, ‘Did he not tell us that on such-and-such a day such-and-such would happen, and we found it to be true?’ This was because of the one word that had been heard from the heaven.”","Another wording adds: “And the soothsayer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4701)."},{"num":17,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا تَكَلَّمَ اللَّهُ بِالْوَحْيِ سَمِعَ أَهْلُ السَّمَاءِ لِلسَّمَاءِ صَلْصَلَةً كَجَرِّ السِّلْسِلَةِ عَلَى الصَّفَا، فَيُصْعَقُونَ، فَلَا يَزَالُونَ كَذَلِكَ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَهُمْ جِبْرِيلُ حَتَّى إِذَا جَاءَهُمْ جِبْرِيلُ فُزِّعَ عَنْ قُلُوبِهِمْ، قَالَ: فَيَقُولُونَ: يَا جِبْرِيلُ، مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكَ؟ فَيَقُولُ: الْحَقَّ، فَيَقُولُونَ: الْحَقَّ، الْحَقَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4738) عن أحمد بن أبي سريج الرازيّ، وعلي بن الحسين بن إبراهيم، وعلي بن مسلم، قالوا: حدثنا أبو معاوية، حدثنا الأعمش، عن مسلم، عن مسروق، عن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وصف أهل السماء عند نزول الوحي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4738), Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (280), and Ibn Ḥibbān (37).","chapter_en":"The State of the Inhabitants of the Heavens When Revelation Descends","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah speaks with revelation, the inhabitants of heaven hear throughout the heaven a ringing sound like a chain being dragged across a smooth rock. They are overcome and remain in that state until Jibrīl, peace be upon him, comes to them. When Jibrīl comes to them, fear is removed from their hearts, and they ask: ‘O Jibrīl, what did your Lord say?’ He replies: ‘The truth.’ They then say: ‘The truth, the truth.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[404],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4738)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (280)، وابن حبان (37)."},{"num":18,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ قَالَ: لَمَّا نَزَلَتْ ﴿لَا يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ﴾ [سورة النساء: 95] قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ادْعُ لِي زَيْدًا وَلْيَجِئْ بِاللَّوْحِ وَالدَّوَاةِ وَالْكَتِفِ أَوِ الْكَتِفِ وَالدَّوَاةِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اكْتُبْ: لَا يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُجَاهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: وَخَلْفَ ظَهْرِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَمْرُو بْنُ أُمِّ مَكْتُومٍ الْأَعْمَى، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ فَمَا تَأْمُرُنِي فَإِنِّي رَجُلٌ ضَرِيرُ الْبَصَرِ؟ فَنَزَلَتْ مَكَانَهَا:﴿ لَا يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ﴾[سورة النساء: 95]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في فضائل القرآن (4990) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء، فذكره. ورواه مسلم في الإمارة (1898) من وجه آخر عن أبي إسحاق مختصرا، وسيأتي في موضعه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب نزول آية واحدة في دفعتين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4990) and Muslim (1898).","chapter_en":"A Single Verse Being Revealed in Two Stages","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ may Allah be pleased with him reported: When the verse: “Not equal are those believers who remain behind and those who strive in the way of Allah” was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Call Zayd for me, and let him bring the writing tablet, the inkpot, and the shoulder blade”—or, “the shoulder blade and the inkpot.” He then said: “Write: ‘Not equal are those believers who remain behind.’” Behind the Prophet ﷺ was ʿAmr ibn Umm Maktūm, who was blind. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me to do, for I am a man without sight?” Then the verse was revealed in its completed form: “Not equal are those believers who remain behind — except those with a disability — and those who strive in the way of Allah.” [Sūrat al-Nisāʾ 4:95]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4990)، ومسلم (1898)."},{"num":19,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِيتُونِي بِالْكَتِفِ أَوِ اللَّوْحِ فَكَتَبَ:﴿لَا يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ﴾ وَعَمْرُو بْنُ أُمِّ مَكْتُومٍ خَلْفَ ظَهْرِهِ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ لِي مِنْ رُخْصَةٍ؟ فَنَزَلَتْ: ﴿غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ﴾."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذيّ (1670)، والنسائيّ (3101) كلاهما عن نصر بن علي الجهضميّ قال: أخبرنا معتمر بن سليمان، عن أبيه، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب نزول آية واحدة في دفعتين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1670) and al-Nasāʾī (3101).","chapter_en":"A Single Verse Being Revealed in Two Stages","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me the shoulder blade or the writing tablet.” He then wrote: “Not equal are those believers who remain behind.” ʿAmr ibn Umm Maktūm was behind him and asked: “Is there any concession for me?” Then the words were revealed: “Except those with a disability.” [Sūrat al-Nisāʾ 4:95]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1670)، والنسائي (3101)."},{"num":20,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى تَابَعَ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْوَحْيَ قَبْلَ وَفَاتِهِ حَتَّى تَوَفَّاهُ أَكْثَرَ مَا كَانَ الْوَحْيُ، ثُمَّ تُوُفِّيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في فضائل القرآن (4982)، ومسلم في كتاب التفسير (3016) كلاهما عن عمرو بن محمد بن بُكير النّاقد، حدثنا يعقوب بن إبراهيم بن سعد، عن أبيه، عن صالح بن كيسان، عن ابن شهاب، قال: أخبرني أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لم ينقطع الوحي عن النبي ﷺ حتى توفاه الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4982) and Muslim (3016).","chapter_en":"Revelation Did Not Cease From the Prophet ﷺ Until Allah Took Him in Death","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported: Allah Most High continued sending revelation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before his death, until the period immediately preceding his death became the time in which revelation came to him most frequently. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar explained in Fatḥ al-Bārī that revelation became more frequent near the death of the Prophet ﷺ because delegations increased after the conquest of Makkah, and their questions concerning legal rulings increased. Consequently, revelation also increased in response to those matters."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4982)، ومسلم (3016)."},{"num":21,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ بَعْدَ وَفَاةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعُمَرَ: انْطَلِقْ بِنَا إِلَى أُمِّ أَيْمَنَ، نَزُورُهَا كَمَا كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَزُورُهَا، فَلَمَّا انْتَهَيْنَا إِلَيْهَا بَكَتْ، فَقَالَا لَهَا: مَا يُبْكِيكِ؟ مَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِرَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: مَا أَبْكِي أَنْ لَا أَكُونَ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ مَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِرَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلَكِنْ أَبْكِي أَنَّ الْوَحْيَ قَدِ انْقَطَعَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ، فَهَيَّجَتْهُمَا عَلَى الْبُكَاءِ فَجَعَلَا يَبْكِيَانِ مَعَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصّحابة (2454) عن زهير بن حرب، أخبرني عمرو بن عاصم الكلابيّ، حدثنا سليمان بن المغيرة، عن ثابت، عن أنس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب انقطاع الوحي بعد وفاة رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الوحي","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (2454).","chapter_en":"The Cessation of Revelation After the Death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Revelation","group_ar":"","group_en":"","part_no":1,"group_no":0,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported: After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr said to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them: “Come with us to visit Umm Ayman, just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit her.” When we reached her, she began to weep. They asked her: “What makes you weep? What is with Allah is better for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She replied: “I am not weeping because I do not know that what is with Allah is better for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Rather, I am weeping because revelation from heaven has ceased.” Anas said: Her words moved them both to tears, and they began weeping with her."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[10441],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2454)."},{"num":22,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَارِزًا يَوْمًا لِلنَّاسِ، فَأَتَاهُ جِبْرِيلُ فَقَالَ: مَا الْإِيمَانُ؟ قَالَ: الْإِيمَانُ أَنْ تُؤْمِنَ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَبِلِقَائِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْبَعْثِ، قَالَ: مَا الْإِسْلَامُ؟ قَالَ: الْإِسْلَامُ أَنْ تَعْبُدَ اللَّهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمَ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤَدِّيَ الزَّكَاةَ الْمَفْرُوضَةَ، وَتَصُومَ رَمَضَانَ، قَالَ: مَا الْإِحْسَانُ؟ قَالَ: أَنْ تَعْبُدَ اللَّهَ كَأَنَّكَ تَرَاهُ فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ تَرَاهُ فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاكَ، قَالَ: مَتَى السَّاعَةُ؟ قَالَ: مَا الْمَسْئُولُ عَنْهَا بِأَعْلَمَ مِنَ السَّائِلِ، وَسَأُخْبِرُكَ عَنْ أَشْرَاطِهَا إِذَا وَلَدَتِ الْأَمَةُ رَبَّهَا، وَإِذَا تَطَاوَلَ رُعَاةُ الْإِبِلِ الْبُهْمُ فِي الْبُنْيَانِ فِي خَمْسٍ لَا يَعْلَمُهُنَّ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ تَلَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ عِنْدَهُ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ﴾ [سورة لقمان: 34] الآية،ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ فَقَالَ: رُدُّوهُ، فَلَمْ يَرَوْا شَيْئًا، فَقَالَ: هَذَا جِبْرِيلُ، جَاءَ يُعَلِّمُ النَّاسَ دِينَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (50)، ومسلم في الإيمان (9) كلاهما من حديث إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن عُليّة، عن أبي حيّان التيميّ، عن أبي زرعة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب سؤال جبريل عن الإيمان والإسلام والإحسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (50) and Muslim (9).","chapter_en":"Jibrīl’s Questions About Faith, Islam, and Iḥsān","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet ﷺ was sitting in public among the people one day when a man came to him and asked: “What is faith?” He replied: “Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His Book, meeting Him, His messengers, and that you believe in the resurrection.” He asked: “What is Islam?” He replied: “Islam is that you worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prayer, pay the obligatory zakāh, and fast Ramaḍān.” He asked: “What is iḥsān?” He replied: “That you worship Allah as though you see Him; and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you.” He asked: “When is the Hour?” He replied: “The one being asked knows no more about it than the questioner. But I will tell you about its signs: when the slave woman gives birth to her master, and when the shepherds of black camels compete with one another in constructing buildings. That is among its signs. It is one of five matters known only to Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ then recited: “Indeed, Allah alone has knowledge of the Hour.” [Sūrat Luqmān 31:34] The man then departed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring him back.” But they could see no one. He then said: “That was Jibrīl. He came to teach the people their religion.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration in Muslim:","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Ask me.” They were hesitant to question him, so a man came and a similar narration followed. At its conclusion he said: “This was Jibrīl. He wanted you to learn when you did not ask.”","His saying, “Bring him back,” apparently indicates that at first he did not know that it was Jibrīl. He later came to know, through revelation from Allah Most High, that it was Jibrīl who had come to teach the people their religion."]},"intro_kitab":{"ar":["الأصل فيه حديث جبريل عليه السلام، وهو يتضمن أركان الإيمان الستة، وهي:","الإيمان بالله عز وجل.","والإيمان بالملائكة.","والإيمان بالكتب التي أنزلها الله تعالى.","والإيمان بالرسل.","والإيمان باليوم الآخر.","والإيمان بالقدر خيره وشره.","كما يتضمن أركان الإسلام الخمسة، وهي:","شهادة أن لا إله إلا الله، وأن محمداً رسول الله.","وإقام الصلاة.","وإيتاء الزكاة.","وصوم رمضان.","وحج البيت لمن استطاع إليه سبيلاً.","وكتاب الإيمان وكتاب العبادات مرتبان كما جاء في حديث جبريل عليه السلام."],"en":["The foundation of this Book is the ḥadīth of Jibrīl, peace be upon him. It contains the six pillars of faith:","Belief in Allah, Mighty and Majestic.","Belief in the angels.","Belief in the Books revealed by Allah Most High.","Belief in the messengers.","Belief in the Last Day.","Belief in divine decree, both its good and its evil.","It also contains the five pillars of Islam:","Testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.","Establishing the prayer.","Giving zakāh.","Fasting Ramaḍān.","Performing pilgrimage to the House for whoever is able to find a way to it.","The Book of Faith and the Book of Acts of Worship are arranged according to the order found in the ḥadīth of Jibrīl, peace be upon him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (50)، ومسلم (9)."},{"num":23,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ قَالَ: بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ إِذْ طَلَعَ عَلَيْنَا رَجُلٌ شَدِيدُ بَيَاضِ الثِّيَابِ شَدِيدُ سَوَادِ الشَّعَرِ، لَا يُرَى عَلَيْهِ أَثَرُ السَّفَرِ، وَلَا يَعْرِفُهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ، حَتَّى جَلَسَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَسْنَدَ رُكْبَتَيْهِ إِلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ، وَوَضَعَ كَفَّيْهِ عَلَى فَخِذَيْه وَقَالَ: يَا مُحَمَّدُ! أَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الإِسْلَامِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الإِسْلَامُ أَنْ تَشْهَدَ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَتُقِيمَ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِيَ الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومَ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجَّ الْبَيْتَ إِنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَعَجِبْنَا لَهُ يَسْأَلُهُ، وَيُصَدِّقُهُ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الإِيمَنِ، قَالَ: أَنْ تُؤْمِنَ بِاللَّهِ، وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ، وَكُتُبِهِ، وَرُسُلِهِ، وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْقَدَرِ خَيْرِهِ وَشَرِّهِ، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الإِحْسَانِ، قَالَ: أَنْ تَعْبُدَ اللَّهَ كَأَنَّكَ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاكَ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ السَّاعَةِ، قَالَ: مَا الْمَسْئُولُ عَنْهَا بِأَعْلَمَ مِنَ السَّائِلِ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ أَمَارَتِهَا، قَالَ:أَنْ تَلِدَ الأَمَةُ رَبَّتَهَا، وَأَنْ تَرَى الْحُفَاةَ الْعُرَاةَ الْعَالَةَ رِعَاءَ الشَّاءِ، يَتَطَاوَلُونَ فِي الْبُنْيَانِ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَ فَلَبِثْتُ مَلِيًّا، ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: يَا عُمَرُ أَتَدْرِي مَنِ السَّائِلُ؟ قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: فَإِنَّهُ جِبْرِيلُ، أَتَاكُمْ يُعَلِّمُكُمْ دِينَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (8) من طرق عن يحيى بن يعمر، قال: أوّل من قال في القدر بالبصرة معبد الجهنيّ، فانطلقت أنا وحُميد بن عبد الرحمن الحميري حاجَيْن أو معتمرين. فقلنا: لو لقينا أحداً من أصحاب رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فسألناه عمّا يقول هؤلاء في القدر، فوفق لنا عبدالله بن عمر بن الخطاب داخلاً المسجد فاكتنفتُه أنا وصاحبي، أحدُنا عن يمينه والآخر عن شماله، فظننت أنّ صاحبي سيكل الكلامَ إليَّ فقلتُ: أبا عبدالرحمن! إنه قد ظهر قِبلنا ناسٌ يقرؤون القرآن ويتقفَّرون العلم، وذكر من شأنهم، وأنَّهم يزعمون أن لا قدر، وأنّ الأمر أُنُفٌ؟ قال: فإذا لقيت أولئك فأخبرهم أنّي برئٌ منهم، وأنّهم برآءٌ مني، والذي يحلف به عبدالله بن عمر لو أنّ لأحدهم مثلَ أُحُدٍ ذهباً فأنفقه ما قبل الله منه حتى يُؤْمنَ بالقدر، ثم قال: حدثني أبي عمر بن الخطاب قال، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سؤال جبريل عن الإيمان والإسلام والإحسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (8).","chapter_en":"Jibrīl’s Questions About Faith, Islam, and Iḥsān","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, a man appeared before us whose clothing was exceedingly white and whose hair was exceedingly black. No sign of travel could be seen upon him, yet none of us knew him. He sat before the Prophet ﷺ, placed his knees against the Prophet’s knees, rested his hands upon his thighs, and said: “O Muḥammad, tell me about Islam.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Islam is that you testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah; establish the prayer; pay zakāh; fast Ramaḍān; and perform pilgrimage to the House if you are able to find a way to it.” He said: “You have spoken the truth.” ʿUmar said: We were astonished that he would ask him and then confirm his answer. He then said: “Tell me about faith.” He replied: “That you believe in Allah, His angels, His Books, His messengers, the Last Day, and that you believe in divine decree, both its good and its evil.” He said: “You have spoken the truth.” He asked: “Tell me about iḥsān.” He replied: “That you worship Allah as though you see Him; and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you.” He asked: “Tell me about the Hour.” He replied: “The one being asked knows no more about it than the questioner.” He asked: “Then tell me about its signs.” He replied: “That the slave woman will give birth to her mistress, and that you will see barefoot, naked, destitute shepherds competing with one another in constructing buildings.” Then the man departed. After I had remained for some time, the Prophet ﷺ said to me: “O ʿUmar, do you know who the questioner was?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That was Jibrīl. He came to teach you your religion.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Supplement:","Through the routes from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmur, who said: “The first person to speak publicly in Basra denying divine decree was Maʿbad al-Juhanī. So I set out with Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥimyarī for ḥajj or ʿumrah. We said: If only we could meet one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him about what these people are saying regarding qadar. We happened to meet ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb as he entered the mosque. My companion and I flanked him, one on his right and the other on his left. I thought my companion would leave the speaking to me, so I said: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, people have appeared among us who recite the Qurʾān and pursue knowledge,” and he mentioned their condition, “and they claim there is no qadar and that matters are newly occurring without prior decree.” He said: “If you meet those people, tell them that I am free of them and they are free of me. By the One by whom ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar swears, if one of them possessed gold equal to Mount Uḥud and spent it, Allah would not accept it from him until he believed in qadar.” Then he said: “My father ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to me…” and he mentioned the ḥadīth.","The phrase “my companion and I flanked him” means that we stood on his two sides; the two wings of a bird are its two sides.","The phrase “they pursue knowledge” means that they follow its traces and seek it.","The phrase “the matter is uninitiated” means newly begun, with no prior decree or divine will having preceded it.","Al-Baghawī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “In this ḥadīth the Prophet ﷺ called the outward deeds ‘Islam’ and the inward belief ‘faith.’ This does not mean that deeds are not part of faith or that inward belief is not part of Islam. Rather, this is a detailed explanation of one whole whose sum is the religion. That is why he said: ‘That was Jibrīl; he came to teach you your religion.’ Both belief and action are included under the names faith and Islam together. This is indicated by Allah’s statements: ‘Indeed, the religion with Allah is Islam’ [Āl ʿImrān 3:19], ‘I have approved Islam for you as religion’ [al-Māʾidah 5:3], and ‘Whoever seeks a religion other than Islam, it will never be accepted from him, and in the Hereafter he will be among the losers’ [Āl ʿImrān 3:85]. Thus He informed us that the religion He approves and accepts from His servants is Islam, and religion cannot be accepted and approved except when belief is joined with action.” Sharḥ al-Sunnah (1/10–11)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (8)."},{"num":24,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَحْيَى بْنِ يَعْمَرَ قُلْتُ لِابْنِ عُمَرَ:إِنَّ عِنْدَنَا رِجَالًا يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّ الْأَمْرَ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ، فَإِنْ شَاءُوا عَمِلُوا، وَإِنْ شَاءُوا لَمْ يَعْمَلُوا! فَقَالَ: أَخْبِرْهُمْ أَنِّي مِنْهُمْ بَرِيءٌ، وَأَنَّهُمْ مِنِّي بُرَآءُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: جَاءَ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَام إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: يَا مُحَمَّدُ! مَا الْإِسْلَامُ؟ فَقَالَ: تَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ لَا تُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِي الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومُ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجُّ الْبَيْتَ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا فَعَلْتُ ذَلِكَ، فَأَنَا مُسْلِمٌ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَمَا الْإِحْسَانُ؟ قَالَ: تَخْشَى اللَّهَ تَعَالَى كَأَنَّكَ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنْ لَا تَكُ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاكَ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا فَعَلْتُ ذَلِكَ، فَأَنَا مُحْسِنٌ، قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَمَا الْإِيمَانُ؟ قَالَ: تُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ، وَكُتُبِهِ، وَرُسُلِهِ، وَالْبَعْثِ مِنْ بَعْدِ الْمَوْتِ وَالْجَنَّةِ وَالنَّارِ، وَالْقَدَرِ كُلِّهِ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا فَعَلْتُ ذَلِكَ فَأَنَا مُؤْمِنٌ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (5856) عن عفّان، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، أخبرنا عليُّ بن زيد، عن يحيى بن يَعْمُر، فذكره. وعلي بن زيد هو ابن جدعان ضعيف، لكنه توبع.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سؤال جبريل عن الإيمان والإسلام والإحسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (5856, 5857).","chapter_en":"Jibrīl’s Questions About Faith, Islam, and Iḥsān","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmur reported: I said to Ibn ʿUmar: “We have men among us who claim that affairs are entirely in their own hands: if they wish, they act, and if they wish, they refrain.” He replied: “Tell them that I am free of them and that they are free of me.” He then said: Jibrīl, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “O Muḥammad, what is Islam?” He replied: “That you worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prayer, pay zakāh, fast Ramaḍān, and perform pilgrimage to the House.” He asked: “If I do that, am I a Muslim?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “You have spoken the truth.” He asked: “What is iḥsān?” He replied: “That you fear Allah Most High as though you see Him; and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you.” He asked: “If I do that, am I a muḥsin?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “You have spoken the truth.” He asked: “What is faith?” He replied: “That you believe in Allah, His angels, His Books, His messengers, resurrection after death, Paradise and Hell, and all of divine decree.” He asked: “If I do that, am I a believer?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “You have spoken the truth.” In another narration: Jibrīl, peace be upon him, would come to the Prophet ﷺ in the appearance of Diḥyah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (5856، 5857)."},{"num":25,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: جَلَسَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَجْلِسًا لَهُ، فَأَتَاهُ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَام فَجَلَسَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَاضِعًا كَفَّيْهِ عَلَى رُكْبَتَيْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! حَدِّثْنِي مَا الْإِسْلَامُ؟ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْإِسْلَامُ أَنْ تُسْلِمَ وَجْهَكَ لِلَّهِ، وَتَشْهَدَ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا فَعَلْتُ ذَلِكَ فقد أَسلمتُ ؟، قَالَ: إِذَا فَعَلْتَ ذَلِكَ، فَقَدْ أَسْلَمْتَ. قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَحَدِّثْنِي مَا الْإِيمَانُ؟ قَالَ: الْإِيمَانُ أَنْ تُؤْمِنَ بِاللّهِ، وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، وَالْمَلَائِكَةِ، وَالْكِتَابِ، وَالنَّبِيِّينَ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْمَوْت، وَبِالْحَيَاةِ بَعْدَ الْمَوْتِ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْجَنَّةِ وَالنَّارِ، وَالْحِسَابِ، وَالْمِيزَانِ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْقَدَرِ كُلِّهِ خَيْرِهِ وَشَرِّهِ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا فَعَلْتُ ذَلِكَ فَقَدْ آمَنْتُ؟ قَالَ: إِذَا فَعَلْتَ ذَلِكَ فَقَدْ آمَنْتَ. قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، حَدِّثْنِي مَا الْإِحْسَانُ؟ قَالَ: رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْإِحْسَانُ أَنْ تَعْمَلَ لِلَّهِ كَأَنَّكَ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنَّكَ إِنْ لَمْ تَرَهُ، فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاكَ. قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَحَدِّثْنِي مَتَى السَّاعَةُ؟ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ! فِي خَمْسٍ مِنَ الْغَيْبِ لَا يَعْلَمُهُنَّ إِلَّا هُوَ: ﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ عِنْدَهُ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ وَيُنَزِّلُ الْغَيْثَ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِي الْأَرْحَامِ وَمَا تَدْرِي نَفْسٌ مَاذَا تَكْسِبُ غَدًا وَمَا تَدْرِي نَفْسٌ بِأَيِّ أَرْضٍ تَمُوتُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ خَبِيرٌ﴾ [سورة لقمان: 34]، وَلَكِنْ إِنْ شِئْتَ حَدَّثْتُكَ بِمَعَالِمَ لَهَا دُونَ ذَلِكَ، قَالَ: أَجَلْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَحَدِّثْنِي. قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا رَأَيْتَ الْأَمَةَ وَلَدَتْ رَبَّتَهَا أَوْ رَبَّهَا، وَرَأَيْتَ أَصْحَابَ الشَّاءِ تَطَاوَلُوا بِالْبُنْيَانِ، وَرَأَيْتَ الْحُفَاةَ الْجِيَاعَ الْعَالَةَ كَانُوا رُءُوسَ النَّاسِ، فَذَلِكَ مِنْ مَعَالِمِ السَّاعَةِ وَأَشْرَاطِهَا. قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَمَنْ أَصْحَابُ الشَّاءِ وَالْحُفَاةُ الْجِيَاعُ الْعَالَةُ؟ قَالَ: الْعَرَبُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2924) عن أبي النّضر، حدثنا عبدالحميد، حدثنا شهر بن حوشب، حدثني عبدالله بن عباس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب سؤال جبريل عن الإيمان والإسلام والإحسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (2924, 17167) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (24).","chapter_en":"Jibrīl’s Questions About Faith, Islam, and Iḥsān","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in one of his gatherings when Jibrīl, peace be upon him, came and sat before him, placing his hands upon the knees of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me what Islam is.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Islam is that you submit yourself to Allah, testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone with no partner, and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger.” He asked: “If I do that, am I a Muslim?” He replied: “If you do that, then you have submitted as a Muslim.” He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me what faith is.” He replied: “Faith is that you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, and the prophets; that you believe in death and life after death; that you believe in Paradise and Hell, the Reckoning and the Scale; and that you believe in divine decree in its entirety, both its good and its evil.” He asked: “If I do that, have I believed?” He replied: “If you do that, then you have believed.” He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me what iḥsān is.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Iḥsān is that you act for Allah as though you see Him; for although you do not see Him, He indeed sees you.” He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me when the Hour will be.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Glory be to Allah! It is among five matters of the unseen known to none but Him.” He then recited: “Indeed, Allah alone has knowledge of the Hour, sends down the rain, knows what is in the wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware.” [Sūrat Luqmān 31:34] He then said: “But if you wish, I can tell you about signs that precede it.” He replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Tell me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see the slave woman give birth to her mistress — or her master — when you see shepherds competing in constructing buildings, and when you see barefoot, hungry, destitute people becoming the leaders of mankind, these are among the signs and indications of the Hour.” He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who are these shepherds and barefoot, hungry, destitute people?” He replied: “The Arabs.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2924، 17167)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (24)."},{"num":26,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ طَلْحَةَ بْنِ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ يَقُولُ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ أَهْلِ نَجْدٍ، ثَائِرُ الرَّأْسِ نَسْمَعُ دَوِيَّ صَوْتِهِ وَلَا نَفْقَهُ مَا يَقُولُ، حَتَّى دَنَا مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَإِذَا هُوَ يَسْأَلُ عَنِ الإِسْلَامِ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: خَمْسُ صَلَوَاتٍ فِي الْيَوْمِ وَاللَّيْلَةِ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ عَلَيَّ غَيْرُهُنَّ؟ قَالَ: لَا إِلَّا أَنْ تَطَّوَّعَ، وَصِيَامُ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ عَلَيَّ غَيْرُهُ؟ فَقَالَ: لَا، إِلَّا أَنْ تَطَّوَّعَ، وَذَكَرَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الزَّكَاةَ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ عَلَيَّ غَيْرُهَا؟ قَالَ: لَا، إِلَّا أَنْ تَطَّوَّعَ، قَالَ: فَأَدْبَرَ الرَّجُلُ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: وَاللَّهِ لَا أَزِيدُ عَلَى هَذَا، وَلَا أَنْقُصُ مِنْهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَفْلَحَ إِنْ صَدَقَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في قصر الصلاة (94) عن عمّه أبي سهيل بن مالك، عن أبيه، أنّه سمع طلحة بن عبيد الله، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (94), al-Bukhārī (46), and Muslim (11).","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: A man from Najd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with disheveled hair. We could hear the loud murmur of his voice but could not understand what he was saying until he drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Five prayers during each day and night.” The man asked: “Is anything else obligatory upon me?” He replied: “No, unless you voluntarily perform more.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “And fasting the month of Ramaḍān.” He asked: “Is anything else obligatory upon me?” He replied: “No, unless you voluntarily do more.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also mentioned zakāh to him. He asked: “Is anything else obligatory upon me?” He replied: “No, unless you voluntarily do more.” The man turned away saying: “By Allah, I will neither add anything to this nor subtract anything from it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The man has succeeded, if he is truthful.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (94)، والبخاري (46)، ومسلم (11)."},{"num":27,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ يَقُولُ: بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ جُلُوسٌ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ، دَخَلَ رَجُلٌ عَلَى جَمَلٍ فَأَنَاخَهُ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ ثُمَّ عَقَلَهُ ثُمَّ قَالَ لَهُمْ: أَيُّكُمْ مُحَمَّدٌ؟ وَالنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُتَّكِئٌ بَيْنَ ظَهْرَانَيْهِمْ، فَقُلْنَا: هَذَا الرَّجُلُ الْأَبْيَضُ الْمُتَّكِئُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ الرَّجُلُ: يَا ابْنَ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَدْ أَجَبْتُكَ، فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ، فَمُشَدِّدٌ عَلَيْكَ فِي الْمَسْأَلَةِ فَلَا تَجِدْ عَلَيَّ فِي نَفْسِكَ، فَقَالَ: سَلْ عَمَّا بَدَا لَكَ، فَقَالَ: أَسْأَلُكَ بِرَبِّكَ وَرَبِّ مَنْ قَبْلَكَ، آللَّهُ أَرْسَلَكَ إِلَى النَّاسِ كُلِّهِمْ؟ فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ بِاللَّهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ نُصَلِّيَ الصَّلَوَاتِ الْخَمْسَ فِي الْيَوْمِ وَاللَّيْلَةِ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ بِاللَّهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ نَصُومَ هَذَا الشَّهْرَ مِنَ السَّنَةِ، قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ بِاللَّهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تَأْخُذَ هَذِهِ الصَّدَقَةَ مِنْ أَغْنِيَائِنَا فَتَقْسِمَهَا عَلَى فُقَرَائِنَا؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ: آمَنْتُ بِمَا جِئْتَ بِهِ، وَأَنَا رَسُولُ مَنْ وَرَائِي مِنْ قَوْمِي، وَأَنَا ضِمَامُ بْنُ ثَعْلَبَةَ أَخُو بَنِي سَعْدِ بْنِ بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في العلم (63) عن عبدالله بن يوسف، قال: حدثنا الليث، عن سعيد، هو المقبريّ، ، عن شريك بن عبدالله بن أبي نمر، أنّه سمع أنس بن مالك، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (63) and Muslim (12).","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: While we were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque, a man entered riding a camel. He made it kneel in the mosque, tied it, and then asked: “Which of you is Muḥammad?” The Prophet ﷺ was reclining among them. We replied: “This fair-complexioned man who is reclining.” The man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “I am going to question you and be demanding in my questioning, so do not become upset with me.” He replied: “Ask whatever you wish.” The man said: “I ask you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you: has Allah sent you to all mankind?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Allah: has Allah commanded you that we perform five prayers each day and night?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Allah: has Allah commanded you that we fast this month of the year?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Allah: has Allah commanded you to take this charity from our wealthy and distribute it among our poor?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “O Allah, yes.” The man said: “I believe in what you have brought. I am a messenger on behalf of the people whom I have left behind. I am Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlabah, brother of Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim (12) also narrated it with the wording: “We were forbidden from asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about things, so it used to please us when an intelligent man from the desert would come and ask him while we listened. A Bedouin man came and said: ‘O Muḥammad! Your messenger came to us and claimed that you say Allah sent you.’ He said: ‘He spoke the truth.’","He asked: ‘Who created the sky?’ He said: ‘Allah.’","He asked: ‘Who created the earth?’ He said: ‘Allah.’","He asked: ‘Who set up these mountains and placed in them what He placed?’ He said: ‘Allah.’","He said: ‘By the One who created the sky and the earth and set up these mountains, has Allah sent you?’ He said: ‘Yes.’","He said: ‘Your messenger claimed that we must pray five prayers in our day and night.’ He said: ‘He spoke the truth.’","He said: ‘By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?’ He said: ‘Yes.’","He said: ‘Your messenger claimed that we must pay zakāh from our wealth.’ He said: ‘He spoke the truth.’","He said: ‘By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?’ He said: ‘Yes.’","He said: ‘Your messenger claimed that we must fast the month of Ramaḍān each year.’ He said: ‘He spoke the truth.’","He said: ‘By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?’ He said: ‘Yes.’","He said: ‘Your messenger claimed that we must perform ḥajj to the House, for whoever is able.’ He said: ‘He spoke the truth.’","Then he turned away and said: ‘By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add to these nor subtract from them.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If he is truthful, he will surely enter Paradise.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (63)، ومسلم (12)."},{"num":28,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: بَيْنَمَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَ أَصْحَابِهِ، جَاءَ رَجُلٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَادِيَةِ، قَالَ: أَيُّكُمْ ابْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ؟ قَالُوا: هَذَا الْأَمْغَرُ الْمُرْتَفِقُ، قَالَ حَمْزَةُ: الْأَمْغَرُ: الْأَبْيَضُ مُشْرَبٌ حُمْرَةً، فَقَالَ: إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ فَمُشْتَدٌّ عَلَيْكَ فِي الْمَسْأَلَةِ، قَالَ: سَلْ عَمَّا بَدَا لَكَ، قَالَ: أَسْأَلُكَ بِرَبِّكَ وَرَبِّ مَنْ قَبْلَكَ وَرَبِّ مَنْ بَعْدَكَ، آللَّهُ أَرْسَلَكَ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ بِهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تُصَلِّيَ خَمْسَ صَلَوَاتٍ فِي كُلِّ يَوْمٍ وَلَيْلَةٍ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ بِهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تَأْخُذَ مِنْ أَمْوَالِ أَغْنِيَائِنَا، فَتَرُدَّهُ عَلَى فُقَرَائِنَا؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ بِهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تَصُومَ هَذَا الشَّهْرَ مِنْ اثْنَيْ عَشَرَ شَهْرًا؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ بِهِ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ يَحُجَّ هَذَا الْبَيْتَ مَنْ اسْتَطَاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ قَالَ: فَإِنِّي آمَنْتُ وَصَدَّقْتُ، وَأَنَا ضِمَامُ بْنُ ثَعْلَبَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (2094) عن أبي بكر بن علي، قال: حدثنا إسحاق (هو ابن أبي إسرائيل)، قال: حدثنا أبو عمارة حمزة بن الحارث بن عمير، قال: سمعت أبي يذكر عن عبيد الله بن عمر، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبري، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Nasāʾī (2094) and Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī (2449).","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: While the Prophet ﷺ was with his Companions, a man from the desert came and asked: “Which of you is the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?” They replied: “This reddish-complexioned man who is reclining.” Ḥamzah explained: “Al-amghar means fair-complexioned with a reddish hue.” The man said: “I am going to question you and be demanding in my questions.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ask whatever you wish.” He said: “I ask you by your Lord, the Lord of those before you, and the Lord of those after you: did Allah send you?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Him: did Allah command you to perform five prayers during each day and night?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Him: did Allah command you to take from the wealth of our rich and return it to our poor?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Him: did Allah command you to fast this month out of the twelve months?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He said: “I adjure you by Him: did Allah command whoever is able to perform pilgrimage to this House?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” The man said: “Then I have believed and affirmed, and I am Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlabah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (2094)، وأبو داود الطيالسي (2449)."},{"num":29,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: بَعَثَتْ بَنُو سَعْدِ بْنِ بَكْرٍ ضِمَامَ بْنَ ثَعْلَبَةَ وَافِدًا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَدِمَ عَلَيْهِ وَأَنَاخَ بَعِيرَهُ عَلَى بَابِ الْمَسْجِدِ ثُمَّ عَقَلَهُ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ الْمَسْجِدَ وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَالِسٌ فِي أَصْحَابِهِ، وَكَانَ ضِمَامٌ رَجُلًا جَلْدًا أَشْعَرَ ذَا غَدِيرَتَيْنِ، فَأَقْبَلَ حَتَّى وَقَفَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي أَصْحَابِهِ، فَقَالَ: أَيُّكُمْ ابْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنَا ابْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، قَالَ: مُحَمَّدٌ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، فَقَالَ: ابْنَ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ وَمُغَلِّظٌ فِي الْمَسْأَلَةِ، فَلَا تَجِدَنَّ فِي نَفْسِكَ، قَالَ: لَا أَجِدُ فِي نَفْسِي، فَسَلْ عَمَّا بَدَا لَكَ، قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ إِلَهَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ هُوَ كَائِنٌ بَعْدَكَ، آللَّهُ بَعَثَكَ إِلَيْنَا رَسُولًا؟ فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ إِلَهَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ هُوَ كَائِنٌ بَعْدَكَ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تَأْمُرَنَا أَنْ نَعْبُدَهُ وَحْدَهُ، لَا نُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَأَنْ نَخْلَعَ هَذِهِ الْأَنْدَادَ الَّتِي كَانَتْ آبَاؤُنَا يَعْبُدُونَ مَعَهُ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَم، قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ إِلَهَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ هُوَ كَائِنٌ بَعْدَكَ، آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ نُصَلِّيَ هَذِهِ الصَّلَوَاتِ الْخَمْسَ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ جَعَلَ يَذْكُرُ فَرَائِضَ الْإِسْلَامِ فَرِيضَةً فَرِيضَةً: الزَّكَاةَ، وَالصِّيَامَ، وَالْحَجَّ، وَشَرَائِعَ الْإِسْلَامِ كُلَّهَا، يُنَاشِدُهُ عِنْدَ كُلِّ فَرِيضَةٍ كَمَا يُنَاشِدُهُ فِي الَّتِي قَبْلَهَا، حَتَّى إِذَا فَرَغَ، قَالَ: فَإِنِّي أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَسَأُؤَدِّي هَذِهِ الْفَرَائِضَ، وَأَجْتَنِبُ مَا نَهَيْتَنِي عَنْهُ، ثُمَّ لَا أَزِيدُ وَلَا أَنْقُصُ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ رَاجِعًا إِلَى بَعِيرِهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ وَلَّى: إِنْ يَصْدُقْ ذُو الْعَقِيصَتَيْنِ، يَدْخُلْ الْجَنَّةَ.","قَالَ: فَأَتَى إِلَى بَعِيرِهِ، فَأَطْلَقَ عِقَالَهُ، ثُمَّ خَرَجَ حَتَّى قَدِمَ عَلَى قَوْمِهِ، فَاجْتَمَعُوا إِلَيْهِ، فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ مَا تَكَلَّمَ بِهِ أَنْ قَالَ: بِئْسَتِ اللَّاتُ وَالْعُزَّى، قَالُوا: مَهْ يَا ضِمَامُ، اتَّقِ الْبَرَصَ وَالْجُذَامَ، اتَّقِ الْجُنُونَ، قَالَ وَيْلَكُمْ، إِنَّهُمَا وَاللَّهِ لَا يَضُرَّانِ وَلَا يَنْفَعَانِ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ قَدْ بَعَثَ رَسُولًا، وَأَنْزَلَ عَلَيْهِ كِتَابًا اسْتَنْقَذَكُمْ بِهِ مِمَّا كُنْتُمْ فِيهِ، وَإِنِّي أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، وإِنِّي قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ بِمَا أَمَرَكُمْ بِهِ، وَنَهَاكُمْ عَنْهُ، قَالَ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا أَمْسَى مِنْ ذَلِكَ الْيَوْمِ وَفِي حَاضِرِهِ رَجُلٌ وَلَا امْرَأَةٌ إِلَّا مُسْلِمًا، قَالَ: يَقُولُ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: فَمَا سَمِعْنَا بِوَافِدِ قَوْمٍ كَانَ أَفْضَلَ مِنْ ضِمَامِ بْنِ ثَعْلَبَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2380) عن يعقوب، حدثنا أبي، عن محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني محمد بن الوليد بن نويفع، عن كريب مولى عبدالله بن عباس، عن عبدالله بن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (2380), Abū Dāwūd (487), and al-Ḥākim (4380).","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr sent Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlabah as their delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He arrived, made his camel kneel at the entrance of the mosque, tied it, and then entered while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among his Companions. Ḍimām was a strong, hairy man with two braids. He came forward until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “Which of you is the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “I am the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.” He asked: “Muḥammad?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “O son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, I am going to question you and be severe in my questioning, so do not take offense at me.” He replied: “I will not take offense. Ask whatever you wish.” He said: “I adjure you by Allah — your God, the God of those before you, and the God of those who will come after you — has Allah sent you to us as a Messenger?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He continued: “I adjure you by Allah — your God, the God of those before you, and the God of those after you — has Allah commanded you to order us to worship Him alone without associating anything with Him, and to abandon these rivals that our forefathers used to worship alongside Him?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” He asked: “I adjure you by Allah — your God, the God of those before you, and the God of those after you — has Allah commanded you that we perform these five prayers?” He replied: “O Allah, yes.” Ḍimām then continued mentioning the obligations of Islam one by one — zakāh, fasting, pilgrimage, and the other laws of Islam — adjuring him by Allah concerning each obligation just as he had done concerning the one before it. When he had finished, he said: “I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah. I will perform these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me, neither adding anything nor subtracting anything.” He then turned away and returned to his camel. As he departed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the man with the two braids is truthful, he will enter Paradise.” Ḍimām went to his camel, untied it, and departed until he reached his people.","They gathered around him. The first thing he said was: “Wretched are al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā!” They exclaimed: “Stop, O Ḍimām! Beware of vitiligo and leprosy! Beware of madness!” He replied: “Woe to you! By Allah, those two can neither harm nor benefit. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sent a Messenger and revealed to him a Book through which He has rescued you from the condition you were in. I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone with no partner, and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger. I have come to you from him with what he has commanded you and what he has forbidden you.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “By Allah, by that evening there was not a man or woman among those present except that they had embraced Islam.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “We never heard of any delegate of a people who was better than Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlabah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2380)، وأبو داود (487)، والحاكم (4380)."},{"num":30,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حَكِيمِ بْنِ مُعَاوِيَةَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: مَا أَتَيْتُكَ حَتَّى حَلَفْتُ عَدَدَ أَصَابِعِي هَذِهِ أَنْ لَا آتِيَكَ أَرَانَا عَفَّانُ وَطَبَّقَ كَفَّيْهِ، فَبِالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ، مَا الَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِهِ؟ قَالَ: الْإِسْلَامُ، قَالَ: وَمَا الْإِسْلَامُ؟ قَالَ: أَنْ يُسْلِمَ قَلْبُكَ لِلَّهِ، وَأَنْ تُوَجِّهَ وَجْهَكَ إِلَى اللَّهِ، وَتُصَلِّيَ الصَّلَاةَ الْمَكْتُوبَةَ، وَتُؤَدِّيَ الزَّكَاةَ الْمَفْرُوضَةَ، كُلُّ مُسْلِمٍ عَلَى مُسْلِمٍ، أَخَوَانِ نَصِيرَانِ، لَا يَقْبَلُ اللَّهُ مِنْ أَحَدٍ تَوْبَةً أَشْرَكَ بَعْدَ إِسْلَامِهِ. قُلْتُ: مَا حَقُّ زَوْجَةِ أَحَدِنَا عَلَيْهِ؟ قَالَ: تُطْعِمُهَا إِذَا طَعِمْتَ، وَتَكْسُوهَا إِذَا اكْتَسَيْتَ، وَلَا تَضْرِبْ الْوَجْهَ، وَلَا تُقَبِّحْ، وَلَا تَهْجُرْ إِلَّا فِي الْبَيْتِ.","قَالَ: تُحْشَرُونَ هَاهُنَا وَأَوْمَأَ بِيَدِهِ إِلَى نَحْوِ الشَّامِ، مُشَاةً وَرُكْبَانًا وَعَلَى وُجُوهِكُمْ، تُعْرَضُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ تَعَالَى وَعَلَى أَفْوَاهِكُمْ الْفِدَامُ، وَأَوَّلُ مَا يُعْرِبُ عَنْ أَحَدِكُمْ فَخِذُهُ. وَقَالَ: مَا مِنْ مَوْلًى يَأْتِي مَوْلًى لَهُ، فَيَسْأَلُهُ مِنْ فَضْلٍ عِنْدَهُ فَيَمْنَعُهُ، إِلَّا جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى عَلَيْهِ شُجَاعًا يَنْهَسُهُ قَبْلَ الْقَضَاءِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (20022) عن عفّان، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، أخبرنا أبو قزعة الباهليّ، عن حكيم بن معاوية، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20022), Abū Dāwūd (2142), Ibn Ḥibbān (160), and al-Nasāʾī (2436, 2568).","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated from his father may Allah be pleased with him: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I did not come to you until I had sworn, as many times as the number of these fingers of mine, that I would not come to you.” ʿAffān demonstrated by pressing his palms together. I said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, what has He sent you with?” He replied: “Islam.” I asked: “What is Islam?” He replied: “That your heart submit to Allah, that you turn your face toward Allah, perform the prescribed prayer, and pay the obligatory zakāh. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim; they are two brothers supporting one another. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept repentance from one who returns to associating partners with Him after embracing Islam.” I asked: “What right does the wife of one of us have over him?” He replied: “That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike her face, do not revile her, and do not abandon her except within the house.”","He also said: “You will be gathered here” — and he gestured with his hand toward the direction of al-Shām — “walking, riding, and upon your faces. You will be presented before Allah with restraints upon your mouths, and the first part of one of you to speak will be his thigh.” He also said: “No man comes to his cousin and asks him for some of the surplus he possesses, only for him to withhold it, except that Allah will make it into a serpent that will bite him before judgment.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (20022)، وأبو داود (2142)، وابن حبان (160)، والنسائي (2436، 2568)."},{"num":31,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بُنِيَ الْإِسْلَامُ عَلَى خَمْسٍ، شَهَادَةِ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَإِقَامِ الصَّلَاةِ، وَإِيتَاءِ الزَّكَاةِ، وَالْحَجِّ، وَصَوْمِ رَمَضَانَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (8)، ومسلم في الإيمان (16،22) كلاهما من حديث حنظلة بن أبي سفيان قال: سمعتُ عكرمة بن خالد، عن ابن عمر، فذكر الحديث، واللّفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السؤال عن أركان الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (8) and Muslim (16), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"Asking About the Pillars of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah; establishing the prayer; giving zakāh; performing pilgrimage; and fasting Ramaḍān.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[4293,4714],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (8)، ومسلم (16)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":32,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: الإِيمَانُ بِضْعٌ وَسِتُّونَ شُعْبَةً، وَالْحَيَاءُ شُعْبَةٌ مِنَ الإِيمَانِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (9)، ومسلم في الإيمان (35) كلاهما من حديث أبي عامر العقديّ، قال: حدثنا سليمان بن بلال، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره. واللفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم: بضع وسبعون شعبة.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شعب الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (9) and Muslim (35), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Branches of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Faith consists of sixty-something branches, and modesty is a branch of faith.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In Muslim’s wording:","“Faith consists of seventy-something branches — or sixty-something branches. The highest of them is the statement, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ and the lowest of them is removing something harmful from the road. Modesty is a branch of faith.”","Al-Khaṭṭābī, may Allah have mercy on him, said:","The meaning of the Prophet’s statement, “Modesty is a branch of faith,” is that modesty restrains its possessor from acts of disobedience. It therefore becomes part of faith, because faith consists of obeying what Allah has commanded and refraining from what He has forbidden."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (9)، ومسلم (35)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":33,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي أُمَامَةَ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ أَحَبَّ لِلَّهِ وَأَبْغَضَ لِلَّهِ وَأَعْطَى لِلَّهِ وَمَنَعَ لِلَّهِ، فَقَدِ اسْتَكْمَلَ الْإِيمَانَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4681) عن مؤمل بن الفضل، حدثنا محمد بن شُعيب بن شابور، عن يحي بن الحارث، عن القاسم، عن أبي أمامة فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4681).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves for Allah, hates for Allah, gives for Allah, and withholds for Allah has perfected faith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4681)."},{"num":34,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ أَنَسٍ الْجُهَنِيِّ أَنّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ أَعْطَى لِلَّهِ وَمَنَعَ لِلَّهِ، وَأَحَبَّ لِلَّهِ وَأَبْغَضَ لِلَّه، ِ وَأَنْكَحَ لِلَّهِ فَقَدِ اسْتَكْمَلَ إِيمَانَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2521) عن عباس الدُوري، حدثنا عبدالله بن يزيد، حدثنا سعيد بن أبي أيوب، عن أبي مرحوم عبدالرحيم بن ميمون، عن سهل بن معاذ بن أنس الجهني، عن أبيه، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2521), Aḥmad (15638), and al-Ḥākim (2694).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Anas al-Juhanī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and gives in marriage for Allah has perfected his faith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2521)، وأحمد (15638)، والحاكم (2694)."},{"num":35,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَكْمَلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِيمَانًا أَحْسَنُهُمْ خُلُقًا، وَخِيَارُكُمْ خِيَارُكُمْ لِنِسَائِهِمْ خُلُقًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1162) وأبو داود (4682) وابن حبان في صحيحه (479، 4176) كلهم من حديث محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكر الحديث. واللفظ للترمذي. واقتصر أبو داود على الشطر الأول. قال الترمذي: حسن صحيح.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1162), Abū Dāwūd (4682), and Ibn Ḥibbān (479, 4176).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believers with the most complete faith are those with the best character, and the best of you are those who are best in character toward their wives.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1162)، وأبو داود (4682)، وابن حبان (479، 4176)."},{"num":36,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَكْمَلُ النَّاسِ إِيمَانًا أَحْسَنُهُمْ خُلُقًا، وَإِنَّ حُسْنَ الْخُلُقِ لَيَبْلُغُ دَرَجَةَ الصَّوْمِ وَالصَّلَاةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار- كشف الأستار (35) وأبو يعلى (4166) كلاهما عن محمد بن المثنى أبو موسى، حدثنا زكريا بن يحيى الطائي، ثنا شُعيب بن الحبحاب، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (35) and Abū Yaʿlā (4166).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people with the most complete faith are those with the best character, and indeed good character can raise a person to the rank attained through fasting and prayer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (35)، وأبو يعلى (4166)."},{"num":37,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَكْمَلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِيمَانًا أَحْسَنُهُمْ خُلُقًا، الْمُوَطَّئُونَ أَكْنَافًا الَّذِينَ يَأْلَفُونَ وَيُؤْلَفُونَ، وَلَا خَيْرَ فِيمَنْ لَا يَأْلَفُ وَلَا يُؤْلَفُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (4422) والصغير sh13068(605)، مجمع البحرين (105)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (7616) كلاهما من طريق يعقوب بن أبي عبّاد القلزمي، حدثنا محمد بن عيينة، عن محمد بن عمرو بن علقمة، عن أبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ and al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr, as cited in Majmaʿ al-Baḥrayn (105), and by al-Bayhaqī in Shuʿab al-Īmān (7616).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believers with the most complete faith are those with the best character: those who are gentle and easy to approach, who form bonds of affection with others and are loved by others. There is no good in one who neither forms bonds with people nor allows others to form bonds with him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط والصغير، مجمع البحرين (105)، والبيهقي في الشعب (7616)."},{"num":38,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يَزْنِي الزَّانِي حِينَ يَزْنِي وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَشْرَبُ الْخَمْرَ حِينَ يَشْرَبُهَا وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَسْرِقُ السَّارِقُ حِينَ يَسْرِقُ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأشربة (5578)، ومسلم في الإيمان (57) كلاهما عن ابن وهب قال: أخبرني يونس، عن ابن شهاب قال: سمعتُ أبا سلمة بن عبدالرحمن، وابن المسيب يقولان: قال أبو هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5578) and Muslim (57).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer; the one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer; and the thief does not steal while he is a believer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5578)، ومسلم (57)."},{"num":39,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَزْنِي الْعَبْدُ حِينَ يَزْنِي وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَشْرَبُ الْخَمْرَ حِينَ يَشْرَبُهَا، وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَسْرِقُ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَقْتُلُ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ.","قَالَ عِكْرِمَةُ: قُلْتُ لِابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: كَيْفَ يُنْزَعُ الْإِيمَانُ مِنْهُ؟ قَالَ: هَكَذَا: وَشَبَّكَ بَيْنَ أَصَابِعِهِ ثُمَّ أَخْرَجَهَا، فَإِنْ تَابَ، عَادَ إِلَيْهِ هَكَذَا: وَشَبَّكَ بَيْنَ أَصَابِعِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحدود (6809) عن محمد بن المثنى، أخبرنا إسحاق بن يوسف، أخبرنا الفضيل بن غزوان، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس، فذكرت الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6809).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant does not commit fornication while he is a believer, does not steal while he is a believer, does not drink intoxicants while he is a believer, and does not kill while he is a believer.”","ʿIkrimah said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās: “How is faith removed from him?” He replied: “Like this.” He interlaced his fingers and then separated them. He then said: “If he repents, it returns to him.” He interlaced his fingers again."]},"buhuth":{"ar":["«فإن تاب عاد إليه».","وشبك بين أصابعه.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٨٠٩)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6809)."},{"num":40,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَزْنِي الزَّانِي حِينَ يَزْنِي وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَسْرِقُ حِينَ يَسْرِقُ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار- كشف الأستار (112)، عن محمد بن المثنى، ثنا محمد بن الفضل، ثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (112).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (112)."},{"num":41,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِي أَوْفَى، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يَشْرَبُ الْخَمْرَ حِينَ يَشْرَبُهَا وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَزْنِي حِينَ يَزْنِي وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يَنْتَهِبُ نُهْبَةً ذَاتَ شَرَفٍ أَوْ سَرَفٍ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (19102)، والبزّار- كشف الأستار (111)، كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن فراس، عن مدرك بن عُمارة، عن ابن أبي أوفى، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (19102) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (111).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Abī Awfā may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer; the one who commits fornication does not commit it while he is a believer; and the one who plunders a notorious or valuable booty does not do so while he is a believer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (19102)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (111)."},{"num":42,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بإِذَا زَنَى الرَّجُلُ خَرَجَ مِنْهُ الْإِيمَانُ كَانَ عَلَيْهِ كَالظُّلَّةِ فَإِذَا انْقَطَعَ رَجَعَ إِلَيْهِ الْإِيمَانُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4690) عن إسحاق بن سويد الرّمليّ، حدثنا ابن أبي مريم، أخبرنا نافع، يعني ابن زيد، ، قال: حدثني ابن الهاد، أن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبريّ حدّثه، أنه سمع أبا هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4690), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (56).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man commits fornication, faith departs from him and remains above him like a canopy. When he ceases from the act, faith returns to him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4690)، وصححه الحاكم (56)."},{"num":43,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: مَا خَطَبَنَا نَبِيُّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِلَّا قَالَ: لَا إِيمَانَ لِمَنْ لَا أَمَانَةَ لَهُ، وَلَا دِينَ لِمَنْ لَا عَهْدَ لَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (12383)، وأبو يعلى (2863)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (100)، ، والطبراني في الأوسط (2627) كلّهم من طريق أبي هلال، حدثنا قتادة، عن أنس، قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب النقص في كمال الإيمان بالمعاصي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (12383), Abū Yaʿlā (2863), and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (100).","chapter_en":"The Diminution of Perfect Faith Through Acts of Disobedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ never delivered a sermon to us except that he said in it: “There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who does not honor his covenant.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Nawawī (may Allah have mercy on him) said in his commentary on Muslim: This ḥadīth is one in which scholars differed regarding its meaning. The correct view held by the verifying scholars is that the meaning is that a person does not commit these sins while being complete in faith. This is a style of wording in which something is negated while what is intended is the negation of its perfection, like the sayings, “No knowledge except what benefits,” “No wealth except camels,” and “No life except the life of the Hereafter.” We interpret it this way because of the ḥadīth of Abū Dharr and others: “Whoever says ‘lā ilāha illa Allāh’ will enter Paradise, even if he committed fornication and even if he stole.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15038],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (12383)، وأبو يعلى (2863)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (100)."},{"num":44,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي أَضْحَى أَوْ فِطْرٍ إِلَى الْمُصَلَّى، فَمَرَّ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ فَقَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ، تَصَدَّقْنَ فَإِنِّي أُرِيتُكُنَّ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقُلْنَ: وَبِمَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: تُكْثِرْنَ اللَّعْنَ، وَتَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ مَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ نَاقِصَاتِ عَقْلٍ وَدِينٍ أَذْهَبَ لِلُبِّ الرَّجُلِ الْحَازِمِ مِنْ إِحْدَاكُنَّ، قُلْنَ: وَمَا نُقْصَانُ دِينِنَا وَعَقْلِنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: أَلَيْسَ شَهَادَةُ الْمَرْأَةِ مِثْلَ نِصْفِ شَهَادَةِ الرَّجُلِ؟ قُلْنَ: بَلَى، قَالَ: فَذَلِكِ مِنْ نُقْصَانِ عَقْلِهَا، أَلَيْسَ إِذَا حَاضَتْ لَمْ تُصَلِّ وَلَمْ تَصُمْ؟ قُلْنَ: بَلَى، قَالَ: فَذَلِكِ مِنْ نُقْصَانِ دِينِهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحيض (304) عن سعيد بن أبي مريم، أخبرنا محمد بن جعفر، قال: أخبرني زيد، وهو ابن أسلم، ، عن عياض بن عبدالله، عن أبي سعيد الخدريّ، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان نقصان الإيمان بنقص الطاعات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (304) and Muslim (80).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Diminution of Faith Through Deficiency in Acts of Obedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the prayer ground on the day of al-Aḍḥā or al-Fiṭr. He passed by the women and said: “O assembly of women, give charity, for I have been shown that you constitute the majority of the people of the Fire.” They asked: “Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more capable of overcoming the judgment of a resolute man than one of you.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the deficiency in our religion and intellect?” He replied: “Is not the testimony of a woman equal to half the testimony of a man?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “That is from the deficiency in her intellect. And is it not the case that when she menstruates, she does not pray and does not fast?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “That is from the deficiency in her religion.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (304)، ومسلم (80)."},{"num":45,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ تَصَدَّقْنَ، وَأَكْثِرْنَ الِاسْتِغْفَارَ، فَإِنِّي رَأَيْتُكُنَّ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقَالَتِ امْرَأَةٌ مِنْهُنَّ جَزْلَةٌ: وَمَا لَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ؟ قَالَ: تُكْثِرْنَ اللَّعْنَ، وَتَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ، وَمَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ نَاقِصَاتِ عَقْلٍ وَدِينٍ أَغْلَبَ لِذِي لُبٍّ مِنْكُنَّ، قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَمَا نُقْصَانُ الْعَقْلِ وَالدِّينِ؟ قَالَ: أَمَّا نُقْصَانُ الْعَقْلِ، فَشَهَادَةُ امْرَأَتَيْنِ تَعْدِلُ شَهَادَةَ رَجُلٍ، فَهَذَا نُقْصَانُ الْعَقْلِ، وَتَمْكُثُ اللَّيَالِي، مَا تُصَلِّي، وَتُفْطِرُ فِي رَمَضَانَ، فَهَذَا نُقْصَانُ الدِّينِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (79) عن محمد بن رمح، أخبرنا اللّيث، عن ابن الهاد، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان نقصان الإيمان بنقص الطاعات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (79).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Diminution of Faith Through Deficiency in Acts of Obedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O assembly of women, give charity and frequently seek forgiveness, for I have seen that you constitute the majority of the people of the Fire.” A woman among them who was intelligent and strong-minded asked: “Why are we the majority of the people of the Fire, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more capable of overcoming a person of sound judgment than you.” She asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the deficiency in intellect and religion?” He replied: “As for the deficiency in intellect, the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man; this is the deficiency in intellect. And you remain for nights without praying, and you refrain from fasting during Ramaḍān; this is the deficiency in religion.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression «امرأة منهن جزلة» means a woman of intelligence, sound judgment, and firm opinion."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6747],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (79)."},{"num":46,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، بِمِثْلِ مَعْنَى حَدِيثِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (80) عن يحيى بن أيوب، وقتيبة، وابن حجر قالوا: حدثنا إسماعيل (وهو ابن جعفر)، عن عمرو بن أبي عمرو، عن المقبريّ، عن أبي هريرة ولم يسق لفظ الحديث وإنّما أحال على لفظ حديث ابن عمر.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان نقصان الإيمان بنقص الطاعات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (80).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Diminution of Faith Through Deficiency in Acts of Obedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him narrated from the Prophet ﷺ a report similar to the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (80)."},{"num":47,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَة: أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ انْصَرَفَ مِنَ الصُّبْحِ يَوْمًا، فَأَتَى النِّسَاءَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ، فَوَقَفَ عَلَيْهِنَّ، فَقَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ، مَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ نَوَاقِصِ عُقُولٍ وَدِينٍ أَذْهَبَ لِقُلُوبِ ذَوِي الْأَلْبَابِ مِنْكُنَّ، فَإِنِّي قَدْ رَأَيْتُكُنَّ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، فَتَقَرَّبْنَ إِلَى اللَّهِ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُنَّ، وَكَانَ فِي النِّسَاءِ امْرَأَةُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، فَأَتَتْ إِلَى عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، فَأَخْبَرَتْهُ بِمَا سَمِعَتْ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَخَذَتْ حُلِيًّا لَهَا، فَقَالَ ابْنُ مَسْعُودٍ: فَأَيْنَ تَذْهَبِينَ بِهَذَا الْحُلِيِّ؟ فَقَالَتْ: أَتَقَرَّبُ بِهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ وَرَسُولِهِ، لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ أَنْ لَا يَجْعَلَنِي مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقَالَ: وَيْلَكِ، هَلُمِّي فَتَصَدَّقِي بِهِ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَى وَلَدِي، فَإِنَّا لَهُ مَوْضِعٌ، فَقَالَتْ: لَا وَاللَّهِ حَتَّى أَذْهَبَ بِهِ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَهَبَتْ تَسْتَأْذِنُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالُوا لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَذِهِ زَيْنَبُ تَسْتَأْذِنُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَقَالَ: أَيُّ الزَّيَانِبِ هِيَ؟ فَقَالُوا: امْرَأَةُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنُوا لَهَا، فَدَخَلَتْ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنِّي سَمِعْتُ مِنْكَ مَقَالَةً، فَرَجَعْتُ إِلَى ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ فَحَدَّثْتُهُ، وَأَخَذْتُ حُلِيًّا أَتَقَرَّبُ بِهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَإِلَيْكَ رَجَاءَ أَنْ لَا يَجْعَلَنِي اللَّهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقَالَ لِي ابْنُ مَسْعُودٍ: تَصَدَّقِي بِهِ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَى وَلَدِي، فَإِنَّا لَهُ مَوْضِعٌ، فَقُلْتُ: حَتَّى أَسْتَأْذِنَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: تَصَدَّقِي بِهِ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَى بَنِيهِ فَإِنَّهُمْ لَهُ مَوْضِعٌ، ثُمَّ قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَرَأَيْتَ مَا سَمِعْتُ مِنْكَ حِينَ وَقَفْتَ عَلَيْنَا: مَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ نَوَاقِصِ عُقُولٍ قَطُّ وَلَا دِينٍ أَذْهَبَ بِقُلُوبِ ذَوِي الْأَلْبَابِ مِنْكُنَّ، قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَمَا نُقْصَانُ دِينِنَا وَعُقُولِنَا؟ فَقَالَ: أَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتُ مِنْ نُقْصَانِ دِينِكُنَّ: فَالْحَيْضَةُ الَّتِي تُصِيبُكُنَّ، تَمْكُثُ إِحْدَاكُنَّ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَنْ تَمْكُثَ لَا تُصَلِّي وَلَا تَصُومُ، فَذَلِكَ مِنْ نُقْصَانِ دِينِكُنَّ، وَأَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتُ مِنْ نُقْصَانِ عُقُولِكُنَّ: فَشَهَادَتُكُنَّ، إِنَّمَا شَهَادَةُ الْمَرْأَةِ نِصْفُ شَهَادَةٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (8862) عن سليمان، أخبرنا إسماعيل، أخبرني عمرو، يعني ابن أبي عمرو، ، عن أبي سعيد المقبريّ، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان نقصان الإيمان بنقص الطاعات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8862) and Ibn Khuzaymah (2461).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Diminution of Faith Through Deficiency in Acts of Obedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: One day, after the Prophet ﷺ had completed the dawn prayer, he went to the women in the mosque, stood before them, and said: “O assembly of women, I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more capable of taking away the hearts of people of sound understanding than you. I have been shown that you will constitute the majority of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, so draw near to Allah as much as you are able.” Among the women was the wife of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd. She went to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd and informed him of what she had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she took some of her jewelry. Ibn Masʿūd asked: “Where are you going with this jewelry?” She replied: “I wish to draw near to Allah and His Messenger through it, hoping that Allah will not make me among the people of the Fire.” He said: “Woe to you! Come and give it in charity to me and to my children, for we are suitable recipients of it.” She replied: “No, by Allah, not until I take it to the Prophet ﷺ.” She went and sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, Zaynab is asking permission to enter.” He asked: “Which Zaynab?” They replied: “The wife of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd.” He said: “Allow her to enter.” She entered and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I heard something from you, so I returned to Ibn Masʿūd and informed him. I took my jewelry intending to draw near through it to Allah and to you, hoping that Allah would not make me among the people of the Fire. Ibn Masʿūd told me, ‘Give it in charity to me and my children, for we are suitable recipients of it.’ I said that I would first ask the Prophet ﷺ.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Give it in charity to him and to his children, for they are suitable recipients of it.” She then asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about what I heard you say when you stood before us: ‘I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more capable of taking away the hearts of people of sound understanding than you’? What is the deficiency in our religion and intellect?” He replied: “As for the deficiency in your religion, it is the menstruation that affects you. One of you remains for as long as Allah wills without praying or fasting, and that is from the deficiency in your religion. As for what I mentioned concerning the deficiency in your intellect, it is your testimony: the testimony of a woman is half a testimony.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (8862)، وابن خزيمة (2461)."},{"num":48,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: تَصَدَّقْنَ يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ، وَلَوْ مِنْ حُلِيِّكُنَّ، فَإِنَّكُنَّ أَكْثَرُ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقَامَتِ امْرَأَةٌ لَيْسَتْ مِنْ عِلْيَةِ النِّسَاءِ، فَقَالَتْ: لِمَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: لِأَنَّكُنَّ تُكْثِرْنَ اللَّعْنَ، وَتَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةِ: وَمَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ نَاقِصَاتِ عَقْلٍ وَدِينٍ أَغْلَبَ لِلُبِّ الرَّجُلِ مِنْكُنَّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (3569، 4152)، وأبو يعلى (5112، 5144)، والحاكم (2772)، كلهم من طريق منصور بن أبي الأسود، عن ذر، عن وائل بن مهانة، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان نقصان الإيمان بنقص الطاعات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (3569, 4152), Abū Yaʿlā (5112, 5144), and al-Ḥākim (2772).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Diminution of Faith Through Deficiency in Acts of Obedience","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give charity, O assembly of women, even from your jewelry, for you constitute the majority of the people of the Fire.” A woman who was not among the prominent women stood and asked: “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Because you frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands.” In another narration: “I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more capable of overcoming the judgment of men than you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (3569، 4152)، وأبو يعلى (5112، 5144)، والحاكم (2772)."},{"num":49,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ (فَذَكَرَهُ فِي حَدِيثِ طَوِيلٍ): قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: حَتَّى إِذَا خَلَصَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ مِنَ النَّارِ، فَوَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ، مَا مِنْكُمْ مِنْ أَحَدٍ بِأَشَدَّ مُنَاشَدَةً لِلَّهِ فِي اسْتِقْصَاءِ الْحَقِّ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، لِلَّهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ لِإِخْوَانِهِمُ الَّذِينَ فِي النَّارِ، يَقُولُونَ: رَبَّنَا كَانُوا يَصُومُونَ مَعَنَا، وَيُصَلُّونَ، وَيَحُجُّونَ، فَيُقَالُ لَهُمْ: أَخْرِجُوا مَنْ عَرَفْتُمْ، فَتُحَرَّمُ صُوَرُهُمْ عَلَى النَّار، فَيُخْرِجُونَ خَلْقًا كَثِيرًا قَدْ أَخَذَتِ النَّارُ إِلَى نِصْفِ سَاقَيْهِ وَإِلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ، ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ: رَبَّنَا مَا بَقِيَ فِيهَا أَحَدٌ مِمَّنْ أَمَرْتَنَا بِهِ، فَيَقُولُ: ارْجِعُوا، فَمَنْ وَجَدْتُمْ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالَ دِينَارٍ مِنْ خَيْرٍ، فَأَخْرِجُوهُ فَيُخْرِجُونَ خَلْقًا كَثِيرًا، ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ: رَبَّنَا لَمْ نَذَرْ فِيهَا أَحَدًا مِمَّنْ أَمَرْتَنَا، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: ارْجِعُوا فَمَنْ وَجَدْتُمْ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالَ نِصْفِ دِينَارٍ مِنَ خَيْرٍ فَأَخْرِجُوهُ، فَيُخْرِجُونَ خَلْقًا كَثِيرًا، ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ: رَبَّنَا لَمْ نَذَرْ فِيهَا مِمَّنْ أَمَرْتَنَا أَحَدًا، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: ارْجِعُوا فَمَنْ وَجَدْتُمْ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ مِنْ خَيْر، فَأَخْرِجُوهُ فَيُخْرِجُونَ خَلْقًا كَثِيرًا، ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ: رَبَّنَا لَمْ نَذَرْ فِيهَا خَيْرًا.","وَكَانَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيُّ، يَقُولُ: إِنْ لَمْ تُصَدِّقُونِي بِهَذَا الْحَدِيثِ، فَاقْرَءُوا إِنْ شِئْتُمْ ﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضَاعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا﴾ [سورة النساء: 40]. فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: شَفَعَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ، وَشَفَعَ النَّبِيُّونَ، وَشَفَعَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ، وَلَمْ يَبْقَ إِلَّا أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ، فَيَقْبِضُ قَبْضَةً مِنَ النَّارِ، فَيُخْرِجُ مِنْهَا قَوْمًا لَمْ يَعْمَلُوا خَيْرًا قَطُّ، قَدْ عَادُوا حُمَمًا، فَيُلْقِيهِمْ فِي نَهَرٍ فِي أَفْوَاهِ الْجَنَّةِ، يُقَالُ لَهُ: نَهَرُ الْحَيَاةِ، فَيَخْرُجُونَ كَمَا تَخْرُجُ الْحِبَّةُ فِي حَمِيلِ السَّيْلِ...الْحَدِيثَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التوحيد (7439)، ومسلم في الإيمان (183) كلاهما عن زيد بن أسلم، عن عطاء بن يسار، عن أبي سعيد، واللّفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tawḥīd (7439) and Muslim in al-Īmān (183).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the believers have been delivered from the Fire, then by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of you will plead more insistently with Allah in seeking justice than the believers will plead with Allah on the Day of Resurrection on behalf of their brothers who are in the Fire. They will say: ‘Our Lord, they used to fast with us, pray with us, and perform ḥajj with us.’ It will be said to them: ‘Bring out those whom you recognize.’ Their forms will be made forbidden to the Fire, and they will bring out a great number of people whom the Fire had reached as far as the middle of their shins or their knees. They will then say: ‘Our Lord, none remains among those whom You commanded us to bring out.’ He will say: ‘Return, and whoever you find in whose heart there is the weight of a dīnār of goodness, bring him out.’ They will bring out a great number of people. They will then say: ‘Our Lord, we have left no one among those whom You commanded us to bring out.’ He will say: ‘Return, and whoever you find in whose heart there is the weight of half a dīnār of goodness, bring him out.’ They will bring out a great number of people. They will then say: ‘Our Lord, we have left no one among those whom You commanded us to bring out.’ He will say: ‘Return, and whoever you find in whose heart there is the weight of an atom of goodness, bring him out.’ They will bring out a great number of people. They will then say: ‘Our Lord, we have left no goodness remaining there.’”","Abū Saʿīd used to say: If you do not believe me concerning this ḥadīth, then recite, if you wish: “Indeed, Allah does not wrong even by the weight of an atom; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a tremendous reward.” [Sūrat al-Nisāʾ 4:40] Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will then say: “The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded. None remains except the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.” He will then take a handful from the Fire and bring forth from it people who had never performed any good deed. They will have become like pieces of charcoal. He will cast them into a river at the entrances of Paradise called the River of Life, and they will emerge from it as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿وَمَا زَادَهُمْ إِلَّا إِيمَانًا وَتَسْلِيمًا﴾","[الأحزاب: ٢٢]","وقال جل ذكره:","﴿وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِيمَانًا﴾","[المدثر: ٣١]","وقال تبارك وتعالى:","﴿فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَزَادَتْهُمْ إِيمَانًا﴾","[التوبة: ١٢٤]","وقال تعالى:","﴿فَاخْشَوْهُمْ فَزَادَهُمْ إِيمَانًا﴾","[آل عمران: ١٧٣]","وقال تعالى:","﴿لِيَزْدَادُوا إِيمَانًا مَعَ إِيمَانِهِمْ﴾","[الفتح: ٤]"],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“And it only increased them in faith and submission.”","[Sūrat al-Aḥzāb 33:22]","And He, Glorified is His remembrance, said:","“So that those who believe may increase in faith.”","[Sūrat al-Muddaththir 74:31]","And He, Blessed and Exalted, said:","“As for those who believe, it increases them in faith.”","[Sūrat al-Tawbah 9:124]","And He said:","“So fear them; and it increased them in faith.”","[Āl ʿImrān 3:173]","And He said:","“So that they may increase in faith along with their faith.”","[Sūrat al-Fatḥ 48:4]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7439)، ومسلم (183)."},{"num":50,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: يَدْخُلُ أَهْلُ الْجَنَّةِ الْجَنَّةَ، وَأَهْلُ النَّارِ النَّارَ، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: أَخْرِجُوا مَنْ كَانَ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالُ حَبَّةٍ مِنْ خَرْدَلٍ مِنْ إِيمَانٍ، فَيُخْرَجُونَ مِنْهَا قَدِ اسْوَدُّوا، فَيُلْقَوْنَ فِي نَهَرِ الْحَيَا أَوِ الْحَيَاةِ شَكَّ مَالِكٌ فَيَنْبُتُونَ كَمَا تَنْبُتُ الْحِبَّةُ فِي جَانِبِ السَّيْلِ، أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهَا تَخْرُجُ صَفْرَاءَ مُلْتَوِيَةً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الإيمان (22) عن إسماعيل، ومسلم في الإيمان (184) من حديث ابن وهب، كلاهما عن مالك، عن عمرو بن يحيى بن عمارة المازنيّ، قال: حدثني أبي، عن أبي سعيد الخدريّ، فذكر الحديث، واللفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Īmān (22) and Muslim in al-Īmān (184).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of the Fire will enter the Fire. Then Allah Most High will say: ‘Bring out of the Fire whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith.’ They will be brought out, having become blackened, and they will be cast into the River of Life — Mālik was uncertain regarding the exact form of the word — and they will grow as a seed grows at the edge of a stream. Have you not seen how it emerges yellow and curved?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (22)، ومسلم (184)."},{"num":51,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: يَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ مَنْ قَالَ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَفِي قَلْبِهِ وَزْنُ شَعِيرَةٍ مِنْ خَيْرٍ، وَيَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ مَنْ قَالَ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَفِي قَلْبِهِ وَزْنُ بُرَّةٍ مِنْ خَيْرٍ، وَيَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ مَنْ قَالَ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَفِي قَلْبِهِ وَزْنُ ذَرَّةٍ مِنْ خَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (44)، ومسلم في الإيمان (193: 325) كلاهما من حديث هشام صاحب الدستوائيّ، قال: حدثنا قتادة، عن أنس، فذكره، واللّفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم قريب منه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Īmān (44) and Muslim in al-Īmān (193).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There will come out of the Fire whoever said, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ while in his heart was the weight of a barley grain of goodness. And there will come out of the Fire whoever said, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ while in his heart was the weight of a grain of wheat of goodness. And there will come out of the Fire whoever said, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ while in his heart was the weight of an atom of goodness.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[16190],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (44)، ومسلم (193)."},{"num":52,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ النَّارَ أَحَدٌ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالُ حَبَّةِ خَرْدَلٍ مِنَ إِيمَانٍ، وَلَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ أَحَدٌ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالُ حَبَّةِ خَرْدَلٍ مِنْ كِبْرِيَاءَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (91: 148) من طرق عن علي بن مسهر، عن الأعمش، عن إبراهيم، عن علقمة، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim in al-Īmān (91).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith will enter the Fire, and no one who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (91)."},{"num":53,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا مُيِّزَ أَهْلُ الْجَنَّةِ وَأَهْلُ النَّارِ، فَدَخَلَ أَهْلُ الْجَنَّةِ الْجَنَّةَ، وَأَهْلُ النَّارِ النَّارَ، قَامَتْ الرُّسُلُ فَشَفَعُوا فَيَقُولُ: انْطَلِقُوا، أَوْ اذْهَبُوا، فَمَنْ عَرَفْتُمْ فَأَخْرِجُوهُ، فَيُخْرِجُونَهُمْ قَدْ امْتُحِشُوا، فَيُلْقُونَهُمْ فِي نَهَرٍ، أَوْ عَلَى نَهَرٍ، يُقَالُ لَهُ الْحَيَاةُ، قَالَ: فَتَسْقُطُ مَحَاشُّهُمْ عَلَى حَافَةِ النَّهَرِ، وَيَخْرُجُونَ بِيضًا مِثْلَ الثَّعَارِيرِ ثُمَّ يَشْفَعُونَ، فَيَقُولُ: اذْهَبُوا أَوْ انْطَلِقُوا فَمَنْ وَجَدْتُمْ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالَ قِيرَاطٍ مِنْ إِيمَانٍ فَأَخْرِجُوهُمْ، قَالَ: فَيُخْرِجُونَ بَشَرًا، ثُمَّ يَشْفَعُونَ، فَيَقُولُ: اذْهَبُوا أَوْ انْطَلِقُوا فَمَنْ وَجَدْتُمْ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِنْ خَرْدَلَةٍ مِنْ إِيمَانٍ فَأَخْرِجُوهُ، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: أَنَا الْآنَ أُخْرِجُ بِعِلْمِي وَرَحْمَتِي، قَالَ: فَيُخْرِجُ أَضْعَافَ مَا أَخْرَجُوا وَأَضْعَافَهُ، فَيُكْتَبُ فِي رِقَابِهِمْ عُتَقَاءُ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ، ثُمَّ يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ، فَيُسَمَّوْنَ فِيهَا الْجَهَنَّمِيِّينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14491، 15048) من وجهين عن أبي الزبير، قال: حدثني جابر، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (14491, 15048).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire have been separated, and the people of Paradise have entered Paradise while the people of the Fire have entered the Fire, the messengers will stand and intercede. It will be said: ‘Go — or proceed — and bring out everyone you recognize.’ They will bring them out after they have been severely burned, and they will cast them into a river — or beside a river — called the River of Life. Their burned flesh will fall away at the bank of the river, and they will emerge white, like small cucumbers. Then they will intercede again, and it will be said: ‘Go — or proceed — and bring out whoever you find in whose heart there is the weight of a qīrāṭ of faith.’ They will bring out people. Then they will intercede again, and it will be said: ‘Go — or proceed — and bring out whoever you find in whose heart there is the weight of a mustard seed of faith.’ Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘Now I will bring people out through My knowledge and My mercy.’ He will bring out many times as many as those whom they brought out, and upon their necks will be written: ‘Those freed by Allah.’ They will then enter Paradise and will be called therein al-Jahannamiyyūn — those who had formerly been in Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14491، 15048)."},{"num":54,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جُنْدُبِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَنَحْنُ فِتْيَانٌ حَزَاوِرَةٌ، فَتَعَلَّمْنَا الْإِيمَانَ قَبْلَ أَنْ نَتَعَلَّمَ الْقُرْآنَ، ثُمَّ تَعَلَّمْنَا الْقُرْآنَ فَازْدَدْنَا بِهِ إِيمَانًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (61) عن علي بن محمد، قال: حدثنا وكيع، قال: حدثنا حماد بن نجيح، وكان ثقة، ، عن أبي عمران الجوني، عن جندب، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (61).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jundub ibn ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: “We were with the Prophet ﷺ while we were strong young men. We learned faith before we learned the Qurʾān. Then we learned the Qurʾān, and through it we increased in faith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (61)."},{"num":55,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ الإِيمَانَ لَيَخْلَقُ فِي جَوْفِ أَحَدِكُمْ كَمَا يَخْلَقُ الثَّوْبُ الْخَلِقُ، فَاسْأَلُوا اللَّهَ أَنْ يُجَدِّدَ الإِيمَانَ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (5) عن أبي جعفر محمد بن صالح بن هانئ، حدثنا محمد بن إسماعيل بن مهران، ثنا أبو الطاهر، أنبأنا ابنُ وهب، أخبرني عبدالرحمن بن ميسرة، عن أبي هانئ الخولاني حميد بن هانئ، عن أبي عبدالرحمن الحبلّي، عن عبدالله بن عمرو بن العاص قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة الإيمان ونقصانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Good: Reported by al-Ḥākim (1/45).","chapter_en":"The Increase and Decrease of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, faith wears out within one of you just as a worn-out garment wears out. So ask Allah to renew faith in your hearts.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (5)."},{"num":56,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي أَيُّوبَ، أَنَّ رَجُلًا قَالَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَخْبِرْنِي بِعَمَلٍ يُدْخِلُنِي الْجَنَّةَ، قَالَ (أَيْ الْقَوْمِ): مَا لَهُ، مَا لَهُ، وَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَرَبٌ مَا لَهُ تَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِي الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الزكاة (1396)، ومسلم في الإيمان (13) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، حدثنا محمد بن عثمان بن عبدالله بن موهب، وأبوه عثمان كلاهما سمعا موسى بن طلحة يحدّث عن أبي أيوب، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Zakāh (1396) and Muslim in al-Īmān (13).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Ayyūb, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise.” The people said: “What is the matter with him? What is the matter with him?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He has an important need.” Then he said: “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, give zakāh, and maintain the ties of kinship.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1396)، ومسلم (13)."},{"num":57,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ أَعْرَابِيًّا أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: دُلَّنِي عَلَى عَمَلٍ إِذَا عَمِلْتُهُ دَخَلْتُ الْجَنَّةَ ؟، قَالَ: تَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ لَا تُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ الْمَكْتُوبَةَ، وَتُؤَدِّي الزَّكَاةَ الْمَفْرُوضَةَ، وَتَصُومُ رَمَضَانَ، قَالَ: وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ لَا أَزِيدُ عَلَى هَذَا، فَلَمَّا وَلَّى قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ سَرَّهُ أَنْ يَنْظُرَ إِلَى رَجُلٍ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، فَلْيَنْظُرْ إِلَى هَذَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الزّكاة (1397)، ومسلم في الإيمان (14)، كلاهما من حديث عفّان بن عثمان، حدّثنا وهيب، عن يحيى بن سعيد بن حيّان، عن أبي زرعة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Zakāh (1397) and Muslim in al-Īmān (14).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Guide me to a deed which, if I perform it, will cause me to enter Paradise.” He replied: “Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakāh, and fast Ramaḍān.” The man said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will add nothing to this.” When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this man.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1397)، ومسلم (14)."},{"num":58,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي جَمْرَةَ قَالَ: كُنْتُ أَقْعُدُ مَعَ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ يُجْلِسُنِي عَلَى سَرِيرِهِ فَقَالَ: أَقِمْ عِنْدِي حَتَّى أَجْعَلَ لَكَ سَهْمًا مِنْ مَالِي، فَأَقَمْتُ مَعَهُ شَهْرَيْنِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنَّ وَفْدَ عَبْدِ الْقَيْسِ لَمَّا أَتَوْا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: مَنِ الْقَوْمُ أَوْ مَنِ الْوَفْدُ؟ قَالُوا: رَبِيعَةُ، قَالَ: مَرْحَبًا بِالْقَوْمِ أَوْ بِالْوَفْدِ غَيْرَ خَزَايَا وَلَا نَدَامَى، فَقَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّا لَا نَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ نَأْتَيِكَ إِلَّا فِي شَهْرِ الْحَرَامِ وَبَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ هَذَا الْحَيُّ مِنْ كُفَّارِ مُضَرَ، فَمُرْنَا بِأَمْرٍ فَصْلٍ نُخْبِرْ بِهِ مَنْ وَرَاءَنَا وَنَدْخُلْ بِهِ الْجَنَّةَ، وَسَأَلُوهُ عَنِ الْأَشْرِبَةِ؟ فَأَمَرَهُمْ بِأَرْبَعٍ وَنَهَاهُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ، أَمَرَهُمْ بِالْإِيمَانِ بِاللَّهِ وَحْدَهُ، قَالَ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَا الْإِيمَانُ بِاللَّهِ وَحْدَهُ؟ قَالُوا: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: شَهَادَةُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَإِقَامُ الصَّلَاةِ، وَإِيتَاءُ الزَّكَاةِ، وَصِيَامُ رَمَضَانَ، وَأَنْ تُعْطُوا مِنَ الْمَغْنَمِ الْخُمُسَ، وَنَهَاهُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ: عَنِ الْحَنْتَمِ وَالدُّبَّاءِ وَالنَّقِيرِ وَالْمُزَفَّتِ، وَرُبَّمَا قَالَ: الْمُقَيَّرِ، وَقَالَ: احْفَظُوهُنَّ وَأَخْبِرُوا بِهِنَّ مَنْ وَرَاءَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (53)، ومسلم في الإيمان (17) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن أبي جمرة، فذكره، واللّفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Īmān (53) and Muslim in al-Īmān (17).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Jamrah reported: I used to sit with Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them, and he would seat me upon his couch. He said: “Stay with me, and I will assign you a share from my wealth.” So I remained with him for two months. He then said: “When the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ, he asked: ‘Who are the people?’ — or, ‘Who is the delegation?’ They replied: ‘Rabīʿah.’ He said: ‘Welcome to the people — or the delegation — who have come without disgrace and without regret.’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we are unable to come to you except during the sacred month, for between us and you lies this tribe of the disbelievers of Muḍar. Command us with a decisive matter that we can convey to those whom we have left behind and through which we may enter Paradise.’ They also asked him about drinks. He commanded them with four matters and prohibited them from four. He commanded them to believe in Allah alone. He asked: ‘Do you know what belief in Allah alone is?’ They replied: ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said: ‘To testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah; to establish the prayer; to give zakāh; to fast Ramaḍān; and to give one-fifth of the spoils of war.’ He prohibited them from four things: al-ḥantam, al-dubbāʾ, al-naqīr, and al-muzaffat — and sometimes he said al-muqayyar. He said: ‘Memorize these matters and convey them to those whom you have left behind.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “al-muqayyar” means al-muzaffat: a vessel coated with pitch or tar. It has also been said that zift is a type of pitch. The purpose of forbidding these four was to forbid preparing fermented drinks (nabīdh) in these particular containers, because intoxication develops quickly in them and the drink then becomes unlawful."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9767],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (53)، ومسلم (17)."},{"num":59,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: إِنَّ أُنَاسًا مِنْ عَبْدِ الْقَيْسِ، قَدِمُوا عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالُوا: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، إِنَّا حَيٌّ مِنْ رَبِيعَةَ، وَبَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ كُفَّارُ مُضَرَ، وَلَا نَقْدِرُ عَلَيْكَ إِلَّا فِي أَشْهُرِ الْحُرُمِ، فَمُرْنَا بِأَمْرٍ نَأْمُرُ بِهِ مَنْ وَرَاءَنَا وَنَدْخُلُ بِهِ الْجَنَّةَ، إِذَا نَحْنُ أَخَذْنَا بِهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: آمُرُكُمْ بِأَرْبَعٍ وَأَنْهَاكُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ، اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ، وَآتُوا الزَّكَاةَ، وَصُومُوا رَمَضَانَ، وَأَعْطُوا الْخُمُسَ مِنَ الْغَنَائِمِ، وَأَنْهَاكُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ، عَنِ الدُّبَّاءِ، وَالْحَنْتَمِ، وَالْمُزَفَّتِ، وَالنَّقِيرِ، قَالُوا: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، مَا عِلْمُكَ بِالنَّقِيرِ؟ قَالَ: بَلَى، جِذْعٌ تَنْقُرُونَهُ فَتَقْذِفُونَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْقُطَيْعَاءِ، قَالَ سَعِيدٌ أَوَ قَالَ: مِنَ التَّمْرِ، ثُمَّ تَصُبُّونَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْمَاءِ، حَتَّى إِذَا سَكَنَ غَلَيَانُهُ شَرِبْتُمُوهُ، حَتَّى إِنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ أَوْ إِنَّ أَحَدَهُمْ لَيَضْرِبُ ابْنَ عَمِّهِ بِالسَّيْفِ، قَالَ: وَفِي الْقَوْمِ رَجُلٌ أَصَابَتْهُ جِرَاحَةٌ كَذَلِكَ، قَالَ: وَكُنْتُ أَخْبَأُهَا حَيَاءً مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: فَفِيمَ نَشْرَبُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: فِي أَسْقِيَةِ الأَدَمِ الَّتِي يُلَاثُ عَلَى أَفْوَاهِهَا، قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ أَرْضَنَا كَثِيرَةُ الْجِرْذَانِ، وَلَا تَبْقَى بِهَا أَسْقِيَةُ الأَدَمِ، فَقَالَ نَبِيُّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَإِنْ أَكَلَتْهَا الْجِرْذَانُ، وَإِنْ أَكَلَتْهَا الْجِرْذَانُ، وَإِنْ أَكَلَتْهَا الْجِرْذَانُ، قَالَ: وَقَالَ نَبِيُّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِأَشَجِّ عَبْدِ الْقَيْسِ: إِنَّ فِيكَ لَخَصْلَتَيْنِ يُحِبُّهُمَا اللَّهُ، الْحِلْمُ وَالأَنَاةُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (18) عن يحيى بن أيوب، حدثنا ابنُ عليّة، حدّثنا سعيد بن أبي عروبة، عن قتادة، قال: حدّثنا من لقي الوفدَ الذين قدموا على رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم من عبدالقيس. قال سعيد (ابن أبي عروبة): وذكر قتادة أبا نضرة، عن أبي سعيد في حديثه هذا: أنّ ناساً من عبدالقيس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (18).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: Some people from ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, we are a tribe from Rabīʿah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Muḍar. We are unable to reach you except during the sacred months. Command us with something that we may command those whom we have left behind and through which we may enter Paradise if we adhere to it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I command you with four matters and prohibit you from four: worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, give zakāh, fast Ramaḍān, and give one-fifth of the spoils of war. And I prohibit you from four vessels: al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, al-muzaffat, and al-naqīr.” They asked: “O Prophet of Allah, what do you know about al-naqīr?” He replied: “Yes. It is a tree trunk that you hollow out. You place qutayʿāʾ into it” — Saʿīd said: or he said dates — “then pour water into it. When its bubbling subsides, you drink it, until one of you — or one of them — may strike his cousin with a sword.” The narrator said: Among the people was a man who had suffered a wound in precisely this way. He said: I used to conceal it out of shyness before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I asked: “Then from what should we drink, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “From leather waterskins whose mouths are tied.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, our land contains many rats, and leather waterskins do not survive there.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ replied: “Even if the rats eat them; even if the rats eat them; even if the rats eat them.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ also said to al-Ashajj of ʿAbd al-Qays: “Indeed, you possess two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Ashajj of ʿAbd al-Qays was named al-Mundhir ibn ʿĀʾidh, as al-Tirmidhī stated. He was al-Mundhir ibn ʿĀʾidh ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Ḥārith al-ʿAbdī al-ʿAṣrī, a Companion who settled in Baṣrah and died there."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (18)."},{"num":60,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ النُّعْمَانُ بْنُ قَوْقَلٍ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! أَرَأَيْتَ إِذَا صَلَّيْتُ الْمَكْتُوبَةَ، وَحَرَّمْتُ الْحَرَامَ، وَأَحْلَلْتُ الْحَلَالَ، أَأَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّة؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نَعَمْ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: صَلَّيْتُ الصَّلَوَاتِ الْمَكْتُوبَاتِ، وَصُمْتُ رَمَضَانَ، وَأَحْلَلْتُ الْحَلَالَ، وَحَرَّمْتُ الْحَرَامَ، وَلَمْ أَزِدْ عَلَى ذَلِكَ شَيْئًا، أَأَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ لَا أَزِيدُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ شَيْئًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (15) من طرق عن جابر، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (15).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: Al-Nuʿmān ibn Qawqal came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, if I perform the prescribed prayers, regard the unlawful as forbidden, and regard the lawful as lawful, will I enter Paradise?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yes.” In another narration:","“If I perform the prescribed prayers, fast Ramaḍān, regard the lawful as lawful, regard the unlawful as forbidden, and add nothing beyond that, will I enter Paradise?” He replied: “Yes.” The man said: “By Allah, I will add nothing to that.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (15)."},{"num":61,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ قَالَ: كُنْتُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سَفَرٍ فَأَصْبَحْتُ يَوْمًا قَرِيبًا مِنْهُ وَنَحْنُ نَسِيرُ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَخْبِرْنِي بِعَمَلٍ يُدْخِلُنِي الْجَنَّةَ، وَيُبَاعِدُنِي عَنِ النَّارِ، قَالَ: لَقَدْ سَأَلْتَنِي عَنْ عَظِيمٍ وَإِنَّهُ لَيَسِيرٌ عَلَى مَنْ يَسَّرَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ، تَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكْ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِي الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومُ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجُّ الْبَيْتَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أَدُلُّكَ عَلَى أَبْوَابِ الْخَيْرِ: الصَّوْمُ جُنَّةٌ، وَالصَّدَقَةُ تُطْفِئُ الْخَطِيئَةَ كَمَا يُطْفِئُ الْمَاءُ النَّارَ، وَصَلَاةُ الرَّجُلِ مِنْ جَوْفِ اللَّيْلِ، قَالَ ثُمَّ تَلَا :﴿تَتَجَافَى جُنُوبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ﴾ حَتَّى بَلَغَ ﴿يَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [سورة السجدة:16، 17]، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أُخْبِرُكَ بِرَأْسِ الْأَمْرِ كُلِّهِ وَعَمُودِهِ وَذِرْوَةِ سَنَامِهِ؟ قُلْتُ: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: رَأْسُ الْأَمْرِ الْإِسْلَامُ، وَعَمُودُهُ الصَّلَاةُ، وَذِرْوَةُ سَنَامِهِ الْجِهَادُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أُخْبِرُكَ بِمَلَاكِ ذَلِكَ كُلِّهِ؟ قُلْتُ: بَلَى يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، فَأَخَذَ بِلِسَانِهِ قَالَ: كُفَّ عَلَيْكَ هَذَا، فَقُلْتُ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ وَإِنَّا لَمُؤَاخَذُونَ بِمَا نَتَكَلَّمُ بِهِ؟ فَقَالَ: ثَكِلَتْكَ أُمُّكَ يَا مُعَاذُ وَهَلْ يَكُبُّ النَّاسَ فِي النَّارِ عَلَى وُجُوهِهِمْ أَوْ عَلَى مَنَاخِرِهِمْ إِلَّا حَصَائِدُ أَلْسِنَتِهِمْ؟."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2616) واللّفظ له، وابن ماجه (3973) كلاهما عن محمد بن أبي عمر العدنيّ، حدثنا عبدالله بن معاذ الصنعانيّ، عن معمر، عن عاصم ابن أبي النُّجود، عن أبي وائل، عن معاذ بن جبل، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2616) and Ibn Mājah (3973).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ. One morning, while we were journeying, I was close to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.” He replied: “You have asked me about a tremendous matter, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prayer; give zakāh; fast Ramaḍān; and perform pilgrimage to the House.” Then he said: “Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and there is the prayer of a man in the depths of the night.” He then recited: “Their sides forsake their beds…” until he reached: “…what they used to do.” [Sūrat al-Sajdah 32:16–17] Then he said: “Shall I not tell you of the head of the entire matter, its pillar, and the peak of its summit?” I replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The head of the matter is Islam, its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its summit is jihād.” Then he said: “Shall I not tell you what controls all of that?” I replied: “Yes, O Prophet of Allah.” He took hold of his tongue and said: “Restrain this.” I asked: “O Prophet of Allah, will we really be held accountable for what we say?” He replied: “May your mother lose you, O Muʿādh! Is there anything that casts people into the Fire upon their faces — or upon their noses — other than the harvests of their tongues?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2616)، وابن ماجه (3973)."},{"num":62,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ حَتَّى تُؤْمِنُوا، وَلَا تُؤْمِنُوا حَتَّى تَحَابُّوا أَوَلَا أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَى شَيْءٍ إِذَا فَعَلْتُمُوهُ تَحَابَبْتُمْ؟ أَفْشُوا السَّلَامَ بَيْنَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (54) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا أبو معاوية، ووكيع، عن الأعمش، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (54).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, will cause you to love one another? Spread the greeting of peace among yourselves.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (54)."},{"num":63,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِنِّي إِذَا رَأَيْتُكَ طَابَتْ نَفْسِي وَقَرَّتْ عَيْنِي، فَأَنْبِئْنِي عَنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، فَقَالَ: كُلُّ شَيْءٍ خُلِقَ مِنْ مَاءٍ. قَالَ: قُلْتُ: أَنْبِئْنِي عَنْ أَمْرٍ إِذَا أَخَذْتُ بِهِ دَخَلْتُ الْجَنَّةَ، قَالَ: أَفْشِ السَّلامَ، وَأَطْعِمِ الطَّعَامَ، وَصِلِ الأَرْحَامَ، وَقُمْ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّاسُ نِيَامٌ، ثُمَّ ادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَ بِسَلامٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (7932)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (508)، والحاكم (7371) كلهم من طريق همام بن يحيى، عن قتادة، عن أبي ميمون، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Aḥmad (7932), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (508) and al-Ḥākim (7278).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, whenever I see you my soul feels content and my eyes are comforted. Tell me about all things.” He replied: “Everything was created from water.” I said: “Tell me of something that, if I adhere to it, will cause me to enter Paradise.” He replied: “Spread the greeting of peace, feed people, maintain ties of kinship, and stand in prayer at night while the people are asleep; then enter Paradise in peace.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[2680,8194,12750,13660,13725,14216],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (7932)، وصححه ابن حبان (508)، والحاكم (7371)."},{"num":64,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اعْبُدُوا الرَّحْمَنَ، وَأَفْشُوا السَّلَامَ، وَأَطْعِمُوا الطَّعَامَ تَدْخُلُونَ الْجِنَانَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذيّ (1855) من طريق أبي الأحوص،، وابن ماجه (3694) من طريق محمد بن فضيل،، والإمام أحمد (6587) من طريقين أبي عوانة وعبدالرزاق،، وابن حبان في صحيحه (489، 507) من طريق جرير بن عبدالحميد،، وعبدبن حميد في المنتخب (355) من طريق زائدة بن قدامة، كلّهم عن عطاء ابن السّائب، عن أبيه، عن عبدالله بن عمرو، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1855), Ibn Mājah (3694), and Aḥmad (6587).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Worship the Most Merciful, spread the greeting of peace, and feed people; you will enter the Gardens of Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhī said:","“Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1855)، وابن ماجه (3694)، وأحمد (6587)."},{"num":65,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ سَلَامٍ قَالَ: لَمَّا قَدِمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْمَدِينَةَ انْجَفَلَ النَّاسُ إِلَيْهِ وَقِيلَ: قَدِمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَجِئْتُ فِي النَّاسِ لِأَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهِ فَلَمَّا اسْتَبَنْتُ وَجْهَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَرَفْتُ أَنَّ وَجْهَهُ لَيْسَ بِوَجْهِ كَذَّابٍ، وَكَانَ أَوَّلُ شَيْءٍ تَكَلَّمَ بِهِ أَنْ قَالَ: أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ أَفْشُوا السَّلَامَ، وَأَطْعِمُوا الطَّعَامَ، وَصَلُّوا وَالنَّاسُ نِيَامٌ، تَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ بِسَلَامٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذيّ (2485)، وابن ماجه (1334)، وصحّحه الحاكم (4306، 7370) كلهم من طريق عوف بن أبي جميلة، حدثنا زرارة ابن أبي أوفى، عن عبدالله بن سلام، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2485), who authenticated it, Ibn Mājah (1334), and al-Ḥākim (4283).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived — meaning in Madinah — the people rushed toward him, and it was announced: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has arrived!” I went among the people to look at him. When I looked carefully at the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I knew that his face was not the face of a liar. The first words I heard him say were: “O people, spread the greeting of peace, feed people, and pray while the people are asleep; you will enter Paradise in peace.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14219],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2485) وصححه، وابن ماجه (1334)، والحاكم (4306)."},{"num":66,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ هَانِئِ بْنِ يَزِيدَ أَنَّهُ لَمَّا وَفَدَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَ قَوْمِهِ، فَسَمِعَهُمُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُمْ يُكَنُّونَهُ بِأَبِي الْحَكَمِ، فَدَعَاهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْحَكَمُ، وَإِلَيْهِ الْحُكْمُ، فَلِمَ تَكَنَّيْتَ بِأَبِي الْحَكَمِ؟ قَالَ: لَا، وَلَكِنَّ قَوْمِي إِذَا اخْتَلَفُوا فِي شَيْءٍ أَتَوْنِي فَحَكَمْتُ بَيْنَهُمْ، فَرَضِيَ كِلاَ الْفَرِيقَيْنِ، قَالَ: مَا أَحْسَنَ هَذَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَا لَكَ مِنَ الْوَلَدِ؟ قُلْتُ: لِي شُرَيْحٌ، وَعَبْدُ اللهِ، وَمُسْلِمٌ، بَنُو هَانِئٍ، قَالَ: فَمَنْ أَكْبَرُهُمْ؟ قُلْتُ: شُرَيْحٌ، قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ أَبُو شُرَيْحٍ، وَدَعَا لَهُ وَوَلَدِهِ. وَسَمِعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَوْمًا يُسَمُّونَ رَجُلا مِنْهُمْ: عَبْدَ الْحَجَرِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا اسْمُكَ؟، قَالَ: عَبْدُ الْحَجَرِ، قَالَ: لَا، أَنْتَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ. قَالَ شُرَيْحٌ: وَإِنَّ هَانِئًا لَمَّا حَضَرَ رُجُوعُهُ إِلَى بِلادِهِ أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: أَخْبِرْنِي بِأَيِّ شَيْءٍ يُوجِبُ لِيَ الْجَنَّةَ؟ قَالَ: عَلَيْكَ بِحُسْنِ الْكَلامِ، وَبَذْلِ الطَّعَامِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب المفرد (811)، وابن حبان (504)، و أبو داود (4955)، وابن حبان (490)، والحاكم (62)، والطبرانيّ في الكبير (470) كلّهم من طرق عن يزيد بن المقدام بن شريح، عن أبيه المقدام، عن أبيه شريح، عن أبيه هانئ بن يزيد، قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad (811), Ibn Ḥibbān (504), and Abū Dāwūd (4955).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hāniʾ ibn Yazīd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: When he came to the Prophet ﷺ as part of a delegation from his people, the Prophet ﷺ heard them calling him by the kunyah Abū al-Ḥakam. The Prophet ﷺ called him and said: “Indeed, Allah is al-Ḥakam — the Judge — and judgment belongs to Him. Why, then, are you called Abū al-Ḥakam?” He replied: “When my people disagree concerning something, they come to me and I judge between them, and both parties are satisfied.” He said: “How excellent that is!” Then he asked: “What children do you have?” I replied: “I have Shurayḥ, ʿAbdullāh, and Muslim, the sons of Hāniʾ.” He asked: “Which of them is the eldest?” I replied: “Shurayḥ.” He said: “Then you are Abū Shurayḥ.” He supplicated for him and his children. The Prophet ﷺ also heard some people calling one of their men ʿAbd al-Ḥajar — “servant of the stone.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “ʿAbd al-Ḥajar.” He said: “No. You are ʿAbdullāh.” Shurayḥ said: When Hāniʾ was preparing to return to his homeland, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “Tell me what will make Paradise obligatory for me.” He replied: “Adhere to good speech and generously provide food.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (811)، وابن حبان (504)، وأبو داود (4955)."},{"num":67,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ كَانَ آخِرُ كَلَامِهِ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3116)، وأحمد (22127)، والحاكم (1303) كلهم من حديث عبد الحميد بن جعفر، حدثني صالح بن أبي عَريب، عن كثير بن مرة الحضرمي، عن معاذ بن جبل فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بيان الأمور الجامعة التي يدخل بها المسلم الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3116), Aḥmad (22127), and al-Ḥākim (1299).","chapter_en":"Comprehensive Deeds Through Which a Muslim Enters Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Jabal may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever’s last words are, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3501],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3116)، وأحمد (22127)، والحاكم (1303)."},{"num":68,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَعْطَى رَهْطًا وَسَعْدٌ جَالِسٌ فَتَرَكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَجُلًا هُوَ أَعْجَبُهُمْ إِلَيَّ فَقُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَا لَكَ عَنْ فُلَانٍ؟ فَوَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لَأَرَاهُ مُؤْمِنًا. فَقَالَ: أَوْ مُسْلِمًا فَسَكَتُّ قَلِيلًا ثُمَّ غَلَبَنِي مَا أَعْلَمُ مِنْهُ فَعُدْتُ لِمَقَالَتِي فَقُلْتُ: مَا لَكَ عَنْ فُلَانٍ فَوَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لَأَرَاهُ مُؤْمِنًا فَقَالَ: أَوْ مُسْلِمًا ثُمَّ غَلَبَنِي مَا أَعْلَمُ مِنْهُ فَعُدْتُ لِمَقَالَتِي وَعَادَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا سَعْدُ إِنِّي لَأُعْطِي الرَّجُلَ وَغَيْرُهُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِنْهُ خَشْيَةَ أَنْ يَكُبَّهُ اللَّهُ فِي النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (27)، ومسلم في الإيمان (150) كلاهما من حديث الزهري، عن عامر بن سعد بن أبي وقاص، عن سعد، فذكر مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إذا لم يكن الإسلام على الحقيقة لا ينفع في الآخرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (27) and Muslim (150).","chapter_en":"If Islam Is Not Genuine, It Will Not Benefit in the Hereafter","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave gifts to a group of people while Saʿd was sitting with him, but he left out a man who was more impressive to me than the others. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, why have you left so-and-so? By Allah, I consider him a believer.” He replied: “Or a Muslim.” I remained silent for a short while, but what I knew about the man compelled me to speak again, so I said: “Why have you left so-and-so? By Allah, I consider him a believer.” He replied: “Or a Muslim.” Again, what I knew of him compelled me to repeat what I had said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated his response. Then he said: “O Saʿd, I may give something to a man even though another person is more beloved to me than he is, fearing that Allah might cast him into the Fire.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿قَالَتِ الأَعْرَابُ آمَنَّا قُلْ لَمْ تُؤْمِنُوا وَلَكِنْ قُولُوا أَسْلَمْنَا﴾","[الحجرات: ١٤]","فإذا كان على الحقيقة، فهو على قوله جل ذكره:","﴿إِنَّ الدِّينَ عِنْدَ اللهِ الإِسْلَامُ﴾","[آل عمران: ١٩]"],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“The Bedouins say, ‘We believe.’ Say: ‘You have not yet believed; rather say, “We have submitted.”’”","[Sūrat al-Ḥujurāt 49:14]","But when Islam is genuine in reality, then it accords with His statement, Glorified is His remembrance:","“Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.”","[Āl ʿImrān 3:19]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13372],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (27)، ومسلم (150)."},{"num":69,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَادَةَ بْنِ الصَّامِتِ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ شَهِدَ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، وَأَنَّ عِيسَى عَبْدُ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولُهُ وَكَلِمَتُهُ أَلْقَاهَا إِلَى مَرْيَمَ وَرُوحٌ مِنْهُ وَالْجَنَّةُ حَقٌّ وَالنَّارُ حَقٌّ أَدْخَلَهُ اللَّهُ الْجَنَّةَ عَلَى مَا كَانَ مِنَ الْعَمَلِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في أحاديث الأنبياء (3435) عن صدقة بن الفضل، حدثنا الوليد، عن الأوزاعي، قال: حدثني عمير بن هانئ، قال: حدثني جنادة بن أبي أمية، عن عبادة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3435) and Muslim (28).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner; that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger; that Jesus is the servant of Allah and His Messenger, His word which He cast to Mary, and a spirit from Him; and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true — Allah will admit him into Paradise according to whatever deeds he had performed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[702],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3435)، ومسلم (28)."},{"num":70,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ قَالَ: بَيْنَا أَنَا رَدِيفُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْسَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهُ إِلَّا أَخِرَةُ الرَّحْلِ فَقَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ قُلْتُ: لَبَّيْكَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ، ثُمَّ سَارَ سَاعَةً ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ قُلْتُ: لَبَّيْكَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ، ثُمَّ سَارَ سَاعَةً ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ قُلْتُ: لَبَّيْكَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ قَالَ: هَلْ تَدْرِي مَا حَقُّ اللَّهِ عَلَى عِبَادِهِ؟ قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: حَقُّ اللَّهِ عَلَى عِبَادِهِ أَنْ يَعْبُدُوهُ وَلَا يُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئًا ثُمَّ سَارَ سَاعَةً ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ بْنَ جَبَلٍ قُلْتُ: لَبَّيْكَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ تَدْرِي مَا حَقُّ الْعِبَادِ عَلَى اللَّهِ إِذَا فَعَلُوهُ؟ قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: حَقُّ الْعِبَادِ عَلَى اللَّهِ أَنْ لَا يُعَذِّبَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (5967)، وفي الرقاق bukhari(6500)، ومسلم في الإيمان (30) كلاهما عن هدّاب بن خالد الأزديّ، حدثنا همام، حدثنا قتادة، حدثنا أنس بن مالك، عن معاذ بن جبل، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5967, 6500) and Muslim (30).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, with nothing between me and him except the rear portion of the saddle. He said: “O Muʿādh.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He traveled for a while, then said: “O Muʿādh.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He traveled for a while longer, then said: “O Muʿādh.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He asked: “Do you know what Allah’s right upon His servants is?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Allah’s right upon His servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.” He traveled for a while, then said: “O Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He asked: “Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is if they do that?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The right of the servants upon Allah is that He will not punish them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5967، 6500)، ومسلم (30)."},{"num":71,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ قَالَ: كُنْتُ رِدْفَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى حِمَارٍ يُقَالُ لَهُ: عُفَيْرٌ، فَقَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ هَلْ تَدْرِي حَقَّ اللَّهِ عَلَى عِبَادِهِ وَمَا حَقُّ الْعِبَادِ عَلَى اللَّهِ؟ قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: فَإِنَّ حَقَّ اللَّهِ عَلَى الْعِبَادِ أَنْ يَعْبُدُوهُ، وَلَا يُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَحَقَّ الْعِبَادِ عَلَى اللَّهِ أَنْ لَا يُعَذِّبَ مَنْ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَفَلَا أُبَشِّرُ بِهِ النَّاسَ؟ قَالَ: لَا تُبَشِّرْهُمْ فَيَتَّكِلُوا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الجهاد والسير (2856)، ومسلم في الإيمان (30،49) كلاهما من حديث أبي الأحوص سلاّم بن سُليم، عن أبي إسحاق، عن عمرو بن ميمون، عن معاذ بن جبل، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2856) and Muslim (30).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ upon a donkey called ʿUfayr. He said: “O Muʿādh, do you know the right of Allah upon His servants and the right of the servants upon Allah?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Allah’s right upon His servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. The right of the servants upon Allah is that He will not punish one who does not associate anything with Him.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, should I not give the people this glad tidings?” He replied: “Do not give them the glad tidings, lest they rely upon it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2856)، ومسلم (30)."},{"num":72,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَمُعاذٌ رَدِيفُهُ عَلَى الرَّحْلِ قَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ، قَالَ: لَبَّيْكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ، قَالَ: يَا مُعَاذُ، قَالَ: لَبَّيْكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَسَعْدَيْكَ ثَلَاثًا، قَالَ: مَا مِنْ أَحَدٍ يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صِدْقًا مِنْ قَلْبِهِ، إِلَّا حَرَّمَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّارِ، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَفَلَا أُخْبِرُ بِهِ النَّاسَ فَيَسْتَبْشِرُوا، قَالَ: إِذًا يَتَّكِلُوا، وَأَخْبَرَ بِهَا مُعَاذٌ عِنْدَ مَوْتِهِ تَأَثُّمًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في العلم (128)، ومسلم في الإيمان (32) كلاهما عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم، قال: حدثنا معاذ بن هشام، قال: حدثني أبي، عن قتادة، قال: حدثنا أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (128) and Muslim (32).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was riding with Muʿādh ibn Jabal behind him on the saddle. He said: “O Muʿādh!” Muʿādh replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He said again: “O Muʿādh!” He replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He said a third time: “O Muʿādh!” He replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and ready to obey you.” He said: “No servant testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger except that Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.” Muʿādh asked: “O Messenger of Allah, should I not inform the people so that they may rejoice?” He replied: “Then they would rely upon it.” Muʿādh therefore disclosed the ḥadīth near the time of his death out of fear of being sinful for withholding knowledge."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (128)، ومسلم (32)."},{"num":73,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ هِصَّانَ بْنِ الْكَاهِنِ قَالَ: جَلَسْتُ مَجْلِسًا فِيهِ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ سَمُرَةَ وَلا أَعْرِفُهُ، قَالَ حَدَّثَنَا مُعَاذِ بْنُ جَبَلٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا عَلَى الأَرْضِ نَفْسٌ تَمُوتُ لا تُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا تَشْهَدُ أَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْجِعُ ذَلِكَ إِلَى قَلْبٍ مُوقِنٍ إِلا غُفِرَ لَهَا، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: أَنْتَ سَمِعْتَ هَذَا مِنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ ؟ قَالَ: فَعَنَّفَنِي الْقَوْمُ، فَقَالَ: دَعُوهُ فَإِنَّهُ لَمْ يُسِئْ الْقَوْلَ، نَعَمْ أَنَا سَمِعْتُهُ مِنْ مُعَاذٍ، زَعَمَ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَهُ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22000)، والبزار في مسنده (2624)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (1138) وبن حبان (203) كلهم من حديث محمد بن أبي عدي، عن الحجّاج، يعني ابن أبي عثمان،، حدثني حميد بن هلال، حدثنا هِصَّان بن الكاهل، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (22000), al-Bazzār (2624), and al-Nasāʾī in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah (1138).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hiṣṣān ibn al-Kāhin reported: I sat in a gathering in which ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah was present, though I did not recognize him. He said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no soul upon the earth that dies without associating anything with Allah, testifying that I am the Messenger of Allah, with that testimony coming from a heart certain of it, except that it will be forgiven.” I asked him: “Did you yourself hear this from Muʿādh ibn Jabal?” The people rebuked me. He said: “Leave him. He has said nothing improper. Yes, I heard it from Muʿādh, who stated that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22000)، والبزار (2624)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (1138)."},{"num":74,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: يَخْرُجُ قَوْمٌ مِنَ النَّارِ بَعْدَ مَا مَسَّهُمْ مِنْهَا سَفْعٌ، فَيَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ، فَيُسَمِّيهِمْ أَهْلُ الْجَنَّةِ: الْجَهَنَّمِيِّينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الرّقاق (6559) عن هُدبة بن خالد، حدثنا همام، عن قتادة، حدثنا أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Riqāq (6559).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Some people will be brought out of the Fire after its scorching has touched them. They will then enter Paradise, and the people of Paradise will call them al-Jahannamiyyūn — those who had been in Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6559)."},{"num":75,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: يَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ أَرْبَعَةٌ، فَيُعْرَضُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ، فَيَلْتَفِتُ أَحَدُهُمْ، فَيَقُولُ: أَيْ رَبِّ إِذْ أَخْرَجْتَنِي مِنْهَا فَلَا تُعِدْنِي فِيهَا، فَيُنْجِيهِ اللَّهُ مِنْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (192) عن هدّاب بن خالد الأزديّ، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن أبي عمران وثابت، عن أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim in al-Īmān (192).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four people will be brought out of the Fire and presented before Allah. One of them will turn back toward it and say: ‘My Lord, now that You have brought me out of it, do not return me to it.’ So Allah will save him from it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[152,16189,16472],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (192)."},{"num":76,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عِتْبَانَ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: فَبَعَثْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَنِّي أُحِبُّ أَنْ تَأْتِيَنِي فَتُصَلِّيَ فِي مَنْزِلِي فَأَتَّخِذَهُ مُصَلًّى، قَالَ: فَأَتَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَمَنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ فَدَخَلَ وَهُوَ يُصَلِّي فِي مَنْزِلِي، وَأَصْحَابُهُ يَتَحَدَّثُونَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ أَسْنَدُوا عُظْمَ ذَلِكَ وَكِبْرَهُ إِلَى مَالِكِ بْنِ دُخْشُمٍ، قَالُوا: وَدُّوا أَنَّهُ دَعَا عَلَيْهِ فَهَلَكَ، وَوَدُّوا أَنَّهُ أَصَابَهُ شَرٌّ، فَقَضَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الصَّلَاةَ، وَقَالَ: أَلَيْسَ يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ؟ قَالُوا: إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ وَمَا هُوَ فِي قَلْبِهِ، قَالَ: لَا يَشْهَدُ أَحَدٌ، أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، فَيَدْخُلَ النَّارَ أَوْ تَطْعَمَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (33) عن شيبان بن فرّوخ، حدّثنا سليمان، يعني ابن المغيرة، ، قال: حدثنا ثابت، عن أنس بن مالك، قال: حدثني محمود ابن الرّبيع، عن عتبان بن مالك، قال: قدمت المدينة فلقيت عتبان، فقلت: حديث بلغني عنك؟ قال: أصابني في بصري بعض الشيء فبعثت. فذكر الحديث. قال أنس: فأعجبني هذا الحديث، فقلت لابني: اكتبه، فكتبه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (33) and al-Bukhārī (425).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿItbān ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I sent a message to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “I would like you to come to me and pray in my house so that I may take that place as a designated prayer area.” The Prophet ﷺ came, accompanied by whichever of his Companions Allah willed. He entered and prayed in my house while his Companions spoke among themselves. They eventually attributed the seriousness of the matter to Mālik ibn al-Dukhshum. They expressed the wish that the Prophet ﷺ would supplicate against him so that he would perish or that some evil would befall him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed the prayer, he said: “Does he not testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” They replied: “He says that, but it is not in his heart.” He said: “No one testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah and then enters the Fire, or is consumed by it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (33)، والبخاري (425)."},{"num":77,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ (فَذَكَرَهُ فِي حَدِيثِ طَوِيلٍ)، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: حَتَّى إِذَا فَرَغَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْقَضَاءِ بَيْنَ عِبَادِهِ، وَأَرَادَ أَنْ يُخْرِجَ مِنَ النَّارِ مَنْ أَرَادَ أَنْ يُخْرِجَ مِمَّنْ كَانَ يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، أَمَرَ الْمَلَائِكَةَ أَنْ يُخْرِجُوهُمْ فَيَعْرِفُونَهُمْ بِعَلَامَةِ آثَارِ السُّجُودِ، وَحَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّارِ أَنْ تَأْكُلَ مِنَ ابْنِ آدَمَ أَثَرَ السُّجُودِ، فَيُخْرِجُونَهُمْ قَدِ امْتُحِشُوا فَيُصَبُّ عَلَيْهِمْ مَاءٌ يُقَالُ لَهُ: مَاءُ الْحَيَاةِ فَيَنْبُتُونَ نَبَاتَ الْحِبَّةِ فِي حَمِيلِ السَّيْلِ... الْحَدِيثَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التوحيد (7437)، ومسلم في الإيمان (182) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد، عن ابن شهاب، عن عطاء بن يزيد الليثيّ، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث في سياق طويل.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7437) and Muslim (182).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah has completed judgment between His servants and wills to bring out of the Fire whomever He wills from among those who used to testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, He will command the angels to bring them out. The angels will recognize them by the marks of prostration, for Allah has forbidden the Fire from consuming the marks of prostration upon the children of Ādam. They will be brought out after having been severely burned. Water known as the Water of Life will then be poured over them, and they will grow from it as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7437)، ومسلم (182)."},{"num":78,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: كُنَّا قُعُودًا حَوْلَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، مَعَنَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ فِي نَفَرٍ، فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ بَيْنِ أَظْهُرِنَا، فَأَبْطَأَ عَلَيْنَا وَخَشِينَا أَنْ يُقْتَطَعَ دُونَنَا، وَفَزِعْنَا فَقُمْنَا، فَكُنْتُ أَوَّلَ مَنْ فَزِعَ، فَخَرَجْتُ أَبْتَغِي رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، حَتَّى أَتَيْتُ حَائِطًا لِلأَنْصَار لِبَنِي النَّجَّارِ، فَدُرْتُ بِهِ، هَلْ أَجِدُ لَهُ بَابًا؟ فَلَمْ أَجِدْ، فَإِذَا رَبِيعٌ، يَدْخُلُ فِي جَوْفِ حَائِطٍ مِنْ بِئْرٍ خَارِجَةَ، وَالرَّبِيعُ الْجَدْوَلُ، فَاحْتَفَزْتُ كَمَا يَحْتَفِزُ الثَّعْلَبُ، فَدَخَلْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ؟ فَقُلْتُ: نَعَمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: مَا شَأْنُكَ؟ قُلْتُ: كُنْتَ بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِنَا، فَقُمْتَ فَأَبْطَأْتَ عَلَيْنَا، فَخَشِينَا أَنْ تُقْتَطَعَ دُونَنَا، فَفَزِعْنَا، فَكُنْتُ أَوَّلَ مِنْ فَزِعَ، فَأَتَيْتُ هَذَا الْحَائِطَ فَاحْتَفَزْتُ كَمَا يَحْتَفِزُ الثَّعْلَبُ، وَهَؤُلَاءِ النَّاسُ وَرَائِي، فَقَالَ: يَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ، وَأَعْطَانِي نَعْلَيْهِ، قَالَ: اذْهَبْ بِنَعْلَيَّ هَاتَيْنِ، فَمَنْ لَقِيتَ مِنْ وَرَاءِ هَذَا الْحَائِطِ، يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، مُسْتَيْقِنًا بِهَا قَلْبُهُ، فَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ لَقِيتُ عُمَرُ، فَقَالَ: مَا هَاتَانِ النَّعْلَانِ يَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ؟ فَقُلْتُ: هَاتَانِ نَعْلَا رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، بَعَثَنِي بِهِمَا مَنْ لَقِيتُ، يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، مُسْتَيْقِنًا بِهَا قَلْبُهُ بَشَّرْتُهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، فَضَرَبَ عُمَرُ بِيَدِهِ بَيْنَ ثَدْيَيَّ، فَخَرَرْتُ لِاسْتِي، فَقَالَ: ارْجِعْ يَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ، فَرَجَعْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَجْهَشْتُ بُكَاءً، وَرَكِبَنِي عُمَرُ، فَإِذَا هُوَ عَلَى أَثَرِي، فَقَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا لَكَ يَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ؟ قُلْتُ: لَقِيتُ عُمَرَ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِالَّذِي بَعَثْتَنِي بِهِ، فَضَرَبَ بَيْنَ ثَدْيَيَّ ضَرْبَةً خَرَرْتُ لِاسْتِي، قَالَ: ارْجِعْ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ: يَا عُمَرُ مَا حَمَلَكَ عَلَى مَا فَعَلْتَ؟ قَال: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، بِأَبِي أَنْتَ وَأُمِّي، أَبَعَثْتَ أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ بِنَعْلَيْكَ، مَنْ لَقِيَ يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، مُسْتَيْقِنًا بِهَا قَلْبُهُ بَشَّرَهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَلَا تَفْعَلْ، فَإِنِّي أَخْشَى أَنْ يَتَّكِلَ النَّاسُ عَلَيْهَا فَخَلِّهِمْ يَعْمَلُون، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَخَلِّهِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (31) عن زهير بن حرب، حدثنا عمر بن يونس الحنفي، حدثنا عكرمة بن عمّار، قال: حدثني أبو كثير، قال: حدثني أبو هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (31).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and a number of others among us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose and left us. He was absent longer than expected, and we feared that something might happen to him before we could reach him. We became alarmed and stood up. I was the first to become alarmed. I went out searching for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until I came to an orchard belonging to the Anṣār of Banū al-Najjār. I walked around it looking for a gate but found none. Then I saw a small stream entering the orchard from an outside well. I squeezed through it the way a fox squeezes through a narrow opening and came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Abū Hurayrah?” I replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He asked: “What has brought you here?” I said: “You were among us, then you stood up and were away for a long time. We feared something might happen to you before we could reach you, so we became alarmed. I was the first to become alarmed. I came to this orchard and squeezed through like a fox, and the rest of the people are behind me.” He said: “O Abū Hurayrah.” He gave me his two sandals and said: “Take these two sandals of mine. Whoever you meet beyond this orchard who testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah with a heart certain of it, give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” The first person I met was ʿUmar. He asked: “What are these sandals, O Abū Hurayrah?” I replied: “These are the sandals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sent me with them and instructed me that whoever I meet who testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah with a heart certain of it, I should give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” ʿUmar struck me upon the chest with his hand, and I fell backward onto my backside. He said: “Go back, O Abū Hurayrah.” I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and burst into tears. ʿUmar followed close behind me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What is wrong with you, O Abū Hurayrah?” I replied: “I met ʿUmar and informed him of what you had sent me to do. He struck me on the chest so that I fell backward, and he told me to return.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “O ʿUmar, what caused you to do that?” He replied: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Did you send Abū Hurayrah with your two sandals and instruct him to give the glad tidings of Paradise to whoever he met who testified that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah with certainty in his heart?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUmar said: “Then do not do so, for I fear that the people will rely upon it. Leave them to continue performing deeds.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then leave them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (31)."},{"num":79,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي مَسِيرٍ قَالَ: فَنَفِدَتْ أَزْوَادُ الْقَوْمِ، قَالَ: حَتَّى هَمَّ بِنَحْرِ بَعْضِ حَمَائِلِهِمْ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَوْ جَمَعْتَ مَا بَقِيَ مِنْ أَزْوَادِ الْقَوْمِ، فَدَعَوْتَ اللَّهَ عَلَيْهَا، قَالَ: فَفَعَلَ، قَالَ: فَجَاءَ ذُو الْبُرِّ بِبُرِّهِ، وَذُو التَّمْرِ بِتَمْرِهِ، قَالَ: وَقَالَ مُجَاهِدٌ: وَذُو النَّوَاةِ بِنَوَاهُ، قُلْتُ: وَمَا كَانُوا يَصْنَعُونَ بِالنَّوَى؟ قَالَ: كَانُوا يَمُصُّونَهُ وَيَشْرَبُونَ عَلَيْهِ الْمَاءَ، قَالَ: فَدَعَا عَلَيْهَا حَتَّى مَلَأَ الْقَوْمُ أَزْوِدَتَهُمْ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ عِنْدَ ذَلِكَ: أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ لَا يَلْقَى اللَّهَ بِهِمَا عَبْدٌ غَيْرَ شَاكٍّ فِيهِمَا إِلَّا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: لَمَّا كَانَ غَزْوَةُ تَبُوكَ، أَصَابَ النَّاسَ مَجَاعَةٌ، قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَوْ أَذِنْتَ لَنَا، فَنَحَرْنَا نَوَاضِحَنَا، فَأَكَلْنَا وَادَّهَنَّا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: افْعَلُوا، قَالَ: فَجَاءَ عُمَرُ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنْ فَعَلْتَ قَلَّ الظَّهْرُ، وَلَكِنِ ادْعُهُمْ بِفَضْلِ أَزْوَادِهِمْ، ثُمَّ ادْعُ اللَّهَ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا بِالْبَرَكَةِ، لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ أَنْ يَجْعَلَ فِي ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَدَعَا بِنِطَعٍ فَبَسَطَهُ، ثُمَّ دَعَا بِفَضْلِ أَزْوَادِهِمْ، قَالَ: فَجَعَلَ الرَّجُلُ يَجِيءُ بِكَفِّ ذُرَةٍ، قَالَ: وَيَجِيءُ الآخَرُ بِكَفِّ تَمْرٍ، قَالَ: وَيَجِيءُ الآخَرُ بِكَسْرَةٍ، حَتَّى اجْتَمَعَ عَلَى النِّطَعِ مِنْ ذَلِكَ شَيْءٌ يَسِيرٌ، قَالَ: فَدَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْبَرَكَةِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: خُذُوا فِي أَوْعِيَتِكُمْ، قَالَ: فَأَخَذُوا فِي أَوْعِيَتِهِمْ، حَتَّى مَا تَرَكُوا فِي الْعَسْكَرِ وِعَاءً إِلَّا مَلَئُوهُ، قَالَ: فَأَكَلُوا حَتَّى شَبِعُوا، وَفَضِلَتْ فَضْلَةٌ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، لَا يَلْقَى اللَّهَ بِهِمَا عَبْدٌ غَيْرَ شَاكٍّ، فَيُحْجَبَ عَنِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (27) عن أبي بكر بن النّضر بن أبي النّضر، قال: حدثني أبو النضر هاشم بن القاسم، حدثنا عبيد الله الأشجعيّ، عن مالك بن مِغْول، عن طلحة بن مصرف، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (27).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: We were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ when the people’s provisions ran out, until they were on the verge of slaughtering some of their riding animals. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, why do you not gather whatever remains of the people’s provisions and supplicate to Allah over them?” The Prophet ﷺ did so. Whoever had wheat brought his wheat, and whoever had dates brought his dates. Mujāhid added: “And whoever had date stones brought his date stones.” I asked: “What did they do with the date stones?” He replied: “They would suck them and drink water afterward.” The Prophet ﷺ supplicated over the food until the people filled their provision bags. At that point he said: “I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant meets Allah with these two testimonies, without doubting them, except that he will enter Paradise.”","In another narration: During the expedition of Tabūk, the people were afflicted by severe hunger. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, if you permit us, we could slaughter our water-carrying camels, eat their meat, and use their fat.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do so.” ʿUmar then came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, if you do that, the number of riding animals will become too few. Instead, ask them to bring whatever remains of their provisions, then supplicate to Allah for blessing upon it. Perhaps Allah will place blessing therein.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Yes.” He called for a leather mat and spread it out, then asked the people to bring the remainder of their provisions. One man came with a handful of grain, another came with a handful of dates, and another came with a piece of bread, until a small quantity had accumulated upon the mat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for blessing over it and then said: “Take it into your containers.” They filled their containers until there was no vessel in the entire army camp that they had not filled. They ate until they were satisfied, and some food still remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant meets Allah with these two testimonies, without doubting them, and is then barred from Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (27)."},{"num":80,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنِّي لَأَعْلَمُ آخِرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ خُرُوجًا مِنْهَا، وَآخِرَ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ دُخُولًا، رَجُلٌ يَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ كَبْوًا، فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ: اذْهَبْ فَادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَ، فَيَأْتِيهَا فَيُخَيَّلُ إِلَيْهِ أَنَّهَا مَلْأَى، فَيَرْجِعُ، فَيَقُولُ: يَا رَبِّ، وَجَدْتُهَا مَلْأَى، فَيَقُولُ: اذْهَبْ فَادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَ، فَيَأْتِيهَا، فَيُخَيَّلُ إِلَيْهِ أَنَّهَا مَلْأَى، فَيَرْجِعُ، فَيَقُولُ: يَا رَبِّ، وَجَدْتُهَا مَلْأَى، فَيَقُولُ: اذْهَبْ فَادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَ فَإِنَّ لَكَ مِثْلَ الدُّنْيَا وَعَشَرَةَ أَمْثَالِهَا أَوْ إِنَّ لَكَ مِثْلَ عَشَرَةِ أَمْثَالِ الدُّنْيَا، فَيَقُولُ: تَسْخَرُ مِنِّي أَوْ تَضْحَكُ مِنِّي وَأَنْتَ الْمَلِكُ، فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ضَحِكَ حَتَّى بَدَتْ نَوَاجِذُهُ، وَكَانَ يَقُولُ: ذَاكَ أَدْنَى أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ مَنْزِلَةً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الرقاق (6571)، ومسلم في الإيمان (186) كلاهما عن عثمان بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا جرير، عن منصور، عن إبراهيم، عن عبيدة، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6571) and Muslim (186).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I certainly know the last person to come out of the Fire and the last person to enter Paradise. It will be a man who comes crawling out of the Fire. Allah will say to him: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will go to it, but it will appear to him as though it is full. He will return and say: ‘My Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will go to it, but again it will appear to him as though it is full. He will return and say: ‘My Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise, for you will have the equivalent of the entire world and ten times as much’ — or: ‘You will have ten times the equivalent of the world.’ The man will say: ‘Are You mocking me — or laughing at me — while You are the King?’” I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molar teeth became visible. It used to be said: “That man will be the lowest in rank among the people of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6571)، ومسلم (186)."},{"num":81,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى الْأَشْعَرِيِّ قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَعِي نَفَرٌ مِنْ قَوْمِي، فَقَالَ: أَبْشِرُوا، وَبَشِّرُوا مَنْ وَرَاءَكُمْ، أَنَّهُ مَنْ شَهِدَ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ صَادِقًا بِهَا، دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، فَخَرَجْنَا مِنْ عِنْدِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، نُبَشِّرُ النَّاسَ، فَاسْتَقْبَلَنَا عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، فَرَجَعَ بِنَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِذَا يَتَّكِلَ النَّاسُ؟ قَالَ: فَسَكَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (19597، 19689) من وجهين عن حماد بن سلمة، حدثنا أبو عمران الجوني، عن أبي بكر بن أبي موسى، عن أبيه أبي موسى الأشعري فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (19689, 19597).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a group of my people, and he said: “Rejoice, and give glad tidings to those whom you have left behind: whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, truthfully affirming it, will enter Paradise.” We left the Prophet ﷺ intending to give the people these glad tidings. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb may Allah be pleased with him met us and brought us back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, then the people may rely upon this and become complacent.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (19689، 19597)."},{"num":82,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ مَاتَ يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ النَّارَ، وَقُلْتُ أَنَا: مَنْ مَاتَ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الجنائز (1238) عن عمر بن حفص بن غياث، حدثنا أبي، حدثنا الأعمش، حدثنا شقيق، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1238) and Muslim (92).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “And I say: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1238)، ومسلم (92)."},{"num":83,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ قَالَ: خَرَجْتُ لَيْلَةً مِنَ اللَّيَالِي فَإِذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمْشِي وَحْدَهُ وَلَيْسَ مَعَهُ إِنْسَانٌ، قَالَ: فَظَنَنْتُ أَنَّهُ يَكْرَهُ أَنْ يَمْشِيَ مَعَهُ أَحَدٌ، قَالَ: فَجَعَلْتُ أَمْشِي فِي ظِلِّ الْقَمَرِ فَالْتَفَتَ فَرَآنِي، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ قُلْتُ: أَبُو ذَرٍّ جَعَلَنِي اللَّهُ فِدَاءَكَ، قَالَ: يَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ تَعَالَهْ، قَالَ: فَمَشَيْتُ مَعَهُ سَاعَةً، فَقَالَ: إِنَّ الْمُكْثِرِينَ هُمُ الْمُقِلُّونَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، إِلَّا مَنْ أَعْطَاهُ اللَّهُ خَيْرًا، فَنَفَحَ فِيهِ يَمِينَهُ، وَشِمَالَهُ، وَبَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، وَوَرَاءَهُ، وَعَمِلَ فِيهِ خَيْرًا، قَالَ: فَمَشَيْتُ مَعَهُ سَاعَةً، فَقَالَ لِي: اجْلِسْ هَا هُنَا، قَالَ: فَأَجْلَسَنِي فِي قَاعٍ حَوْلَهُ حِجَارَةٌ، فَقَالَ لِي: اجْلِسْ هَا هُنَا حَتَّى أَرْجِعَ إِلَيْكَ، قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ فِي الْحَرَّةِ حَتَّى لَا أَرَاهُ، فَلَبِثَ عَنِّي، فَأَطَالَ اللُّبْثَ، ثُمَّ إِنِّي سَمِعْتُهُ وَهُوَ مُقْبِلٌ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: وَإِنْ سَرَقَ وَإِنْ زَنَى، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا جَاءَ لَمْ أَصْبِرْ حَتَّى قُلْتُ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، جَعَلَنِي اللَّهُ فِدَاءَكَ مَنْ تُكَلِّمُ فِي جَانِبِ الْحَرَّةِ، مَا سَمِعْتُ أَحَدًا يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْكَ شَيْئًا، قَالَ: ذَلِكَ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَام عَرَضَ لِي فِي جَانِبِ الْحَرَّةِ، قَالَ: بَشِّرْ أُمَّتَكَ أَنَّهُ مَنْ مَاتَ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا، دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، قُلْتُ: يَا جِبْرِيلُ، وَإِنْ سَرَقَ وَإِنْ زَنَى قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: وَإِنْ سَرَقَ، وَإِنْ زَنَى، قَالَ: نَعَمْ، وَإِنْ شَرِبَ الْخَمْرَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الرقاق (6443)، ومسلم في الزكاة (94) كلاهما من حديث عبدالعزيز بن رفيع، عن زيد بن وهب، عن أبي ذر، فذكره، واللُفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6443) and Muslim (94).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: One night I went out and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walking alone, with no one accompanying him. I thought that perhaps he did not wish anyone to walk with him, so I began walking in the shadow of the moon. He turned, saw me, and asked: “Who is this?” I replied: “Abū Dharr. May Allah make me your ransom.” He said: “O Abū Dharr, come.” I walked with him for a while, and he said: “Those who possess the most wealth will be those with the least on the Day of Resurrection, except one whom Allah has given wealth and who distributes it to his right, to his left, before him, and behind him, and uses it to perform good.” We continued walking for a while, then he said: “Sit here.” He seated me in a low place surrounded by stones and said: “Remain here until I return to you.” He went into the volcanic plain until I could no longer see him and remained away for a long time. Then I heard him returning while saying: “Even if he steals and even if he commits fornication.” When he returned, I said: “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, whom were you speaking to at the side of the volcanic plain? I did not hear anyone answering you.” He replied: “That was Jibrīl, peace be upon him. He appeared to me at the side of the volcanic plain and said: ‘Give your Ummah the glad tidings that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.’” I asked: “O Jibrīl, even if he steals and commits fornication?” He replied: “Yes.” I asked again: “Even if he steals and commits fornication?” He replied: “Yes, even if he drinks wine.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[16354],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6443)، ومسلم (94)."},{"num":84,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ وَهْبٍ قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ أَبُو ذَرٍّ بِالرَّبَذَةِ قَالَ: كُنْتُ أَمْشِي مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَرَّةِ الْمَدِينَةِ عِشَاءً اسْتَقْبَلَنَا أُحُدٌ، فَقَالَ: يَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ، مَا أُحِبُّ أَنَّ أُحُدًا لِي ذَهَبًا يَأْتِي عَلَيَّ لَيْلَةٌ، أَوْ ثَلَاثٌ عِنْدِي مِنْهُ دِينَارٌ، إِلَّا أَرْصُدُهُ لِدَيْنٍ إِلَّا أَنْ أَقُولَ بِهِ فِي عِبَادِ اللَّهِ: هَكَذَا وَهَكَذَا وَهَكَذَا، وَأَرَانَا بِيَدِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ، قُلْتُ: لَبَّيْكَ وَسَعْدَيْكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: الْأَكْثَرُونَ هُمُ الْأَقَلُّونَ، إِلَّا مَنْ قَالَ: هَكَذَا وَهَكَذَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: مَكَانَكَ لَا تَبْرَحْ يَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ حَتَّى أَرْجِعَ، فَانْطَلَقَ حَتَّى غَابَ عَنِّي، فَسَمِعْتُ صَوْتًا فَخَشِيتُ أَنْ يَكُونَ عُرِضَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَذْهَبَ، ثُمَّ ذَكَرْتُ قَوْلَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَا تَبْرَحْ، فَمَكُثْتُ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ سَمِعْتُ صَوْتًا خَشِيتُ أَنْ يَكُونَ عُرِضَ لَكَ، ثُمَّ ذَكَرْتُ قَوْلَكَ، فَقُمْتُ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ذَاكَ جِبْرِيلُ أَتَانِي فَأَخْبَرَنِي أَنَّهُ مَنْ مَاتَ مِنْ أُمَّتِي لَا يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَإِنْ زَنَى وَإِنْ سَرَقَ، قَالَ: وَإِنْ زَنَى وَإِنْ سَرَقَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الاستئذان (6268)، ومسلم في الزكاة (94) كلاهما من حديث الأعمش، عن زيد بن وهب، عن أبي ذر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6268) and Muslim (94).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ at night in the volcanic plain of Madinah when he said: “O Abū Dharr, I would not like to possess gold equal to Mount Uḥud and have one night — or three nights — pass while even one dīnār of it remained with me, except an amount I had reserved to repay a debt. Rather, I would distribute it among the servants of Allah like this, like this, and like this.” He gestured with his hand. Then he said: “O Abū Dharr!” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Those who possess the most will be those with the least, except one who distributes his wealth like this and like this.” Then he said: “Remain where you are, O Abū Dharr, and do not leave until I return.” He departed until he disappeared from my sight. I then heard a sound and feared that something might have happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I wanted to go toward him, but I remembered his command: “Do not leave.” So I remained where I was. When he returned, I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I heard a sound and feared that something had happened to you, but then I remembered your instruction and remained.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That was Jibrīl. He came to me and informed me that whoever from my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.” I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, even if he commits fornication and steals?” He replied: “Even if he commits fornication and steals.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6268)، ومسلم (94)."},{"num":85,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أَتَانِي جِبْرِيلُ، فَبَشَّرَنِي أَنَّهُ مَنْ مَاتَ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، قُلْتُ: وَإِنْ سَرَقَ، وَإِنْ زَنَى، قَالَ: وَإِنْ سَرَقَ وَإِنْ زَنَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التوحيد (7487)، ومسلم في الإيمان (94) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، حدثنا غُندر (محمد بن جعفر)، حدثنا شعبة، عن واصل الأحدب، عن المعرور بن سويد، قال: سمعتُ أبا ذر يحدّث عن النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكر الحديث ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7487) and Muslim (94).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Jibrīl came to me and gave me the glad tidings that whoever from your Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.” I asked: “Even if he commits fornication and steals?” He replied: “Even if he commits fornication and steals.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[634],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7487)، ومسلم (94)."},{"num":86,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَلَمَةَ بْنِ نُعَيْمٍ وَكَانَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الرَّسُولِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ لَقِيَ اللَّهَ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، وَإِنْ زَنَى وَإِنْ سَرَقَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (18284، 22464) من وجهين عن أبي معاوية شيبان، حدثنا منصور، عن سالم بن أبي الجعد، عن سلمة بن نُعيم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (22464, 18284).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn Nuʿaym may Allah be pleased with him, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him will enter Paradise, even if he committed fornication and even if he stole.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Meaning of the ḥadīth: Whoever dies upon pure monotheism and repents from sins will enter Paradise from the outset. Ibn Ḥajar says: “As for the one who fell into the sins mentioned and died without repentance, the apparent meaning of the ḥadīth is that he is also included; however, the Sunni position is that his case is under Allah’s will. This is supported by the ḥadīth of ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit: ‘Whoever commits any of that and is not punished for it, then his matter is left to Allah: if He wills, He punishes him, and if He wills, He pardons him.’ This clarified text is given precedence over what is unspecific, and these narrations refute the innovators among the Khawārij and the Muʿtazilah who claim that anyone who dies after committing major sins without repentance must remain eternally in the Fire.” End."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (22464، 18284)."},{"num":87,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ مَاتَ وَهُوَ يَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (26) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن علية، عن خالد، قال: حدثني الوليد بن مسلم، عن حمران، عن عثمان، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (26).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies knowing that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (26)."},{"num":88,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنِّي لَأَعْلَمُ كَلِمَةً لَا يَقُولُهَا عَبْدٌ حَقًّا مِنْ قَلْبِهِ، إِلَّا حُرِّمَ عَلَى النَّارِ فَقَالَ لَهُ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ: أَنَا أُحَدِّثُكَ مَا هِيَ؟ هِيَ كَلِمَةُ الْإِخْلَاصِ الَّتِي أَعَزَّ اللَّهُ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى بِهَا مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابَهُ، وَهِيَ كَلِمَةُ التَّقْوَى الَّتِي أَلَاصَ عَلَيْهَا نَبِيُّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَمَّهُ أَبَا طَالِبٍ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ: شَهَادَةُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (447)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (204)، والحاكم (1302)كلهم من طريق عبدالوهاب بن عطاء الخفاف، حدثنا سعيد، عن قتادة، عن مسلم بن يسار، عن حُمران بن أبان، أنّ عثمان بن عفّان قال (فذكر الحديث)، واللّفظ لأحمد.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (447), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (204) and al-Ḥākim (1298).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I know a statement that no servant utters sincerely and truthfully from his heart except that the Fire is made forbidden for him.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: “I will tell you what it is. It is the statement of sincere devotion that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, made binding upon Muḥammad ﷺ and his Companions. It is the word of piety that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ repeatedly urged his uncle Abū Ṭālib to say at the time of his death: the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (447)، وصححه ابن حبان (204)، والحاكم (1302)."},{"num":89,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: يَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ بِالشَّفَاعَةِ كَأَنَّهُمُ الثَّعَارِيرُ، قُلْتُ: مَا الثَّعَارِيرُ؟ قَالَ: الضَّغَابِيسُ، وَكَانَ قَدْ سَقَطَ فَمُهُ، فَقُلْتُ لِعَمْرِو بْنِ دِينَارٍ أَبَا مُحَمَّدٍ سَمِعْتَ جَابِرَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ يَقُولُ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: يَخْرُجُ بِالشَّفَاعَةِ مِنَ النَّارِ، قَالَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الرقاق (6558)، ومسلم في الإيمان (191 ، 318) كلاهما من حديث حماد بن زيد، عن عمرو، عن جابر، فذكر مثله، واللفظ للبخاريّ، وأما مسلم فلم يذكر الجزء الأول من الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6558) and Muslim (191).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession, looking like al-thaʿārīr.” The narrator asked: “What are al-thaʿārīr?” He replied: “Al-ḍaghābīs.” His teeth had fallen out. I then asked ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: “O Abū Muḥammad, did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession’?” He replied: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[897,16185],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6558)، ومسلم (191)."},{"num":90,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُخْرِجُ نَاسًا مِنَ النَّارِ، فَيُدْخِلَهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (191 ، 317) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو، سمع جابراً يقول: فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (191).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Allah will bring some people out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (191)."},{"num":91,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ قَوْمًا يُخْرَجُونَ مِنَ النَّارِ، يَحْتَرِقُونَ فِيهَا، إِلَّا دَارَاتِ وُجُوهِهِمْ، حَتَّى يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (191 ، 319) عن حجاج بن الشّاعر، حدثنا أبو أحمد الزبيري، حدثنا قيس بن سليم العنبريّ، حدثني يزيد الفقير، حدثنا جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (191).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Some people will be brought out of the Fire after being burned by it, except for the areas surrounding their faces, until they enter Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word «دارات» is the plural of dārah and refers to the areas surrounding the face. The meaning is that the Fire does not consume these areas because they include the places of prostration, as stated in other narrations:","“Except the places of prostration.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (191)."},{"num":92,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَزِيدَ الْفَقِيرِ قَالَ: كُنْتُ قَدْ شَغَفَنِي رَأْيٌ مِنْ رَأْيِ الْخَوَارِجِ فَخَرَجْنَا فِي عِصَابَةٍ ذَوِي عَدَدٍ نُرِيدُ أَنْ نَحُجَّ، ثُمَّ نَخْرُجَ عَلَى النَّاسِ، قَالَ: فَمَرَرْنَا عَلَى الْمَدِينَةِ، فَإِذَا جَابِرُ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ يُحَدِّثُ الْقَوْمَ، جَالِسٌ إِلَى سَارِيَةٍ، عَنِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: فَإِذَا هُوَ قَدْ ذَكَرَ الْجَهَنَّمِيِّينَ، قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: يَا صَاحِبَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ، مَا هَذَا الَّذِي تُحَدِّثُونَ ! وَاللَّهُ يَقُولُ: ﴿رَبَّنَا إِنَّكَ مَنْ تُدْخِلِ النَّارَ فَقَدْ أَخْزَيْتَهُ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصَارٍ﴾ [آل عمران: 192]، ﴿وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ فَسَقُوا فَمَأْوَاهُمُ النَّارُ كُلَّمَا أَرَادُوا أَنْ يَخْرُجُوا مِنْهَا أُعِيدُوا فِيهَا وَقِيلَ لَهُمْ ذُوقُوا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّذِي كُنْتُمْ بِهِ تُكَذِّبُونَ﴾ [السجدة: 20] فَمَا هَذَا الَّذِي تَقُولُونَ؟ قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَتَقْرَأُ الْقُرْآنَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَهَلْ سَمِعْتَ بِمَقَامِ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّم يَعْنِي الَّذِي يَبْعَثُهُ اللَّهُ فِيهِ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَإِنَّهُ مَقَامُ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْمَحْمُودُ الَّذِي يُخْرِجُ اللَّهُ بِهِ مَنْ يُخْرِجُ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ نَعَتَ وَضْعَ الصِّرَاطِ، وَمَرَّ النَّاسِ عَلَيْهِ، قَالَ: وَأَخَافُ أَنْ لَا أَكُونَ أَحْفَظُ ذَاكَ، قَالَ: غَيْرَ أَنَّهُ قَدْ زَعَمَ، أَنَّ قَوْمًا يَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ النَّارِ، بَعْدَ أَنْ يَكُونُوا فِيهَا، قَالَ: يَعْنِي فَيَخْرُجُونَ كَأَنَّهُمْ عِيدَانُ السَّمَاسِمِ، قَالَ: فَيَدْخُلُونَ نَهَرًا مِنْ أَنْهَارِ الْجَنَّةِ، فَيَغْتَسِلُونَ فِيهِ فَيَخْرُجُونَ كَأَنَّهُمُ الْقَرَاطِيسُ فَرَجَعْنَا، قُلْنَا: وَيْحَكُمْ أَتُرَوْنَ الشَّيْخَ يَكْذِبُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَرَجَعْنَا، فَلَا وَاللَّهِ مَا خَرَجَ مِنَّا غَيْرُ رَجُلٍ وَاحِدٍ، أَوْ كَمَا قَالَ أَبُو نُعَيْمٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: أخرجه مسلم في الإيمان (191 ، 320) عن الحجاج بن الشاعر، حدثنا الفضل بن دُكين، حدثنا أبو عاصم، يعني محمد بن أبي أيوب، قال: حدثني يزيد الفقير، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (191).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd al-Faqīr reported: I had become deeply captivated by one of the doctrines of the Khawārij. A sizeable group of us set out intending to perform ḥajj and afterward rebel against the people. We passed through Madinah and found Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh may Allah be pleased with him seated beside a pillar, narrating to the people from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned those who would be brought out of Hell. I said to him: “O Companion of the Messenger of Allah, what is this that you are narrating? Allah says: ‘Our Lord, whoever You admit into the Fire, You have indeed disgraced him, and the wrongdoers will have no helpers.’ [Āl ʿImrān 3:192] And He says: ‘As for those who defiantly disobeyed, their abode will be the Fire. Whenever they wish to leave it, they will be returned to it, and it will be said to them: Taste the punishment of the Fire which you used to deny.’ [Sūrat al-Sajdah 32:20] So what is this that you are saying?” He asked: “Do you recite the Qurʾān?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Have you heard of the Praised Station of Muḥammad ﷺ — the station to which Allah will raise him?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “That is the Praised Station of Muḥammad ﷺ, through which Allah will bring out whomever He wills to bring out.” He then described the setting up of the Ṣirāṭ and the passing of the people over it. Yazīd said: I fear that I did not preserve all of that portion accurately. But he stated that some people would be brought out of the Fire after having remained in it. They would emerge looking like blackened sticks, then enter one of the rivers of Paradise and wash themselves in it. They would emerge as white as sheets of paper. We then returned to one another saying: “Woe to you! Do you really think this elderly Companion is lying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” We returned from our former view, and by Allah, only one man among us continued upon it — or words to that effect, as Abū Nuʿaym related."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “it captivated me” means that the Khārijite doctrine had occupied his heart — specifically their claim that those who commit major sins will remain eternally in the Fire and that whoever enters it will never come out.","“Then we would rebel against the people” means that they intended openly to act upon the doctrine of the Khawārij.","The expression “like stalks of sesame” is explained as resembling thin, darkened stalks. It has also been suggested that the original expression may refer to a type of dark wood.","The words “like sheets of paper” mean that after they wash in the river of Paradise and the blackness caused by the Fire disappears, they will become intensely white. Al-Nawawī mentioned this explanation.","The statement “By Allah, only one man among us continued” means that after completing their pilgrimage they abandoned the Khārijite doctrine and repented from it, except for one man who did not join them in abandoning it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: أخرجه مسلم (191)."},{"num":93,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَا الْمُوجِبَتَانِ؟ فَقَالَ: مَنْ مَاتَ لَا يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، وَمَنْ مَاتَ يُشْرِكُ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا دَخَلَ النَّارَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (93) من طرق عن أبي معاوية، عن الأعمش، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر، فذكره. ورواه أيضاً من وجه آخر عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، به، مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (93).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two matters that make the outcome certain?” He replied: “Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (93)."},{"num":94,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: بَعَثَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: نَادِ فِي النَّاسِ: مَنْ قَالَ: لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ، فَخَرَجَ فَلَقِيَهُ عُمَرُ فِي الطَّرِيقِ، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ تُرِيدُ؟ قُلْتُ: بَعَثَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِكَذَا وَكَذَا، قَالَ: ارْجِعْ، فَأَبَيْتُ، فَلَهَزَنِي لَهْزَةً فِي صَدْرِي أَلَمُهَا، فَرَجَعْتُ وَلَمْ أَجِدْ بُدًّا، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، بَعَثْتَ هَذَا بِكَذَا وَكَذَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ طَمِعُوا وَخَشُوا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اقْعُدْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (693)، وابن حبان (151) كلاهما من طريق المحرر ابن قعنب الباهلي، قال: حدثني رباح بن عبيدة، أن ذكوان السمان حدّثه، أن جابر ابن عبدالله حدّثه وقال (فذكره)، واللفظ لابن حبان.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (693) and Ibn Ḥibbān (151).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and said: “Announce among the people: whoever says, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ will enter Paradise.” I went out and met ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with him on the road. He asked: “Where are you going?” I replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with such-and-such a message.” He said: “Go back.” I refused, so he gave me a forceful push in the chest. I returned, having little choice. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you send him with such-and-such a message?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, the people have become hopeful and afraid.” The Prophet ﷺ said to Jābir: “Sit down.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (693)، وابن حبان (151)."},{"num":95,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَيُخَلِّصُ رَجُلا مِنْ أُمَّتِي عَلَى رُءُوسِ الْخَلائِقِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فَيَنْشُرُ عَلَيْهِ تِسْعَةً وَتِسْعِينَ سِجِلًّا كُلُّ سِجِلٍّ مَدُّ الْبَصَرِ، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: أَتُنْكِرُ مِنْ هَذَا شَيْئًا؟ أَظَلَمَكَ كَتَبَتِي الْحَافِظُونَ؟ فَيَقُولُ: لَا يَا رَبِّ، فَيَقُولُ: أَفَلَكَ عُذْرٌ؟ فَيَقُولُ: لَا يَا رَبِّ، فَيَقُولُ: بَلَى، إِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَنَا حَسَنَةً فَإِنَّهُ لَا ظُلْمَ عَلَيْكَ الْيَوْمَ، فَتَخْرُجُ بِطَاقَةٌ فِيهَا أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، فَيَقُولُ: احْضُرْ وَزْنَكَ، فَيَقُولُ: يَا رَبِّ مَا هَذِهِ الْبِطَاقَةُ مَعَ هَذِهِ السِّجِلَّاتِ؟ فَقَالَ: إِنَّكَ لَا تُظْلَمُ، قَالَ: فَتُوضَعُ السِّجِلَّاتُ فِي كَفَّةٍ وَالْبِطَاقَةُ فِي كَفَّةٍ، فَطَاشَتِ السِّجِلَّاتُ وَثَقُلَتِ الْبِطَاقَةُ، فَلَا يَثْقُلُ مَعَ اسْمِ اللَّهِ شَيْءٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2639)، واللفظ له، وابن ماجه (4300) كلاهما من حديث الليث بن سعد، قال: حدثني عامر بن يحيى، عن أبي عبدالرحمن المعافري ثم الحبلي، قال: سمعت عبدالله بن عمرو بن العاص، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات على التوحيد دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2639), whose wording is cited here, Ibn Mājah (4300), and Aḥmad (6994).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Upon Tawḥīd Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will single out a man from my Ummah before all creation on the Day of Resurrection. Ninety-nine records will be spread out before him, each one extending as far as the eye can see. Allah will ask: ‘Do you deny any of this? Have My recording angels wronged you?’ He will reply: ‘No, my Lord.’ Allah will ask: ‘Do you have any excuse?’ He will reply: ‘No, my Lord.’ Allah will say: ‘Indeed, you have one good deed with Us, and no injustice will be done to you today.’ A small card will then be brought forth upon which is written: ‘I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I testify that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger.’ Allah will say: ‘Come forward for your weighing.’ The man will say: ‘My Lord, what is this small card compared with all these records?’ Allah will say: ‘You will not be wronged.’ The records will then be placed on one side of the Scale and the card on the other. The records will become light, while the card will outweigh them, for nothing can outweigh the Name of Allah.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “the records became light” means that they rose because their weight was outweighed.","A biṭāqah is a small written card.","Sijillāt is the plural of sijill, meaning large written records.","The statement “Whoever says, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ will enter Paradise” refers to one who says it while believing in the prophethood of Muḥammad ﷺ. Merely uttering it does not benefit a person who rejects the prophethood of Muḥammad ﷺ; belief in his prophethood is also necessary."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2639) واللفظ له، وابن ماجه (4300)، وأحمد (6994)."},{"num":96,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ بْنِ الْيَمَانِ قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَدِيثَيْنِ رَأَيْتُ أَحَدَهُمَا وَأَنَا أَنْتَظِرُ الْآخَرَ، حَدَّثَنَا:\" أَنَّ الْأَمَانَةَ نَزَلَتْ فِي جَذْرِ قُلُوبِ الرِّجَالِ، ثُمَّ عَلِمُوا مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ، ثُمَّ عَلِمُوا مِنَ السُّنَّةِ.","وَحَدَّثَنَا عَنْ رَفْعِهَا، قَالَ: يَنَامُ الرَّجُلُ النَّوْمَةَ، فَتُقْبَضُ الْأَمَانَةُ مِنْ قَلْبِهِ، فَيَظَلُّ أَثَرُهَا مِثْلَ أَثَرِ الْوَكْتِ، ثُمَّ يَنَامُ النَّوْمَةَ، فَتُقْبَضُ فَيَبْقَى أَثَرُهَا مِثْلَ الْمَجْلِ كَجَمْرٍ دَحْرَجْتَهُ عَلَى رِجْلِكَ، فَنَفِطَ فَتَرَاهُ مُنْتَبِرًا وَلَيْسَ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ، فَيُصْبِحُ النَّاسُ يَتَبَايَعُونَ فَلَا يَكَادُ أَحَدٌ يُؤَدِّي الْأَمَانَةَ، فَيُقَالُ: إِنَّ فِي بَنِي فُلَانٍ رَجُلًا أَمِينًا، وَيُقَالُ لِلرَّجُلِ: مَا أَعْقَلَهُ وَمَا أَظْرَفَهُ وَمَا أَجْلَدَهُ وَمَا فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالُ حَبَّةِ خَرْدَلٍ مِنْ إِيمَانٍ.","وَلَقَدْ أَتَى عَلَيَّ زَمَانٌ وَمَا أُبَالِي أَيَّكُمْ بَايَعْتُ لَئِنْ كَانَ مُسْلِمًا رَدَّهُ عَلَيَّ الْإِسْلَامُ، وَإِنْ كَانَ نَصْرَانِيًّا رَدَّهُ عَلَيَّ سَاعِيهِ، فَأَمَّا الْيَوْمَ فَمَا كُنْتُ أُبَايِعُ إِلَّا فُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الرقاق (6497)، ومسلم في الإيمان (143) كلاهما من حديث الأعمش، عن زيد بن وهب، حدّثنا حذيفة، فذكره. واللّفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رفع الأمانة والإيمان من بعض القلوب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6497) and Muslim (143), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"The Removal of Trustworthiness and Faith From Some Hearts","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated two matters to us. I have already witnessed one of them, and I am awaiting the other. He told us: “Trustworthiness was placed deep within the roots of men’s hearts. Then they learned from the Qurʾān, and afterward they learned from the Sunnah.” He also told us about its removal: “A man will sleep, and trustworthiness will be taken from his heart, leaving behind a trace like a faint mark.","Then he will sleep again, and it will be taken away further, leaving behind a mark like a blister — like a burning coal rolled over your foot until it causes swelling. You see it raised, although there is nothing substantial within it. People will then begin buying and selling with one another, yet hardly anyone will fulfill what has been entrusted to him. It will be said: ‘Among the clan of so-and-so there is a trustworthy man.’ And it will be said of a man: ‘How intelligent he is! How refined he is! How strong he is!’ Yet there will not be in his heart even the weight of a mustard seed of faith.” Ḥudhayfah said: There was once a time when I did not care with whom among you I conducted business. If he was a Muslim, his Islam would cause him to return my right to me; and if he was a Christian, his authority would return my right to me.","But today, I would conduct business only with so-and-so and so-and-so. Al-Aṣmaʿī, Abū ʿAmr, and others explained: “The roots of the hearts” means their deepest foundation. Al-wakt means a slight remaining trace. Al-majl refers to the thickened mark that forms upon the palm because of work."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression «بايعت» here refers to buying and selling, not giving political allegiance.","«المنتبر» means something raised or swollen.","«فنفط» refers to swelling in which fluid gathers between the skin and the flesh."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6497)، ومسلم (143)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":97,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: شَهِدْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: لِرَجُلٍ مِمَّنْ يَدَّعِي الْإِسْلَامَ هَذَا مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَلَمَّا حَضَرَ الْقِتَالُ قَاتَلَ الرَّجُلُ قِتَالًا شَدِيدًا فَأَصَابَتْهُ جِرَاحَةٌ، فَقِيلَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، الَّذِي قُلْتَ لَهُ: إِنَّهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ فَإِنَّهُ قَدْ قَاتَلَ الْيَوْمَ قِتَالًا شَدِيدًا وَقَدْ مَاتَ؟، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى النَّارِ، قَالَ: فَكَادَ بَعْضُ النَّاسِ أَنْ يَرْتَابَ فَبَيْنَمَا هُمْ عَلَى ذَلِكَ إِذْ قِيلَ: إِنَّهُ لَمْ يَمُتْ وَلَكِنَّ بِهِ جِرَاحًا شَدِيدًا، فَلَمَّا كَانَ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ لَمْ يَصْبِرْ عَلَى الْجِرَاحِ فَقَتَلَ نَفْسَهُ، فَأُخْبِرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ: اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ أَشْهَدُ أَنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولُهُ، ثُمَّ أَمَرَ بِلَالًا فَنَادَى بِالنَّاسِ إِنَّهُ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ إِلَّا نَفْسٌ مُسْلِمَةٌ، وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَيُؤَيِّدُ هَذَا الدِّينَ بِالرَّجُلِ الْفَاجِرِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الجهاد (3062)، ومسلم في الإيمان (111) كلاهما من حديث عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهريّ، عن ابن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة إلا رجل مؤمن وإن الله يؤيد هذا الدين بالرجل الفاجر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3062) and Muslim (111).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Believer, and Allah May Support This Religion Through a Sinful Man","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Khaybar. He said concerning a man who claimed to be Muslim: “This man is among the people of the Fire.” When the fighting began, the man fought with great intensity and was wounded. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, the man whom you said was among the people of the Fire fought fiercely today and has died!” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “To the Fire.” Some of the people almost began to doubt. Then they were informed that the man had not died but had suffered severe wounds. When night came, he was unable to endure the pain of his wounds and killed himself. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, and he said: “Allāhu akbar! I testify that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.” He then ordered Bilāl to proclaim among the people: “No soul will enter Paradise except a Muslim, and indeed Allah may support this religion through a sinful man.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3062)، ومسلم (111)."},{"num":98,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ خَيْبَرَ، أَقْبَلَ نَفَرٌ مِنْ صَحَابَةِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: فُلَانٌ شَهِيدٌ، فُلَانٌ شَهِيدٌ حَتَّى مَرُّوا عَلَى رَجُلٍ فَقَالُوا: فُلَانٌ شَهِيدٌ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَلَّا إِنِّي رَأَيْتُهُ فِي النَّارِ فِي بُرْدَةٍ غَلَّهَا أَوْ عَبَاءَةٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا ابْنَ الْخَطَّابِ، اذْهَبْ فَنَادِ فِي النَّاسِ، أَنَّهُ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ إِلَّا الْمُؤْمِنُونَ، قَالَ: فَخَرَجْتُ فَنَادَيْتُ، أَلَا إِنَّهُ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ إِلَّا الْمُؤْمِنُونَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (114) عن زهير بن حرب، حدثنا هاشم بن القاسم، حدثنا عكرمة بن عمار، قال: حدثني سماك الحنفيّ أبو زميل، قال: حدثني عبدالله بن عباس، قال: حدثني عمر بن الخطاب، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة إلا رجل مؤمن وإن الله يؤيد هذا الدين بالرجل الفاجر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (114).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Believer, and Allah May Support This Religion Through a Sinful Man","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: On the day of Khaybar, a number of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came saying: “So-and-so is a martyr. So-and-so is a martyr.” Eventually they passed a man and said: “So-and-so is a martyr.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No. I saw him in the Fire because of a cloak — or garment — that he had unlawfully taken from the spoils.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O son of al-Khaṭṭāb, go and announce among the people that no one will enter Paradise except the believers.” I went out and proclaimed: “Indeed, no one will enter Paradise except the believers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[8044,9085,16348],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (114)."},{"num":99,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بِشْرِ بْنِ سُحَيْمٍ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَهُ أَنْ يُنَادِيَ أَيَّامَ التَّشْرِيقِ: أَنَّهُ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ إِلَّا مُؤْمِنٌ، وَهِيَ أَيَّامُ أَكْلٍ وَشُرْبٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائيّ (4994) عن قتيبة، حدثنا حماد، عن عمرو، عن نافع بن جبير بن مطعم، عن بشر بن سحيم، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة إلا رجل مؤمن وإن الله يؤيد هذا الدين بالرجل الفاجر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Nasāʾī (4994), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2960).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Believer, and Allah May Support This Religion Through a Sinful Man","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Bishr ibn Suḥaym, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to proclaim during the Days of Tashrīq: “No one will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Mājah (1720) also narrated that the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon during the Days of Tashrīq and said:","“No soul will enter Paradise except a Muslim, and these days are days of eating and drinking.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (4994)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2960)."},{"num":100,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: يَلْقَى إِبْرَاهِيمُ أَبَاهُ آزَرَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَعَلَى وَجْهِ آزَرَ قَتَرَةٌ وَغَبَرَةٌ، فَيَقُولُ لَهُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكَ لَا تَعْصِنِي، فَيَقُولُ: أَبُوهُ فَالْيَوْمَ لَا أَعْصِيكَ، فَيَقُولُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ: يَا رَبِّ إِنَّكَ وَعَدْتَنِي أَنْ لَا تُخْزِيَنِي يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُونَ فَأَيُّ خِزْيٍ أَخْزَى مِنْ أَبِي الْأَبْعَدِ، فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: إِنِّي حَرَّمْتُ الْجَنَّةَ عَلَى الْكَافِرِينَ، ثُمَّ يُقَالُ: يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ مَا تَحْتَ رِجْلَيْكَ فَيَنْظُرُ فَإِذَا هُوَ بِذِيخٍ مُلْتَطِخٍ فَيُؤْخَذُ بِقَوَائِمِهِ فَيُلْقَى فِي النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في أحاديث الأنبياء (3350) عن إسماعيل بن عبدالله، قال: أخبرني أخي عبدالحميد، عن ابن أبي ذئب، عن سعيد المقبري، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله حرم الجنة على الكافرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3350).","chapter_en":"Allah Has Forbidden Paradise to the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Ibrāhīm will meet his father Āzar on the Day of Resurrection, and Āzar’s face will be covered with darkness and dust. Ibrāhīm will say to him: ‘Did I not tell you not to disobey me?’ His father will reply: ‘Today I will not disobey you.’ Ibrāhīm will then say: ‘My Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me on the Day they are resurrected. What disgrace could be greater than the fate of my distant father?’ Allah Most High will say: ‘I have forbidden Paradise to the disbelievers.’ Then it will be said: ‘O Ibrāhīm, what is beneath your feet?’ He will look and find a male hyena soiled with filth. It will be seized by its legs and cast into the Fire.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word «ذيخ» refers to a male hyena, as al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar explained in Fatḥ al-Bārī."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8366,12523,12929,13531,16350],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3350)."},{"num":101,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَيَأْخُذَنَّ رَجُلٌ بِيَدِ أَبِيهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يُدْخِلَهُ الْجَنَّةَ، فَيُنَادَى: إِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ لا يَدْخُلُهَا مُشْرِكٌ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ حَرَّمَ الْجَنَّةَ عَلَى كُلِّ مُشْرِكٍ، فَيَقُولُ: أَيْ رَبِّ، أَيْ رَبِّ، أَبِي، قَالَ: فَيَتَحَوَّلُ فِي صُورَةٍ قَبِيحَةٍ وَرِيحٍ مُنْتِنَةٍ، فَيَتْرُكُهُ.","قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ: كَانَ أَصْحَابُ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرَوْنَ أَنَّهُ إِبْرَاهِيَمُ، وَلَمْ يَزِدْهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (252)، واللفظ له، والبزار، كشف الأستار (94)، والحاكم (8844) كلهم من حديث المعتمر ابن سليمان، قال: سمعت أبي يحدّث عن قتادة، عن عقبة بن عبدالغافر، عن أبي سعيد، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله حرم الجنة على الكافرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (252), whose wording is cited here, al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (94), and al-Ḥākim (8746).","chapter_en":"Allah Has Forbidden Paradise to the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man will certainly take his father by the hand on the Day of Resurrection, intending to bring him into Paradise. Then it will be proclaimed: ‘No polytheist will enter Paradise. Indeed, Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist.’ The man will say: ‘My Lord! My Lord! My father!’ Then his father will be transformed into an ugly form with a foul odor, and he will leave him.”","Abū Saʿīd said: The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ understood this man to be Ibrāhīm, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not tell them anything beyond that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (252)، واللفظ له، والبزار في كشف الأستار (94)، والحاكم (8844)."},{"num":102,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ مَنْ كَانَ فِي قَلْبِهِ مِثْقَالُ ذَرَّةٍ مِنْ كِبْرٍ، قَالَ رَجُلٌ: إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ، يُحِبُّ أَنْ يَكُونَ ثَوْبُهُ حَسَنًا، وَنَعْلُهُ حَسَنَةً، قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ جَمِيلٌ يُحِبُّ الْجَمَالَ، الْكِبْرُ بَطَرُ الْحَقِّ وَغَمْطُ النَّاسِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (91) من طرق عن شعبة، عن أبان بن تغلب، عن فضيل الُقَيميّ، عن إبراهيم النخعيّ، عن علقمة، عن ابن مسعود، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الترهيب من الكبر وأنه مناف لكمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (91).","chapter_en":"Warning Against Arrogance, and That It Conflicts With the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who has in his heart the weight of a tiny particle of arrogance will enter Paradise.” A man said: “A person likes his clothes to be fine and his shoes to be fine.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Indeed, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down upon people.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[14964],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (91)."},{"num":103,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَنْ يُنَجِّيَ أَحَدًا مِنْكُمْ عَمَلُهُ، قَالُوا: وَلَا أَنْتَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: وَلَا أَنَا، إِلَّا أَنْ يَتَغَمَّدَنِي اللَّهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ سَدِّدُوا، وَقَارِبُوا وَاغْدُوا، وَرُوحُوا وَشَيْءٌ مِنَ الدُّلْجَةِ وَالْقَصْدَ الْقَصْدَ تَبْلُغُوا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الرقاق (6463)، ومسلم في صفات المنافقين (2816) كلاهما من طرق عن أبي هريرة، واللّفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم قريب منه. وفي روايات البخاريّ الأخرى زيادة: والنهي عن تمني الموت. وهو مذكور في كتاب الجنائز.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لن يدخل أحد الجنة إلا برحمة من الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6463) and Muslim (2816).","chapter_en":"No One Will Enter Paradise Except Through the Mercy of Allah","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you will be saved by his deeds.” They asked: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His mercy. So remain upright, strive to come close to what is right, worship in the morning and evening and during a portion of the night, and observe moderation. Observe moderation, and you will reach your destination.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[15143],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6463)، ومسلم (2816)."},{"num":104,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ مَنْ لَا يَأْمَنُ جَارُهُ بَوَائِقَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (46) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن جعفر، قال: أخبرني العلاء، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الترهيب من إيذاء الجار وأنه مناف لكمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (46).","chapter_en":"Warning Against Harming One’s Neighbor, and That It Conflicts With the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word «بوائق» is the plural of bāʾiqah and refers to grave harm, treachery, calamity, or destructive wrongdoing."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14178],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (46)."},{"num":105,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْمُؤْمِنُ مَنْ أَمِنَهُ النَّاسُ، وَالْمُسْلِمُ مَنْ سَلِمَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ مِنْ لِسَانِهِ وَيَدِهِ، وَالْمُهَاجِرُ مَنْ هَجَرَ السُّوءَ، وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ لا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ عَبْدٌ لا يَأْمَنُ جَارُهُ بَوَائِقَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12561)، وابن حبان (510)، والحاكم (25) كلهم من طريق حماد بن سلمة، عن علي بن زيد ويونس بن عبيد وحميد كلهم عن أنس بن مالك فذكره، واللفظ والإسناد لأحمد.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الترهيب من إيذاء الجار وأنه مناف لكمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Aḥmad (12561), Ibn Ḥibbān (510), and al-Ḥākim (25).","chapter_en":"Warning Against Harming One’s Neighbor, and That It Conflicts With the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is the one from whom people feel safe. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The emigrant is the one who abandons evil. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a servant will not enter Paradise if his neighbor is not safe from his harms.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12561)، وابن حبان (510)، والحاكم (25)."},{"num":106,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: ثَلَاثٌ مَنْ كُنَّ فِيهِ وَجَدَ حَلَاوَةَ الْإِيمَانِ، أَنْ يَكُونَ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْهِ مِمَّا سِوَاهُمَا، وَأَنْ يُحِبَّ الْمَرْءَ لَا يُحِبُّهُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِ، وَأَنْ يَكْرَهَ أَنْ يَعُودَ فِي الْكُفْرِ كَمَا يَكْرَهُ أَنْ يُقْذَفَ فِي النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (16)، ومسلم في الإيمان (43) كلاهما من حديث عبدالوهاب الثقفيّ، حدثنا أيوب، عن أبي قلابة، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلاوة الإيمان وطعمه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (16) and Muslim (43).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About the Sweetness and Taste of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There are three qualities which, whoever possesses them, will experience the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that he hates to return to disbelief just as he would hate to be cast into the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (16)، ومسلم (43)."},{"num":107,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْعَبَّاسِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: ذَاقَ طَعْمَ الإِيمَانِ، مَنْ رَضِيَ بِاللَّهِ رَبًّا، وَبِالإِسْلَامِ دِينًا، وَبِمُحَمَّدٍ رَسُولًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (34) من طرق عن عبدالعزيز بن محمد الدراورديّ، عن يزيد بن الهاد، عن محمد بن إبراهيم، عن عامر بن سعد، عن العباس بن عبدالمطلب، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلاوة الإيمان وطعمه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (34).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About the Sweetness and Taste of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib may Allah be pleased with him reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as his Lord, with Islam as his religion, and with Muḥammad as his Messenger.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[743],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (34)."},{"num":108,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ أَحَبَّ أَنْ يَجِدَ طَعْمَ الْإِيمَانِ فَلْيُحِبَّ الْمَرْءَ لَا يُحِبُّهُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِ عَزَّوَجَلَّ. وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: مَنْ سَرَّهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (7967)، والبزّار-كشف الأستار (63)، والحاكم (3) كلهم من طريق شعبة، عن يحيى بن أبي سليم، سمعت عمرو ابن ميمون، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلاوة الإيمان وطعمه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (7967), al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (63), and al-Ḥākim (3).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About the Sweetness and Taste of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever wishes to experience the taste of faith, let him love a person only for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (7967)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (63)، والحاكم (3)."},{"num":109,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى أَكُونَ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ وَالِدِهِ وَوَلَدِهِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (15)، ومسلم في الإيمان (44) كلاهما من حديث عبدالعزيز بن صهيب، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حب الرسول من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (15) and Muslim (44).","chapter_en":"Love for the Messenger Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his father, his child, and all people.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording of Muslim:","“…until I am more beloved to him than his family, his wealth, and all people.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12440],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (15)، ومسلم (44)."},{"num":110,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَن رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: فَوَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ، لَا يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى أَكُونَ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ وَالِدِهِ وَوَلَدِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (14) عن أبي اليمان، قال: أخبرنا شعيب، قال: حدثنا أبو الزّناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حب الرسول من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (14).","chapter_en":"Love for the Messenger Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose Hand is my soul, none of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his father and his child.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[741],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (14)."},{"num":111,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ: أَنَّ أَعْرَابِيًّا قَالَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَتَى السَّاعَةُ؟ قَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا أَعْدَدْتَ لَهَا؟ قَالَ: حُبَّ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، قَالَ: أَنْتَ مَعَ مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في البر والصلة (2639) عن عبدالله بن مسلمة بن قعنب، حدثنا مالك، عن إسحاق بن عبدالله بن أبي طلحة، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من أحب الله ورسوله يكون معه في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"","chapter_en":"Whoever Loves Allah and His Messenger Will Be With Them in Paradise","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “When will the Hour be?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What have you prepared for it?” He replied: “Love for Allah and His Messenger.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You will be with those whom you love.” Narrated by Muslim (2639). Al-Bukhārī (7153) and Muslim also narrated through Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him that: While I was leaving the mosque with the Prophet ﷺ, we met a man at the entrance of the mosque. He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour be?” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What have you prepared for it?” The man seemed humbled by the question and then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have not prepared for it a great amount of fasting, prayer, or charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You will be with those whom you love.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[744,13232,16352],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2639)."},{"num":112,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى يُحِبَّ لِأَخِيهِ مَا يُحِبُّ لِنَفْسِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (13)، ومسلم في الإيمان (45) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن قتادة، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من خصال الإيمان أن يحب لأخيه ما يحب لنفسه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (13) and Muslim (45).","chapter_en":"From the Traits of Faith Is to Love for One’s Brother What One Loves for Oneself","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated through another route:","“By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a servant does not believe until he loves for his neighbor — or his brother — what he loves for himself.”","Ibn Ḥibbān (235) narrated:","“A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he loves for people the good that he loves for himself.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (13)، ومسلم (45)."},{"num":113,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَزِيدَ بْنِ أَسَدٍ قَالَ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا يَزِيدُ ابْنَ أَسَدٍ، أَحِبَّ لِلنَّاسِ مَا تُحِبُّ لِنَفْسِكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابنُ سعد في الطبقات (4600)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد المسند (16656)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 625)، والحاكم (7406)، والبيهقي في الشعب (10617) كلهم من طريق سيّار بن الحكم قال: سمعتُ خالد بن عبد الله القَسري على القسري على المنبر يقول: حدثني أبي، عن جدي يزيد بن أسد قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من خصال الإيمان أن يحب لأخيه ما يحب لنفسه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (7/428) and ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in Zawāʾid al-Musnad (16656).","chapter_en":"From the Traits of Faith Is to Love for One’s Brother What One Loves for Oneself","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Asad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Yazīd ibn Asad, love for people what you love for yourself.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن سعد في الطبقات (4600)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد المسند (16656)."},{"num":114,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلَا يُؤْذِ جَارَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ ضَيْفَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيَقُلْ خَيْرًا أَوْ لِيَصْمُتْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6018)، ومسلم في الإيمان (47) كلاهما من حديث أبي الأحوص، عن أبي حصين، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن إكرام الضيف من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6018) and Muslim (47), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Honoring the Guest Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak what is good or remain silent.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In Muslim’s wording:","“…should speak what is good or remain silent.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14168],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6018)، ومسلم (47)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":115,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي شُرَيْحٍ الْعَدَوِيِّ قَالَ: سَمِعَتْ أُذُنَايَ وَأَبْصَرَتْ عَيْنَايَ حِينَ تَكَلَّمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ جَارَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ ضَيْفَهُ جَائِزَتَهُ، قَالَ: وَمَا جَائِزَتُهُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: يَوْمٌ وَلَيْلَةٌ، وَالضِّيَافَةُ ثَلَاثَةُ أَيَّامٍ فَمَا كَانَ وَرَاءَ ذَلِكَ فَهُوَ صَدَقَةٌ عَلَيْهِ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيَقُلْ خَيْرًا أَوْ لِيَصْمُتْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6019) عن عبدالله بن يوسف، حدثنا الليث، قال: حدثني سعيد المقبري، عن أبي شريح العدويّ، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن إكرام الضيف من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6019) and Muslim (48).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Honoring the Guest Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Shurayḥ al-ʿAdawī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: My own ears heard and my own eyes saw when the Prophet ﷺ spoke and said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest with his due hospitality.” He was asked: “What is his due hospitality, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “One day and one night. Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity for him. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak what is good or remain silent.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14169],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6019)، ومسلم (48)."},{"num":116,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: مَنْ رَأَى مِنْكُمْ مُنْكَرًا فَلْيُغَيِّرْهُ بِيَدِهِ، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِلِسَانِهِ، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِقَلْبِهِ، وَذَلِكَ أَضْعَفُ الإِيمَانِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (49) من طرق عن قيس بن مسلم، عن طارق ابن شهاب قال: أوّل من بدأ بالخطبة يوم العيد قبل الصلاة مروان فقام إليه رجلٌ فقال: الصلاة قبل الخطبة. فقال: قد تُرك ما هنالك. فقال أبو سعيد: أمّا هذا فقد قضى ما عليه، سمعتُ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن النهي عن المنكر من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (49).","chapter_en":"Clarifying That Forbidding Wrong Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand. If he is unable to do so, then with his tongue. If he is unable to do so, then with his heart, and that is the weakest level of faith.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وجاء في سياق الحديث:","كان أول من بدأ بالخطبة يوم العيد قبل الصلاة مروان، فقام إليه رجل فقال:","الصلاة قبل الخطبة.","فقال:","قد ترك ما هنالك.","فقال أبو سعيد رضي الله عنه:","أما هذا فقد قضى ما عليه. سمعت رسول الله ﷺ يقول — فذكر الحديث."],"en":["The context of the narration states that Marwān was the first to begin the sermon on the day of ʿĪd before the prayer. A man stood up and said:","“The prayer should come before the sermon.”","Marwān replied:","“That practice has been abandoned.”","Abū Saʿīd may Allah be pleased with him then said:","“As for this man, he has fulfilled what was required of him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say…” and he then narrated the ḥadīth above."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[14689],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (49)."},{"num":117,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَا مِنْ نَبِيٍّ بَعَثَهُ اللَّهُ فِي أُمَّةٍ قَبْلِي إِلَّا كَانَ لَهُ مِنْ أُمَّتِهِ حَوَارِيُّونَ وَأَصْحَابٌ يَأْخُذُونَ بِسُنَّتِهِ وَيَقْتَدُونَ بِأَمْرِهِ، ثُمَّ إِنَّهَا تَخْلُفُ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ خُلُوفٌ، يَقُولُونَ مَا لَا يَفْعَلُونَ، وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا لَا يُؤْمَرُونَ، فَمَنْ جَاهَدَهُمْ بِيَدِهِ فَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَمَنْ جَاهَدَهُمْ بِلِسَانِهِ فَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَمَنْ جَاهَدَهُمْ بِقَلْبِهِ فَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَيْسَ وَرَاءَ ذَلِكَ مِنَ الإِيمَانِ حَبَّةُ خَرْدَلٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (50) من طرق عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم بن سعد، حدثني أبي، عن صالح بن كيسان، عن الحارث، عن جعفر بن عبدالله ابن الحكم، عن عبدالرحمن بن المسور، عن أبي رافع، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن النهي عن المنكر من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (50).","chapter_en":"Clarifying That Forbidding Wrong Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There was no prophet whom Allah sent to a nation before me except that he had devoted disciples and Companions from among his nation who followed his Sunnah and obeyed his commands. Then there came after them successors who said what they did not do and did what they had not been commanded to do. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer; whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer; and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer. Beyond that there is not even a mustard seed’s weight of faith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15682],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (50)."},{"num":118,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: آيَةُ الْإِيمَانِ حُبُّ الْأَنْصَارِ، وَآيَةُ النِّفَاقِ بُغْضُ الْأَنْصَارِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (17)، ومسلم في الإيمان (74) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، أخبرني عبدالله بن عبدالله بن جَبْر، قال: سمعت أنساً، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن حب الأنصار من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (17) and Muslim (74).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Love for the Anṣār Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A sign of faith is love for the Anṣār, and a sign of hypocrisy is hatred for the Anṣār.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (17)، ومسلم (74)."},{"num":119,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: الْأَنْصَارُ لَا يُحِبُّهُمْ إِلَّا مُؤْمِنٌ، وَلَا يُبْغِضُهُمْ إِلَّا مُنَافِقٌ، فَمَنْ أَحَبَّهُمْ أَحَبَّهُ اللَّهُ، وَمَنْ أَبْغَضَهُمْ أَبْغَضَهُ اللَّهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المناقب الأنصار (3783)، ومسلم في الإيمان (75) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن عدي بن ثابت، عن البراء، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن حب الأنصار من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3783) and Muslim (75).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Love for the Anṣār Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No one loves the Anṣār except a believer, and no one hates them except a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, Allah loves him; and whoever hates them, Allah hates him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3783)، ومسلم (75)."},{"num":120,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يُبْغِضُ الأَنْصَارَ رَجُلٌ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِر."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (77) من طرق عن الأعمش، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي سعيد، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن حب الأنصار من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (77).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Love for the Anṣār Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Anṣār.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (77)."},{"num":121,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَا يُبْغِضُ الأَنْصَارَ رَجُلٌ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الآخِرِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (76) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا يعقوب (يعني عبدالرحمن القاري) عن سُهيل، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن حب الأنصار من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (76).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Love for the Anṣār Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Anṣār.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (76)."},{"num":122,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَرَّ عَلَى رَجُلٍ وَهُوَ يَعِظُ أَخَاهُ فِي الْحَيَاءِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: دَعْهُ فَإِنَّ الْحَيَاءَ مِنَ الْإِيمَانِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في حسن الخلق (10) عن ابن شهاب، عن سالم، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الحياء من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (10), al-Bukhārī (24), and Muslim (36).","chapter_en":"Modesty Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who was admonishing his brother regarding modesty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave him, for modesty is part of faith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (10)، والبخاري (24)، ومسلم (36)."},{"num":123,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عِمْرَانَ بْنِ حُصَيْنٍ يُحَدِّثُ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: الْحَيَاءُ لَا يَأْتِي إِلَّا بِخَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6117)، ومسلم في الإيمان (37) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن قتادة، عن أبي السّوار العدويّ، قال: سمعتُ عمران ابن حصين، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الحياء من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6117) and Muslim (37).","chapter_en":"Modesty Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty brings nothing except good.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated through another route that Abū Qatādah said:","We were sitting with ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn among a group of us, and Bushayr ibn Kaʿb was present.","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated the ḥadīth.","Bushayr ibn Kaʿb said:","“We find in some writings — or in words of wisdom — that some forms of modesty bring tranquility and dignity, while some arise from weakness.”","ʿImrān became angry until his eyes reddened and said:","“I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you oppose it with something else!”","ʿImrān repeated the ḥadīth, and Bushayr repeated his statement, whereupon ʿImrān became angry again.","The narrator said:","We continued trying to calm him, saying:","“He is one of us, O Abū Nujayd. There is nothing wrong with him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6117)، ومسلم (37)."},{"num":124,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَشَدَّ حَيَاءً مِنَ الْعَذْرَاءِ فِي خِدْرِهَا، فَإِذَا رَأَى شَيْئًا يَكْرَهُهُ عَرَفْنَاهُ فِي وَجْهِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6102)، ومسلم في مناقب النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم (2320) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن قتادة، قال: سمعت عبدالله، هو ابن أبي عتبة مولى أنس، ، عن أبي سعيد الخدري، فذكره مثله، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الحياء من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6102) and Muslim (2320).","chapter_en":"Modesty Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: “The Prophet ﷺ was more modest than a virgin secluded in her private chamber. Whenever he saw something he disliked, we could recognize it from his face.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6102)، ومسلم (2320)."},{"num":125,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْحَيَاءُ مِنَ الإِيمَانِ، وَالإِيمَانُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَالْبَذَاءُ مِنَ الْجَفَاءِ، وَالْجَفَاءُ فِي النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2009) من طرق عن محمد بن عمرو، حدثنا أبو سلمة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره. قال الترمذيّ: حسن صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الحياء من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2009), who said, “Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ,” and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (608, 609).","chapter_en":"Modesty Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscene speech is from harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13862],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2009)، وقال: «حسن صحيح»، وصححه ابن حبان (608، 609)."},{"num":126,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْحَيَاءُ وَالإِيمَانُ قُرِنَا جَمِيعًا، فَإِذَا رُفِعَ أَحَدُهُمَا رُفِعَ الآخَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الحاكم (59) عن أبي بكر بن إسحاق الفقيه، أنا محمد بن غالب، أنا موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا جرير بن حازم، عن يعلى بن حكيم، عن سعيد ابن جبير، عن ابن عمر، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الحياء من الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (58).","chapter_en":"Modesty Is Part of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty and faith are joined together. When one of them is removed, the other is removed as well.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13868],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الحاكم (59)."},{"num":127,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جِهَارًا غَيْرَ سِرٍّ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ آلَ أَبِي، قَالَ عَمْرٌو: فِي كِتَابِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ بَيَاضٌ لَيْسُوا بِأَوْلِيَائِي، إِنَّمَا وَلِيِّيَ اللَّهُ وَصَالِحُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (5990) عن عمرو بن عباس، حدثنا محمد بن جعفر، حدثنا شعبة، عن إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن قيس بن أبي حازم، أن عمرو بن العاص قال (فذكره). ورواه مسلم في الإيمان (215) من طريق محمد بن جعفر، بإسناده.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موالاة المؤمنين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5990) and Muslim (215).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning Loyalty to the Believers","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say openly and not secretly: “The family of Abū so-and-so” — ʿAmr said that there is a blank at this point in the written copy of Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar — “are not my allies. Rather, my Protector is Allah and the righteous believers.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The meaning is that the Prophet’s true ally is whoever is righteous, even if his lineage is distant from him; while one who is unrighteous is not thereby his ally merely because his lineage is close."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5990)، ومسلم (215)."},{"num":128,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يُوشِكُ أَنْ يَكُونَ خَيْرَ مَالِ الْمُسْلِمِ غَنَمٌ، يَتْبَعُ بِهَا شَعَفَ الْجِبَالِ وَمَوَاقِعَ الْقَطْرِ، يَفِرُّ بِدِينِهِ مِنَ الْفِتَنِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الاستئذان (16) عن عبدالرحمن بن عبدالله بن عبدالرحمن بن أبي صعصعة، عن أبيه، عن أبي سعيد الخدريّ، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الفرار من الفتن من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Mālik (16) and al-Bukhārī (19).","chapter_en":"Fleeing From Tribulations Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The time is near when the best wealth of a Muslim will be sheep which he takes to the mountain peaks and places where rain falls, fleeing with his religion from tribulations.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15711],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (16)، والبخاري (19)."},{"num":129,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَيُّ النَّاسِ أَفْضَلُ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مُؤْمِنٌ يُجَاهِدُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ بِنَفْسِهِ وَمَالِهِ، قَالُوا: ثُمَّ مَنْ، قَالَ: مُؤْمِنٌ فِي شِعْبٍ مِنَ الشِّعَابِ يَتَّقِي اللَّهَ، وَيَدَعُ النَّاسَ مِنْ شَرِّهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الجهاد والسير (2786)، ومسلم في الإمارة (1888) كلاهما من طرق عن الزّهريّ، عن عطاء بن يزيد اللّيثيّ، عن أبي سعيد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الفرار من الفتن من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6494) and Muslim (1888).","chapter_en":"Fleeing From Tribulations Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?” He replied: “A believer who strives in the way of Allah with his life and his wealth.” They asked: “Then who?” He replied: “A believer living in one of the mountain passes, fearing Allah and keeping the people safe from his harm.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7742],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2786)، ومسلم (1888)."},{"num":130,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: مِنْ خَيْرِ مَعَاشِ النَّاسِ لَهُمْ رَجُلٌ مُمْسِكٌ عِنَانَ فَرَسِهِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، يَطِيرُ عَلَى مَتْنِهِ كُلَّمَا سَمِعَ هَيْعَةً أَوْ فَزْعَةً طَارَ عَلَيْهِ يَبْتَغِي الْقَتْلَ وَالْمَوْتَ مَظَانَّهُ أَوْ رَجُلٌ فِي غُنَيْمَةٍ فِي رَأْسِ شَعَفَةٍ مِنْ هَذِهِ الشَّعَفِ أَوْ بَطْنِ وَادٍ مِنْ هَذِهِ الْأَوْدِيَةِ يُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ، وَيُؤْتِي الزَّكَاةَ، وَيَعْبُدُ رَبَّهُ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَهُ الْيَقِينُ لَيْسَ مِنَ النَّاسِ إِلَّا فِي خَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإمارة (1889) عن يحيى بن يحيى التميميّ، حدّثنا عبدالعزيز بن أبي حازم، عن أبيه، عن بعجة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الفرار من الفتن من كمال الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (1889).","chapter_en":"Fleeing From Tribulations Is Part of the Perfection of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the best ways of life for people is that of a man holding the reins of his horse in the cause of Allah. Whenever he hears a cry of alarm or a call to battle, he flies upon its back, seeking death wherever it is expected. Or that of a man with a small flock of sheep upon one of these mountain peaks or in the depths of one of these valleys, establishing the prayer, giving zakāh, and worshipping his Lord until certainty comes to him. He mixes with people only in what is good.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1889)."},{"num":131,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اكْتُبُوا لِي مَنْ تَلَفَّظَ بِالْإِسْلَامِ مِنَ النَّاسِ فَكَتَبْنَا لَهُ أَلْفًا وَخَمْسَ مِائَةِ رَجُلٍ فَقُلْنَا نَخَافُ وَنَحْنُ أَلْفٌ وَخَمْسُ مِائَةٍ، فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا ابْتُلِينَا حَتَّى إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ لَيُصَلِّي وَحْدَهُ وَهُوَ خَائِفٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الجهاد (3060) عن محمد بن يوسف، حدثنا سفيان، عن الأعمش، عن أبي وائل، عن حذيفة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الاستسرار بالإيمان للخائف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3060).","chapter_en":"The Permissibility of Concealing One’s Faith for One Who Fears Harm","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Write down for me the names of those among the people who have professed Islam.” We recorded one thousand five hundred men for him. We said: “Should we be afraid when we number one thousand five hundred?” Yet I later saw us subjected to such trials that a man would pray alone while afraid."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim (149) narrated another wording in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:","“Count for me how many people profess Islam.”","We said:","“O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us when we number between six hundred and seven hundred?”","He replied:","“You do not know; perhaps you will be put to trial.”","Ḥudhayfah said:","And indeed we were tried, until a man among us would pray only in secret."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3060)."},{"num":132,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَتَى الْمَقْبُرَةَ فَقَالَ: السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ دَارَ قَوْمٍ مُؤْمِنِينَ، وَإِنَّا إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ بِكُمْ لَاحِقُونَ، وَدِدْتُ أَنَّا قَدْ رَأَيْنَا إِخْوَانَنَا، قَالُوا: أَوَلَسْنَا إِخْوَانَكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: أَنْتُمْ أَصْحَابِي، وَإِخْوَانُنَا الَّذِينَ لَمْ يَأْتُوا بَعْدُ، فَقَالُوا: كَيْفَ تَعْرِفُ مَنْ لَمْ يَأْتِ بَعْدُ مِنْ أُمَّتِكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ فَقَالَ: أَرَأَيْتَ لَوْ أَنَّ رَجُلًا لَهُ خَيْلٌ غُرٌّ، مُحَجَّلَةٌ بَيْنَ ظَهْرَيْ خَيْلٍ دُهْمٍ بُهْمٍ، أَلَا يَعْرِفُ خَيْلَهُ؟ قَالُوا: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: فَإِنَّهُمْ يَأْتُونَ غُرًّا، مُحَجَّلِينَ مِنَ الْوُضُوءِ، وَأَنَا فَرَطُهُمْ عَلَى الْحَوْضِ، أَلَا لَيُذَادَنَّ رِجَالٌ عَنْ حَوْضِي، كَمَا يُذَادُ الْبَعِيرُ الضَّالُّ أُنَادِيهِمْ، أَلَا هَلُمَّ؟ فَيُقَالُ: إِنَّهُمْ قَدْ بَدَّلُوا بَعْدَكَ، فَأَقُولُ: سُحْقًا سُحْقًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطهارة (249) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن جعفر، أخبرني العلاء، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الاستثناء في الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (249).","chapter_en":"Making an Exception When Speaking About One’s Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the graveyard and said: “Peace be upon you, dwelling place of believing people. Indeed, if Allah wills, we will join you. I wish that we had seen our brothers.” They asked: “Are we not your brothers, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You are my Companions. Our brothers are those who have not yet come.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those from your Ummah who have not yet come?” He replied: “Suppose a man owned horses with bright white markings on their foreheads and legs among completely black horses. Would he not recognize his own horses?” They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “They will come with their faces and limbs shining from the effects of wuḍūʾ, and I will precede them to the Ḥawḍ. Indeed, some men will be driven away from my Ḥawḍ just as a stray camel is driven away. I will call to them: ‘Come! Come!’ But it will be said: ‘They changed after you.’ So I will say: ‘Away with them! Away with them!’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Sufyān said:","“Whoever dislikes saying, ‘I am a believer, if Allah wills,’ is, according to us, a Murjiʾ.”","A man asked ʿAlqamah:","“Are you a believer?”","He replied:","“I hope so, if Allah wills.”","Al-Bayhaqī said in Shuʿab al-Īmān (1/83):","“We have narrated this from a group of the Companions, the Tābiʿūn, and the righteous early generations, may Allah be pleased with them all.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الأوزاعي رحمه الله:","قال الله تعالى:","﴿لَتَدْخُلُنَّ الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللهُ آمِنِينَ﴾","[الفتح: ٢٧]","قال:","قد علم الله تعالى أنهم سيدخلون، وقد قال:","﴿إِنْ شَاءَ اللهُ﴾."],"en":["Al-Awzāʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said:","Allah Most High said:","“You will surely enter al-Masjid al-Ḥarām, if Allah wills, in safety.”","[Sūrat al-Fatḥ 48:27]","Allah already knew that they would enter it, yet He nevertheless said:","“If Allah wills.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[819],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (249)."},{"num":133,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مَالِكٍ الأَشْعَرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الطُّهُورُ شَطْرُ الإِيمَانِ، وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ تَمْلَأُ الْمِيزَانَ، وَسُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ تَمْلَآَنِ أَوْ تَمْلَأُ مَا بَيْنَ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ، وَالصَّلَاةُ نُورٌ، وَالصَّدَقَةُ بُرْهَانٌ، وَالصَّبْرُ ضِيَاءٌ، وَالْقُرْآنُ حُجَّةٌ لَكَ أَوْ عَلَيْكَ، كُلُّ النَّاسِ يَغْدُو، فَبَائِعٌ نَفْسَهُ فَمُعْتِقُهَا أَوْ مُوبِقُهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطّهارة (223) عن إسحاق بن منصور، حدثنا حبان ابن هلال، حدثنا أبان، حدثنا يحيى، أنّ زيداً حدّثه، أنّ أبا سلاّم حدّثه، عن أبي مالك الأشعريّ قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الطهور شطر الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (223).","chapter_en":"Purification Is Half of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purification is half of faith. ‘Al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fills the Scale. ‘Subḥān Allāh’ and ‘al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fill — or together fill — what lies between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is illumination, and the Qurʾān is an argument either for you or against you. Every person goes out in the morning and sells his own soul, either setting it free or bringing about its destruction.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[1557],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (223)."},{"num":134,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سُفْيَانَ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الثَّقَفِيِّ قَالَ: قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! قُلْ لِي فِي الإِسْلَامِ قَوْلًا لَا أَسْأَلُ عَنْهُ أَحَدًا بَعْدَكَ، وَفِي حَدِيثِ أَبِي أُسَامَةَ: غَيْرَكَ، قَالَ: قُلْ آمَنْتُ بِاللَّهِ فَاسْتَقِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (38) من طرق عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن سفيان بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من آمن بالله ثم استقام عليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (38).","chapter_en":"Whoever Believes in Allah and Then Remains Steadfast","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sufyān ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Thaqafī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me something concerning Islam about which I will not need to ask anyone after you.” He replied: “Say: ‘I believe in Allah,’ then remain steadfast.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (38)."},{"num":135,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَيْنَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ رَأَيْتُ النَّاسَ يُعْرَضُونَ عَلَيَّ، وَعَلَيْهِمْ قُمُصٌ مِنْهَا مَا يَبْلُغُ الثُّدِيَّ وَمِنْهَا مَا دُونَ ذَلِكَ، وَعُرِضَ عَلَيَّ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ وَعَلَيْهِ قَمِيصٌ يَجُرُّهُ، قَالُوا: فَمَا أَوَّلْتَ ذَلِكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: الدِّينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (23)، ومسلم في الفضائل (2390) كلاهما عن إبراهيم بن سعد، عن صالح بن كيسان، عن ابن شهاب، عن أبي أمامة ابن سهل، أنه سمع أبا سعيد الخدريّ، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تفاضل أهل الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (23) and Muslim (2390).","chapter_en":"The Different Levels of the People of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While I was sleeping, I saw the people being presented before me wearing shirts. Some of the shirts reached the chest, while others were shorter than that. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was presented before me wearing a shirt so long that he was dragging it.” They asked: “How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Religion.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (23)، ومسلم (2390)."},{"num":136,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ هَانِئِ بْنِ هَانِئٍ قَالَ: دَخَلَ عَمَّارٌ عَلَى عَلِيٍّ فَقَالَ: مَرْحَبًا بِالطَّيِّبِ الْمُطَيَّبِ، سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: مُلِئَ عَمَّارٌ إِيمَانًا إِلَى مُشَاشِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (147) حدثنا نصر بن علي الجهضميّ، قال: حدثنا عثَّام بن علي، عن الأعمش، عن أبي إسحاق، عن هانئ بن هانئ، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تفاضل أهل الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (147), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7076), and narrated by al-Nasāʾī (5007).","chapter_en":"The Different Levels of the People of Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hāniʾ ibn Hāniʾ reported: ʿAmmār may Allah be pleased with him entered upon ʿAlī may Allah be pleased with him, and ʿAlī said: “Welcome to the good and purified one.” I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “ʿAmmār has been filled with faith to the very ends of his bones.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression «إلى مشاشه» refers to the extremities or heads of his bones, emphasizing the strength and fullness of his faith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10285],"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (147)، وصححه ابن حبان (7076)، والنسائي (5007)."},{"num":137,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: أَشَارَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ نَحْوَ الْيَمَنِ فَقَالَ: الْإِيمَانُ يَمَانٍ هَا هُنَا أَلَا إِنَّ الْقَسْوَةَ وَغِلَظَ الْقُلُوبِ فِي الْفَدَّادِينَ عِنْدَ أُصُولِ أَذْنَابِ الْإِبِلِ حَيْثُ يَطْلُعُ قَرْنَا الشَّيْطَانِ فِي رَبِيعَةَ وَمُضَرَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في بدء الخلق (3302)، ومسلم في الإيمان (51) كلاهما من حديث إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، قال: سمعتُ قيساً يروي عن عقبة بن عمرو أبي مسعود، قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رجحان أهل اليمن في الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3302) and Muslim (51).","chapter_en":"The Excellence of the People of Yemen in Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet ﷺ pointed with his hand toward Yemen and said: “Faith is toward Yemen, here. Indeed, harshness and hard-heartedness are among the loud-voiced people by the bases of camels’ tails, where the two horns of Satan rise, among Rabīʿah and Muḍar.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The term al-faddādīn, with the doubled dāl, is the plural of faddād and is derived from a word denoting a loud, intense sound. It refers to those who raise their voices loudly around their camels, horses, cultivated lands, and similar possessions.","The expression “near the bases of the tails of camels” refers to those who make noise and commotion while driving them.","The words “where the two horns of Satan rise, among Rabīʿah and Muḍar” indicate that Rabīʿah and Muḍar identify the people described as al-faddādīn in this context.","“The two horns of Satan” refers literally to the two sides of his head. What is intended is the particular prevalence in the east of Satanic influence and disbelief, as stated in another ḥadīth:","“The head of disbelief is toward the east.”","This referred to circumstances existing during the time of the Prophet ﷺ when he made the statement, and it will also be manifested when the Dajjāl emerges from the east.","This is abridged from the discussion of Ibn al-Ṣalāḥ in Ṣiyānat Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3302)، ومسلم (51)."},{"num":138,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: الْفَخْرُ وَالْخُيَلَاءُ فِي الْفَدَّادِينَ أَهْلِ الْوَبَرِ وَالسَّكِينَةُ فِي أَهْلِ الْغَنَمِ وَالْإِيمَانُ يَمَانٍ وَالْحِكْمَةُ يَمَانِيَةٌ...(فَذَكَرَ الْحَدِيثَ)."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المناقب (3499) عن أبي اليمان، أخبرنا شعيب، عن الزهريّ، قال: أخبرني أبو سلمة بن عبدالرحمن، أن أبا هريرة قال (فذكر الحديث).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رجحان أهل اليمن في الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3499) and Muslim (52).","chapter_en":"The Excellence of the People of Yemen in Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Pride and arrogance are found among the loud desert people who dwell among camels; tranquility is found among the people of sheep. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration:","“Pride and arrogance are among the owners of camels, while tranquility and dignity are among the owners of sheep.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3499)، ومسلم (52)."},{"num":139,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَتَاكُمْ أَهْلُ الْيَمَنِ هُمْ أَرَقُّ أَفْئِدَةً وَأَلْيَنُ قُلُوبًا، الْإِيمَانُ يَمَانٍ، وَالْحِكْمَةُ يَمَانِيَةٌ، وَالْفَخْرُ وَالْخُيَلَاءُ فِي أَصْحَابِ الْإِبِلِ، وَالسَّكِينَةُ وَالْوَقَارُ فِي أَهْلِ الْغَنَمِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازي (4388)، ومسلم في الإيمان (52) كلاهما من طرق عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رجحان أهل اليمن في الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4388) and Muslim (52).","chapter_en":"The Excellence of the People of Yemen in Faith","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Yemen have come to you. They are the most tender in heart and the gentlest in disposition. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. Pride and arrogance are among the owners of camels, while tranquility and dignity are among the people of sheep.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration found in both collections:","“The people of Yemen have come to you. They are the most tender in heart and the weakest in heart.”","In another narration recorded by al-Bukhārī (4389):","“Tribulation is here; here is where the horn of Satan rises.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4388)، ومسلم (52)."},{"num":140,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: غِلَظُ الْقُلُوبِ، وَالْجَفَاءُ فِي الْمَشْرِقِ، وَالإِيمَانُ فِي أَهْلِ الْحِجَازِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (53) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم، أخبرنا عبدالله بن الحارث المخزوميّ، عن ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الإيمان في أهل الحجاز","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (53).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Faith Is Among the People of the Ḥijāz","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hardness of heart and roughness are in the east, while faith is among the people of the Ḥijāz.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[10547],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (53)."},{"num":141,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا أَحْسَنَ أَحَدُكُمْ إِسْلَامَهُ فَكُلُّ حَسَنَةٍ يَعْمَلُهَا تُكْتَبُ لَهُ بِعَشْرِ أَمْثَالِهَا إِلَى سَبْعِ مِائَةِ ضِعْفٍ، وَكُلُّ سَيِّئَةٍ يَعْمَلُهَا تُكْتَبُ لَهُ بِمِثْلِهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (42)، ومسلم في الإيمان (129) كلاهما من حديث عبدالرزاق، قال: أخبرنا معمر، عن همام، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حسن إسلام المرء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (42) and Muslim (129).","chapter_en":"A Person’s Good Practice of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you perfects his practice of Islam, every good deed he performs is recorded for him as ten times its like, up to seven hundred times, while every bad deed he commits is recorded as only one like it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (42)، ومسلم (129)."},{"num":142,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى الِلَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ مِنْ حُسْنِ إِسْلامِ الْمَرْءِ تَرْكُهُ مَا لا يَعْنِيهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (2317)، وابن ماجه (3976)، وابن حبان في صحيحه (229) كلّهم من طريق الأوزاعيّ، عن قرة بن عبدالرحمن، عن الزهريّ، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حسن إسلام المرء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2317), Ibn Mājah (3976), and Ibn Ḥibbān in his Ṣaḥīḥ (229).","chapter_en":"A Person’s Good Practice of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Part of the excellence of a person’s Islam is that he leaves what does not concern him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2317)، وابن ماجه (3976)، وابن حبان في صحيحه (229)."},{"num":143,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا أَسْلَمَ الْعَبْدُ فَحَسُنَ إِسْلَامُهُ كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَهُ كُلَّ حَسَنَةٍ كَانَ أَزْلَفَهَا، وَمُحِيَتْ عَنْهُ كُلُّ سَيِّئَةٍ كَانَ أَزْلَفَهَا، ثُمَّ كَانَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ الْقِصَاصُ، الْحَسَنَةُ بِعَشْرَةِ أَمْثَالِهَا إِلَى سَبْعِ مِائَةِ ضِعْفٍ، وَالسَّيِّئَةُ بِمِثْلِهَا إِلَّا أَنْ يَتَجَاوَزَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَنْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (4998) عن احمد بن المعلَّى بن زيد، قال: حدثنا صفوان بن صالح، قال: حدثنا الوليد قال: حدثنا مالك، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن عطاء بن يسار، عن أبي سعيد الخدري فذكر مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حسن إسلام المرء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Nasāʾī (4998).","chapter_en":"A Person’s Good Practice of Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a servant embraces Islam and his Islam becomes good, Allah records for him every good deed that he had previously done, and every bad deed that he had previously committed is erased. Thereafter comes recompense: a good deed is multiplied tenfold up to seven hundred times, while a bad deed is recorded as one like it, unless Allah, Mighty and Majestic, pardons it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[177],"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (4998)."},{"num":144,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَرِيرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: بَايَعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى إِقَامِ الصَّلَاةِ، وَإِيتَاءِ الزَّكَاةِ، وَالنُّصْحِ لِكُلِّ مُسْلِمٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (57)، ومسلم في الإيمان (56) كلاهما من حديث إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن قيس، عن جرير، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن النصيحة عماد الدين وقوامه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (57) and Muslim (56).","chapter_en":"Sincere Counsel Is the Pillar and Foundation of the Religion","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to establish the prayer, give zakāh, and offer sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī (7204) and Muslim also narrated the wording:","“I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ to hear and obey” — and he instructed me to say, “as much as I am able” — “and to offer sincere counsel to every Muslim.”","Al-Bukhārī (58) also narrated that Jarīr, may Allah be pleased with him, said:","“You must fear Allah alone, without partner, and maintain dignity and tranquility until your governor comes to you, for he is about to arrive.”","Then he said:","“Ask Allah to pardon your governor, for he used to love pardoning.”","Then he said:","“To proceed: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ‘I pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.’ He stipulated upon me:","‘And sincere counsel to every Muslim.’","So I pledged allegiance to him upon that. By the Lord of this mosque, I am indeed a sincere adviser to you.”","Then he sought forgiveness and descended."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1732],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (57)، ومسلم (56)."},{"num":145,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ تَمِيمٍ الدَّارِيِّ، أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: الدِّينُ النَّصِيحَةُ، قُلْنَا: لِمَنْ؟ قَالَ: لِلَّهِ وَلِكِتَابِهِ، وَلِرَسُولِهِ وَلِأَئِمَّةِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَعَامَّتِهِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (55) عن محمد بن عبّاد المكيّ، حدثنا سفيان (هو ابن عيينة)، قال: قلت لسهيل: إنّ عمراً (يعني ابن دينار) حدّثنا عن القعقاع، عن أبيك. قال: ورجوتُ أن يُسقط عنّي رجلاً. قال: فقال: سمعتُه من الذي سمعه منه أبي كان صديقاً له بالشّام. ثم حدّثنا سفيان، عن سهيل، عن عطاء بن يزيد، عن تميم الدّاريّ، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن النصيحة عماد الدين وقوامه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (55).","chapter_en":"Sincere Counsel Is the Pillar and Foundation of the Religion","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Tamīm al-Dārī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The religion is sincere counsel.” We asked: “To whom?” He replied: “To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[7672],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (55)."},{"num":146,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْمُسَيِّبِ بْنِ حَزْنِ قَالَ: لَمَّا حَضَرَ أَبَا طَالِبٍ الْوَفَاةُ، دَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعِنْدَهُ أَبُو جَهْلٍ، وَعَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ أَبِي أُمَيَّةَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَيْ عَمِّ، قُلْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ أُحَاجُّ لَكَ بِهَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ، فَقَالَ أَبُو جَهْلٍ وَعَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ أَبِي أُمَيَّةَ: يَا أَبَا طَالِبٍ، أَتَرْغَبُ عَنْ مِلَّةِ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَأَسْتَغْفِرَنَّ لَكَ مَا لَمْ أُنْهَ عَنْكَ، فَنَزَلَتْ: ﴿مَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوا لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ وَلَوْ كَانُوا أُولِي قُرْبَى مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ أَنَّهُمْ أَصْحَابُ الْجَحِيمِ﴾ [سورة التوبة: 113]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4675)، ومسلم في الإيمان (24 ، 40) كلاهما عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم، حدثنا عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهريّ، عن شعيب بن المسيب، عن أبيه، فذكره، واللّفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الدليل على صحة إسلام من حضره الموت ما لم يشرع في النزع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4675) and Muslim (24), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"Evidence That the Islam of One Near Death Is Valid So Long as the Final Agony Has Not Begun","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Musayyib ibn Ḥazn, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: When death approached Abū Ṭālib, the Prophet ﷺ entered upon him while Abū Jahl and ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Umayyah were with him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O my uncle, say: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ a statement with which I may plead for you before Allah.” Abū Jahl and ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Umayyah said: “O Abū Ṭālib, will you abandon the religion of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?” They continued speaking to him until his final words were that he remained upon the religion of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he refused to say, “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I will continue to seek forgiveness for you unless I am forbidden from doing so.” Then Allah revealed: “It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they are close relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are inhabitants of the Hellfire.” [Sūrat al-Tawbah 9:113]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4675)، ومسلم (24)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":147,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعَمِّهِ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ: قُلْ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، أَشْهَدُ لَكَ بِهَا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فَأَبَى، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ:﴿إِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ﴾ [سورة القصص: 56]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (25) من طرق عن مروان، عن يزيد بن كيسان، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الدليل على صحة إسلام من حضره الموت ما لم يشرع في النزع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (25).","chapter_en":"Evidence That the Islam of One Near Death Is Valid So Long as the Final Agony Has Not Begun","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: At the time of his uncle’s death, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Say: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ so that I may testify for you by it on the Day of Resurrection.” But he refused. Allah Most High then revealed: “Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those who are guided.” [Sūrat al-Qaṣaṣ 28:56]"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated through another route that Abū Ṭālib said:","“Were it not that Quraysh would reproach me and say, ‘It was only fear that drove him to say it,’ I would certainly have delighted your eyes by saying it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (25)."},{"num":148,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ أَخْبَرَ أَنَّ أبَا سُفْيَانَ بْنُ حَرْبٍ أَخْبَرَهُ، أَنَّ هِرَقْلَ قَالَ لَهُ: سَأَلْتُكَ، هَلْ يَزِيدُونَ أَمْ يَنْقُصُونَ؟ فَزَعَمْتَ أَنَّهُمْ يَزِيدُونَ، وَكَذَلِكَ الْإِيمَانُ حَتَّى يَتِمَّ، وَسَأَلْتُكَ، هَلْ يَرْتَدُّ أَحَدٌ سَخْطَةً لِدِينِهِ بَعْدَ أَنْ يَدْخُلَ فِيهِ؟ فَزَعَمْتَ أَنْ لَا، وَكَذَلِكَ الْإِيمَانُ حِينَ تُخَالِطُ بَشَاشَتُهُ الْقُلُوبَ لَا يَسْخَطُهُ أَحَدٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (51) عن إبراهيم بن حمزة، قال: حدثنا إبراهيم بن سعد، عن صالح، عن ابن شهاب، عن عبيد الله بن عبدالله، أن ابن عباس أخبره عن أبي سفيان، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإيمان إذا خالطت بشاشته القلوب لا يسخطه أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (51) and Muslim (1773).","chapter_en":"When the Joy of Faith Enters the Hearts, No One Becomes Displeased With It","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":37,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them reported that Abū Sufyān informed him that Heraclius said to him: “I asked you whether their numbers were increasing or decreasing, and you said that they were increasing. That is the nature of faith until it becomes complete. I also asked you whether anyone, after entering this religion, turns away from it out of dissatisfaction with it, and you said no. Such is faith: once its delight enters and mingles with the hearts, no one becomes displeased with it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (51)، ومسلم (1773)."},{"num":149,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ الدِّينَ يُسْرٌ، وَلَنْ يُشَادَّ الدِّينَ أَحَدٌ إِلَّا غَلَبَهُ، فَسَدِّدُوا وَقَارِبُوا وَأَبْشِرُوا وَاسْتَعِينُوا بِالْغَدْوَةِ وَالرَّوْحَةِ وَشَيْءٍ مِنَ الدُّلْجَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (39) عن عبدالسلام بن مطهّر، حدّثنا عمر بن عليّ، عن معن بن محمد الغفاريّ، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبريّ، عن أبي هريرة، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من خصال هذا الدين أنه يسر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (39).","chapter_en":"From the Qualities of This Religion Is That It Is Ease","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the religion is ease. No one makes the religion excessively difficult upon himself except that it overwhelms him. So remain upright, come as close as you can to what is right, receive glad tidings, and seek assistance through worship in the morning, the evening, and during a portion of the night.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement:","“No one makes the religion excessively difficult upon himself except that it overwhelms him”","means that no one goes to extremes in religious deeds and abandons gentleness except that he eventually becomes incapable, breaks off, and is overcome."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14711,15282],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (39)."},{"num":150,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَال: لَمَّا نَزَلَتْ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:﴿لِلَّهِ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا مَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ يُحَاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللَّهُ فَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشَاءُ وَاللَّهُ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 284]. قَالَ: فَاشْتَدَّ ذَلِكَ عَلَى أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَتَوْا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ بَرَكُوا عَلَى الرُّكَبِ، فَقَالُوا: أَيْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ كُلِّفْنَا مِنَ الأَعْمَالِ مَا نُطِيقُ، الصَّلَاةُ، وَالصِّيَامُ، وَالْجِهَادُ، وَالصَّدَقَةُ، وَقَدْ أُنْزِلَتْ عَلَيْكَ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ وَلَا نُطِيقُهَا، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَقُولُوا كَمَا قَالَ أَهْلُ الْكِتَابَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ: سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا، بَلْ قُولُوا: سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا غُفْرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا، وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ، قَالُوا: سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا غُفْرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا، وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ، فَلَمَّا اقْتَرَأَهَا الْقَوْمُ ذَلَّتْ بِهَا أَلْسِنَتُهُمْ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ فِي إِثْرِهَا: ﴿آمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِمَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَبِّهِ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ كُلٌّ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْ رُسُلِهِ وَقَالُوا سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا غُفْرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ﴾ [البقرة: 285]. فَلَمَّا فَعَلُوا ذَلِكَ، نَسَخَهَا اللَّهُ تَعَالَى، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿لَا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَعَلَيْهَا مَا اكْتَسَبَتْ رَبَّنَا لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَا إِنْ نَسِينَا أَوْ أَخْطَأْنَا﴾ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. ﴿رَبَّنَا وَلَا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَا إِصْرًا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا﴾ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. ﴿رَبَّنَا وَلَا تُحَمِّلْنَا مَا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا بِهِ وَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا أَنْتَ مَوْلَانَا فَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 286] قَالَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (125) من طرق عن يزيد بن زريع، حدثنا روح (هو ابن القاسم)، عن العلاء، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله سبحانه وتعالى لا يكلف إلا ما يطاق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (125).","chapter_en":"Allah, Glorified and Exalted, Does Not Burden a Soul Beyond What It Can Bear","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: When the following verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Whether you disclose what is within yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it. Then He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills, and Allah is over all things powerful.” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:284] This weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They came to him, knelt down, and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have been charged with deeds that we are capable of performing: prayer, fasting, jihād, and charity. But now this verse has been revealed to you, and we are unable to bear it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you wish to say as the People of the two Scriptures before you said: ‘We hear and we disobey’? Rather, say: ‘We hear and we obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the final return.’” They said: “We hear and we obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the final return.” When the people recited these words and their tongues became accustomed and submissive to them, Allah revealed immediately afterward: “The Messenger believes in what has been revealed to him from his Lord, and so do the believers. Each believes in Allah, His angels, His Books, and His messengers. We make no distinction between any of His messengers. And they say: ‘We hear and we obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the final return.’” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:285] When they responded in this manner, Allah Most High relieved them of the earlier burden and revealed: “Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity. It will have the good that it has earned, and it will bear the evil that it has earned. Our Lord, do not take us to account if we forget or make a mistake.” Allah said: “Yes.” “Our Lord, do not place upon us a burden like that which You placed upon those before us.” Allah said: “Yes.” “Our Lord, do not burden us with what we have no strength to bear. Pardon us, forgive us, and have mercy upon us. You are our Protector, so grant us victory over the disbelieving people.” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:286] Allah said: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (125)."},{"num":151,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: لَمَّا نَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ ﴿وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا مَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ يُحَاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللَّهُ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 284] قَالَ: دَخَلَ قُلُوبَهُمْ مِنْهَا شَيْءٌ، لَمْ يَدْخُلْ قُلُوبَهُمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قُولُوا سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا وَسَلَّمْنَا، قَالَ: فَأَلْقَى اللَّهُ الإِيمَانَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿لَا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَعَلَيْهَا مَا اكْتَسَبَتْ رَبَّنَا لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَا إِنْ نَسِينَا أَوْ أَخْطَأْنَا﴾ قَالَ: قَدْ فَعَلْتُ. ﴿رَبَّنَا وَلَا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَا إِصْرًا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا﴾ قَالَ: قَدْ فَعَلْتُ. ﴿وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا أَنْتَ مَوْلَانَا﴾ [سورة البقرة: 286] قَالَ: قَدْ فَعَلْتُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (126) من طرق عن وكيع، عن سفيان، عن آدم بن سليمان مولى خالد، قال: سمعتُ سعيد بن جبير يحدِّث عن ابن عباس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله سبحانه وتعالى لا يكلف إلا ما يطاق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (126).","chapter_en":"Allah, Glorified and Exalted, Does Not Burden a Soul Beyond What It Can Bear","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: When the verse was revealed: “Whether you disclose what is within yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it.” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:284] something entered their hearts because of it unlike anything that had entered their hearts before. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: ‘We hear, we obey, and we submit.’” Ibn ʿAbbās said: Then Allah placed faith firmly within their hearts and revealed: “Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity. It will have what it has earned, and it will bear what it has earned. Our Lord, do not take us to account if we forget or make a mistake.” Allah said: “I have done so.” “Our Lord, do not place upon us a burden like that which You placed upon those before us.” Allah said: “I have done so.” “Pardon us, forgive us, and have mercy upon us. You are our Protector.” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:286] Allah said: “I have done so.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression:","“Something entered their hearts because of it”","means because of this verse; that is, a tremendous weight of grief and concern entered their hearts because of it.","The expression:","“Unlike anything that had entered their hearts before”","means that nothing before this had affected their hearts in the same manner."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (126)."},{"num":152,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: يَخْرُجُ مِنَ النَّارِ أَرْبَعَةٌ، فَيُعْرَضُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ، فَيَلْتَفِتُ أَحَدُهُمْ، فَيَقُولُ: أَيْ رَبِّ، إِذْ أَخْرَجْتَنِي مِنْهَا فَلَا تُعِدْنِي فِيهَا، فَيُنْجِيهِ اللَّهُ مِنْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (192) عن هدّاب بن خالد الأزديّ، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن أبي عمران وثابت، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حسن الظن بالله مقروناً بالخوف والرجاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (192).","chapter_en":"Having Good Expectations of Allah Along With Fear and Hope","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four people will be brought out of the Fire and presented before Allah. One of them will turn back and say: ‘My Lord, since You have brought me out of it, do not return me to it.’ So Allah will save him from it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[75,16189,16472],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (192)."},{"num":153,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَخْرُجُ رَجُلانِ مِنَ النَّارِ، فَيُعْرَضَانِ عَلَى اللَّهِ، ثُمَّ يُؤْمَرُ بِهِمَا إِلَى النَّارِ، فَيَلْتَفِتُ أَحَدُهُمَا فَيَقُولُ: يَا رَبِّ مَا كَانَ هَذَا رَجَائِي! قَالَ: وَمَا كَانَ رَجَاؤُكَ؟ قَالَ: كَانَ رَجَائِي إِذْ أَخْرَجْتَنِي مِنْهَا، أَنْ لا تُعِيدَنِي، فَيَرْحَمُهُ اللَّهُ فَيُدْخِلُهُ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (632) عن الحسن بن سفيان، قال: حدثنا هدبة بن خالد القيسيّ، قال: حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن أنس بن مالك، فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حسن الظن بالله مقروناً بالخوف والرجاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (632).","chapter_en":"Having Good Expectations of Allah Along With Fear and Hope","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two men will be brought out of the Fire and presented before Allah. Then they will be ordered back toward the Fire. One of them will turn and say: ‘My Lord, this was not what I hoped from You!’ Allah will say: ‘What did you hope for?’ He will reply: ‘My hope was that, once You had brought me out of it, You would not return me to it.’ So Allah will have mercy upon him and admit him into Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (632)."},{"num":154,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ جَلَّ وَعَلا يَقُولُ: أَنَا عِنْدَ ظَنِّ عَبْدِي بِي، إِنْ ظَنَّ خَيْرًا فَلَهُ، وَإِنْ ظَنَّ شَرًّا فَلَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (639) عن عبدالله بن محمد بن سلم، قال: حدثنا حرملة بن يحيى، قال: حدثنا ابن وهب، قال: أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث، وذكر ابن سلم آخر معه، ، أنّ أبا يونس حدّثهم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حسن الظن بالله مقروناً بالخوف والرجاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (639) and Aḥmad (9076).","chapter_en":"Having Good Expectations of Allah Along With Fear and Hope","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Majestic and Exalted, says: ‘I am as My servant expects Me to be. If he expects good, then he will have it; and if he expects evil, then he will have it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (639)، وأحمد (9076)."},{"num":155,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْوِي عَنْ رَبِّهِ جَلَّ وَعَلا، قَالَ: وَعِزَّتِي لا أَجْمَعُ عَلَى عَبْدِي خَوْفَيْنِ وَأَمْنَيْنِ، إِذَا خَافَنِي فِي الدُّنْيَا أَمَّنْتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، وَإِذَا أَمِنَنِي فِي الدُّنْيَا أَخَفْتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (640) عن الحسن بن سفيان، قال: حدثنا إبراهيم بن يعقوب الجوزجانيّ، حدثنا عبدالوهاب بن عطاء، حدثنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حسن الظن بالله مقروناً بالخوف والرجاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (640) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3232, 3233).","chapter_en":"Having Good Expectations of Allah Along With Fear and Hope","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ narrated from his Lord, Majestic and Exalted, that He said: “By My Might, I will not combine for My servant two states of fear and two states of security. If he fears Me in this world, I will grant him security on the Day of Resurrection; and if he feels secure from Me in this world, I will make him afraid on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (640)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (3232، 3233)."},{"num":156,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ حُسْنَ الظَّنِّ بِاللَّهِ مِنْ حُسْنِ عِبَادَةِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4993)، والترمذي (5 ، 3604)، وأحمد (7956)، وابن حبان (631)، كلهم من طرق عن محمد بن واسع، عن سُمير، أو شُتير، ابن نهار العبدي عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حسن الظن بالله مقروناً بالخوف والرجاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4993), al-Tirmidhī (3604), Aḥmad (7956), and Ibn Ḥibbān (631).","chapter_en":"Having Good Expectations of Allah Along With Fear and Hope","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, having good expectations of Allah is part of excellent worship of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4993)، والترمذي (3604)، وأحمد (7956)، وابن حبان (631)."},{"num":157,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ الْعَلَاءِ امْرَأَةً مِنْ الْأَنْصَارِ بَايَعَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَخْبَرَتْهُ أَنَّهُ اقْتُسِمَ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ قُرْعَةً فَطَارَ لَنَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ مَظْعُونٍ فَأَنْزَلْنَاهُ فِي أَبْيَاتِنَا، فَوَجِعَ وَجَعَهُ الَّذِي تُوُفِّيَ فِيهِ فَلَمَّا تُوُفِّيَ وَغُسِّلَ وَكُفِّنَ فِي أَثْوَابِهِ دَخَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: رَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ أَبَا السَّائِبِ فَشَهَادَتِي عَلَيْكَ لَقَدْ أَكْرَمَكَ اللَّهُ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَمَا يُدْرِيكِ أَنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَكْرَمَهُ ؟ فَقُلْتُ: بِأَبِي أَنْتَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَمَنْ يُكْرِمُهُ اللَّهُ ؟، فَقَالَ: أَمَّا هُوَ فَقَدْ جَاءَهُ الْيَقِينُ، وَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لَأَرْجُو لَهُ الْخَيْرَ وَاللَّهِ مَا أَدْرِي وَأَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ مَا يُفْعَلُ بِي، قَالَتْ: فَوَاللَّهِ لَا أُزَكِّي أَحَدًا بَعْدَهُ أَبَدًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الجنائز (1243) عن يحيى بن بكير، حدثنا الليث، عن عُقيل، عن ابن شهاب، قال: أخبرني خارجة بن زيد بن ثابت أنّ أم العلاء ذكرت الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الخوف والتقوى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1243).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning Fear and God-Consciousness","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm al-ʿAlāʾ may Allah be pleased with her, a woman of the Anṣār who had pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, reported: The Muhājirūn were distributed among the Anṣār by drawing lots, and ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn fell to our share. We accommodated him in our homes, and he became afflicted with the illness from which he eventually died. When he died, had been washed, and was wrapped in his burial shrouds, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered. I said: “May Allah have mercy upon you, O Abū al-Sāʾib. My testimony concerning you is that Allah has certainly honored you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “How do you know that Allah has honored him?” I said: “May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. Then whom will Allah honor?” He replied: “As for him, certainty — death — has come to him. By Allah, I certainly hope for good for him. Yet by Allah, I do not know, even though I am the Messenger of Allah, what will be done with me.” She said: “By Allah, after that I never again declared anyone with certainty to be righteous before Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1243)."},{"num":158,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيَّ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنَّ رَجُلًا كَانَ قَبْلَكُمْ رَغَسَهُ اللَّهُ مَالًا، فَقَالَ: لِبَنِيهِ لَمَّا حُضِرَ أَيَّ أَبٍ كُنْتُ لَكُمْ، قَالُوا: خَيْرَ أَبٍ، قَالَ: فَإِنِّي لَمْ أَعْمَلْ خَيْرًا قَطُّ فَإِذَا مُتُّ فَأَحْرِقُونِي ثُمَّ اسْحَقُونِي ثُمَّ ذَرُّونِي فِي يَوْمٍ عَاصِفٍ فَفَعَلُوا فَجَمَعَهُ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فَقَالَ: مَا حَمَلَكَ، قَالَ: مَخَافَتُكَ، فَتَلَقَّاهُ بِرَحْمَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في أحاديث الأنبياء (3478)، ومسلم في التوبة (2757) كلاهما من حديث أبي الوليد، حدثنا أبو عوانة، عن قتادة، عن عقبة بن عبدالغافر، عن أبي سعيد، فذكر الحديث، واللفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن رحمة الله أوسع من عذابه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3478) and Muslim (2757).","chapter_en":"Allah’s Mercy Is More Vast Than His Punishment","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There was a man among those before you whom Allah had granted abundant wealth. When death approached him, he said to his sons: ‘What kind of father have I been to you?’ They replied: ‘The best of fathers.’ He said: ‘I have never performed any good deed. When I die, burn me, then crush me thoroughly, and afterward scatter me on a violently windy day.’ They did so. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gathered him and asked: ‘What caused you to do this?’ He replied: ‘Fear of You.’ So Allah received him with His mercy.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression «رغسه الله مالاً» means that Allah gave him abundant wealth and placed blessing in it. The word al-raghs denotes blessing, growth, and abundant good.","The expression «اسحقوني» means: crush or grind me extremely finely."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3478)، ومسلم (2757)."},{"num":159,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَجُلٌ لَمْ يَعْمَلْ حَسَنَةً قَطُّ لِأَهْلِهِ إِذَا مَاتَ فَحَرِّقُوهُ ثُمَّ أَذْرُوا نِصْفَهُ فِي الْبَرِّ وَنِصْفَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ، فَوَاللَّهِ لَئِنْ قَدَرَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ لَيُعَذِّبَنَّهُ عَذَابًا لَا يُعَذِّبُهُ أَحَدًا مِنَ الْعَالَمِينَ، فَلَمَّا مَاتَ الرَّجُلُ فَعَلُوا مَا أَمَرَهُمْ بِهِ، فَأَمَرَ اللَّهُ الْبَرَّ فَجَمَعَ مَا فِيهِ، وَأَمَرَ الْبَحْرَ فَجَمَعَ مَا فِيهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: لِمَ فَعَلْتَ هَذَا ؟، قَالَ: مِنْ خَشْيَتِكَ يَا رَبِّ وَأَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ قَالَ: فَغَفَرَ لَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الجنائز (52) عن أبي الزّناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن رحمة الله أوسع من عذابه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (52), al-Bukhārī (7506), and Muslim (2756).","chapter_en":"Allah’s Mercy Is More Vast Than His Punishment","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man who had never performed a good deed said to his family: ‘When I die, burn me. Then scatter half of me upon the land and half of me into the sea. By Allah, if Allah gets hold of me, He will surely punish me with a punishment unlike that with which He has punished anyone else among the worlds.’ When the man died, they did as he had commanded them. Allah commanded the land to gather what was within it, and He commanded the sea to gather what was within it. Then He asked: ‘Why did you do this?’ The man replied: ‘Out of fear of You, my Lord, and You know best.’ So Allah forgave him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (52)، والبخاري (7506)، ومسلم (2756)."},{"num":160,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُقْبَةَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ لِحُذَيْفَةَ: أَلَا تُحَدِّثُنَا مَا سَمِعْتَ مِنَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ رَجُلًا حَضَرَهُ الْمَوْتُ لَمَّا أَيِسَ مِنَ الْحَيَاةِ أَوْصَى أَهْلَهُ إِذَا مُتُّ فَاجْمَعُوا لِي حَطَبًا كَثِيرًا، ثُمَّ أَوْرُوا نَارًا حَتَّى إِذَا أَكَلَتْ لَحْمِي وَخَلَصَتْ إِلَى عَظْمِي فَخُذُوهَا فَاطْحَنُوهَا فَذَرُّونِي فِي الْيَمِّ فِي يَوْمٍ حَارٍّ أَوْ رَاحٍ فَجَمَعَهُ اللَّهُ، فَقَالَ: لِمَ فَعَلْتَ، قَالَ: خَشْيَتَكَ فَغَفَرَ لَهُ، قَالَ عُقْبَةُ: وَأَنَا سَمِعْتُهُ، يَقُولُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الأنبياء (3479) عن مسدّد، عن أبي عوانة، عن عبدالملك بن عُمَير، عن ربعي بن حِراش، قال: قال عقبة (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن رحمة الله أوسع من عذابه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3479).","chapter_en":"Allah’s Mercy Is More Vast Than His Punishment","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah reported: He said to Ḥudhayfah: “Will you not tell us what you heard from the Prophet ﷺ?” Ḥudhayfah replied: I heard him say: “A man was approached by death. When he despaired of remaining alive, he instructed his family: ‘When I die, gather a great quantity of firewood for me and kindle a fire. When the fire has consumed my flesh and reached my bones, take my remains and grind them. Then wait for a very windy day and scatter them into the sea.’ Allah then gathered him and asked: ‘Why did you do this?’ He replied: ‘Out of fear of You.’ So Allah forgave him.” ʿUqbah said: “And I too heard him say it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3479)."},{"num":161,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ فِي قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى:﴿لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ﴾ [البقرة: 256] قَالَ: كَانَتَ الْمَرْأَةُ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ لا يَكَادُ يَعِيشُ لَهَا وَلَدٌ، فَتَحْلِفُ: لَئِنْ عَاشَ لَهَا وَلَدٌ لَتُهَوِّدَنَّهُ، فَلَمَّا أُجْلِيَتْ بَنُو النَّضِيرِ فِيهُمْ نَاسٌ مِنْ أَبْنَاءِ الأَنْصَارِ، فَقَالَتِ الأَنْصَارُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَبْنَاؤُنَا، فَأَنْزَلَ الِلَّهِ هَذِهِ الآيَةَ ﴿لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ﴾.","قَالَ سَعِيدُ بْنُ جُبَيْرٍ: فَمَنْ شَاءَ لَحِقَ بِهِمْ، وَمَنْ شَاءَ دَخَلَ فِي الإِسْلامِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (140) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم بن إسماعيل ببُست، قال: حدثنا حسن بن عليّ الحلْوانيّ، قال: حدّثنا وهب بن جرير، قال: حدثنا شعبة، عن أبي بشر، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا إكراه في الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān in his Ṣaḥīḥ (140) and Abū Dāwūd (2682).","chapter_en":"There Is No Compulsion in Religion","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them said concerning the words of Allah Most High: “There is no compulsion in religion.” [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:256] A woman from the Anṣār would have children who rarely survived. She would therefore vow that if a child of hers survived, she would raise him as a Jew. When Banū al-Naḍīr were expelled, there were among them some sons of the Anṣār. The Anṣār said: “O Messenger of Allah, our sons!” Allah then revealed: “There is no compulsion in religion.”","Saʿīd ibn Jubayr said: “Whoever wished could join them, and whoever wished could enter Islam.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In the wording of Abū Dāwūd:","“A woman would be miqlāt, so she would vow that if a child of hers survived, she would make him a Jew.”","Abū Dāwūd explained that «مِقْلاتاً» means a woman whose children do not survive."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (140)، وأبو داود (2682)."},{"num":162,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لِرَجُلٍ: أَسْلِمْ قَالَ: إِنِّي أَجِدُنِي كَارِهًا، قَالَ: وَإِنْ كُنْتَ كَارِهًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (12868) عن يحيى (القطّان)، عن حميد (الطّويل)، عن أنس، فذكره. وإنه من ثلاثيات الإمام أحمد، وهو صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا إكراه في الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Aḥmad (12061, 12868).","chapter_en":"There Is No Compulsion in Religion","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: “Accept Islam.” The man replied: “I find myself disliking it.” He said: “Even if you dislike it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["There is nothing in this ḥadīth indicating that the man was forced to embrace Islam. Rather, the Prophet ﷺ invited him to Islam, and the man explained that inwardly he did not yet feel inclined toward it but instead felt reluctant.","The Prophet ﷺ therefore told him:","“Accept Islam, even if you dislike it,”","for Allah would grant him good intention and sincerity. This was explained by Ibn Kathīr in his Tafsīr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12061، 12868)."},{"num":163,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْأَحْنَفِ بْنِ قَيْسٍ، قَالَ: ذَهَبْتُ لِأَنْصُرَ هَذَا الرَّجُلَ (يَعْنِي عَلِيِّ بْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ) فَلَقِيَنِي أَبُو بَكْرَةَ، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ تُرِيدُ؟ قُلْتُ: أَنْصُرُ هَذَا الرَّجُلَ، قَالَ: ارْجِعْ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِذَا الْتَقَى الْمُسْلِمَانِ بِسَيْفَيْهِمَا، فَالْقَاتِلُ وَالْمَقْتُولُ فِي النَّارِ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، هَذَا الْقَاتِلُ، فَمَا بَالُ الْمَقْتُولِ؟ قَالَ: إِنَّهُ كَانَ حَرِيصًا عَلَى قَتْلِ صَاحِبِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (31)، ومسلم في الفتن (2888) كلاهما من حديث حماد بن زيد، عن أيوب ويونس، عن الحسن، عن الأحنف بن قيس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قول الله تعالى: ﴿وَإِنْ طَائِفَتَانِ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ اقْتَتَلُوا فَأَصْلِحُوا بَيْنَهُمَا﴾ فسمّاهم المؤمنين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (31) and Muslim (2888).","chapter_en":"The Words of Allah, “If Two Groups of the Believers Fight, Reconcile Between Them,” and That He Called Them Believers","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays reported: I went out intending to support this man — meaning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib may Allah be pleased with him — when Abū Bakrah may Allah be pleased with him met me and asked: “Where are you going?” I replied: “To support this man.” He said: “Go back, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When two Muslims confront one another with their swords, both the killer and the one killed are in the Fire.’” I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, this is understandable concerning the killer, but what about the one who was killed?” He replied: “He was eager to kill his companion.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15791],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (31)، ومسلم (2888)."},{"num":164,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: سِبَابُ الْمُسْلِمِ فُسُوقٌ، وَقِتَالُهُ كُفْرٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (48)، ومسلم في الإيمان (64) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن زُبيد، عن أبي وائل، عن عبدالله بن مسعود، فذكر الحديث. قال زُبيد: فقلت لأبي وائل: أنت سمعت من عبدالله يرويه عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم؟ قال: نعم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب سباب المسلم فسوق وقتاله كفر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (48) and Muslim (64).","chapter_en":"Insulting a Muslim Is Sinfulness, and Fighting Him Is Disbelief","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is sinful disobedience, and fighting him is disbelief.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Regarding the words, “fighting him is disbelief,” al-Baghawī said in Sharḥ al-Sunnah (13/130):","“This applies as actual disbelief when a person regards the blood of a Muslim as lawful and does not regard Islam as protecting his life. In that case, it constitutes apostasy and genuine disbelief.","It may also mean that such conduct resembles the actions of the disbelievers without being actual disbelief when the person kills him without regarding his blood as lawful, just as the Prophet ﷺ said:","‘Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.’","That is: do not become like those whose habitual conduct is such.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6799],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (48)، ومسلم (64)."},{"num":165,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَرِيرٍ أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لَهُ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ: اسْتَنْصِتِ النَّاسَ، فَقَالَ: لَا تَرْجِعُوا بَعْدِي كُفَّارًا يَضْرِبُ بَعْضُكُمْ رِقَابَ بَعْضٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في العلم (121)، ومسلم في الإيمان (65) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، قال: أخبرني علي بن مُدركة، عن أبي زرعة، عن جدّه جرير، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان معنى قول النبي ﷺ: «لا ترجعوا بعدي كفاراً»","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (121) and Muslim (65).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Meaning of the Prophet’s Words, “Do Not Return After Me as Disbelievers”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: During the Farewell Pilgrimage, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Make the people listen attentively.” Then he said: “Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The meaning is: do not perform the deeds of the disbelievers by resembling them in killing one another. Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar explained this in Fatḥ al-Bārī (1/217)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6813],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (121)، ومسلم (65)."},{"num":166,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: وَيْلَكُمْ أَوْ وَيْحَكُمْ، لَا تَرْجِعُوا بَعْدِي كُفَّارًا يَضْرِبُ بَعْضُكُمْ رِقَابَ بَعْضٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6166)، ومسلم في الإيمان (66) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن واقد بن محمد، أنه سمع أباه يحدّث عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكر الحديث، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان معنى قول النبي ﷺ: «لا ترجعوا بعدي كفاراً»","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6166) and Muslim (66).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the Meaning of the Prophet’s Words, “Do Not Return After Me as Disbelievers”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Woe to you — or: May Allah have mercy upon you,” Shuʿbah was uncertain which expression was used, “do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6166)، ومسلم (66)."},{"num":167,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ خَالِدٍ الْجُهَنِيِّ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: صَلَّى لَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَلَاةَ الصُّبْحِ بِالْحُدَيْبِيَةِ عَلَى إِثْرِ سَمَاءٍ كَانَتْ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ فَلَمَّا انْصَرَفَ أَقْبَلَ عَلَى النَّاسِ، فَقَالَ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ ؟ قَالُوا: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: قَالَ: أَصْبَحَ مِنْ عِبَادِي مُؤْمِنٌ بِي وَكَافِرٌ بِي، فَأَمَّا مَنْ قَالَ: مُطِرْنَا بِفَضْلِ اللَّهِ وَرَحْمَتِهِ، فَذَلِكَ مُؤْمِنٌ بِي كَافِرٌ بِالْكَوْكَبِ، وَأَمَّا مَنْ قَالَ: مُطِرْنَا بِنَوْءِ كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَذَلِكَ كَافِرٌ بِي مُؤْمِنٌ بِالْكَوْكَبِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الاستسقاء (4) عن صالح بن كيسان، عن عبيد الله ابن عبدالله بن عتبة بن مسعود، عن زيد بن خالد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان إطلاق اسم الكفر على من قال: مُطرنا بالنوء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (4), al-Bukhārī (846), and Muslim (71).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Use of the Term Disbelief for One Who Says, “We Were Given Rain by Such-and-Such Star”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer at al-Ḥudaybiyyah following rainfall that had occurred during the night. When he finished the prayer, he turned toward the people and asked: “Do you know what your Lord has said?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “He said: ‘This morning some of My servants have become believers in Me and others disbelievers in Me. As for the one who said, “We were given rain by the grace of Allah and His mercy,” he is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the star. But as for the one who said, “We were given rain by such-and-such nawʾ,” he is a disbeliever in Me and a believer in the star.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Regarding the word «النوء», Ibn al-Ṣalāḥ said:","“Originally, it does not refer to the star itself. Rather, it is the verbal noun of the expression nāʾa al-najm, meaning that the star set and disappeared; and it has also been said to mean that it rose and appeared.”","He then said:","“The star itself may subsequently be called nawʾ, the doer being named by the verbal noun.”","Abū Isḥāq al-Zajjāj said in some of his dictations that the stars setting in the west are called the anwāʾ, while the corresponding star rising in the east is its raqīb.","Ṣiyānat Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim, pp. 246–247."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (4)، والبخاري (846)، ومسلم (71)."},{"num":168,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلَمْ تَرَوْا إِلَى مَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ؟ قَالَ: مَا أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَى عِبَادِي مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ، إِلَّا أَصْبَحَ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ بِهَا كَافِرِينَ، يَقُولُونَ: الْكَوَاكِبُ وَبِالْكَوَاكِبِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (72) من طرق عن يونس، عن ابن شهاب، قال: حدثني عبيد الله بن عبدالله بن عتبة، أنّ أبا هريرة قال (فذكر الحديث).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان إطلاق اسم الكفر على من قال: مُطرنا بالنوء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (72).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Use of the Term Disbelief for One Who Says, “We Were Given Rain by Such-and-Such Star”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Have you not considered what your Lord said? He said: ‘I do not bestow any blessing upon My servants except that a group among them enters the morning disbelieving in it, saying: The stars, and because of the stars.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another narration adds:","“Allah does not send down any blessing from the sky except that a group of people enters the morning disbelieving in it. Allah sends down the rain, and they say: ‘Such-and-such star caused it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (72)."},{"num":169,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: مُطِرَ النَّاسُ عَلَى عَهْدِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَصْبَحَ مِنَ النَّاسِ شَاكِرٌ، وَمِنْهُمْ كَافِرٌ، قَالُوا: هَذِهِ رَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ، وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: لَقَدْ صَدَقَ نَوْءُ كَذَا وَكَذَا، قَالَ: فَنَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ ﴿فَلَا أُقْسِمُ بِمَوَاقِعِ النُّجُومِ﴾ حَتَّى بَلَغَ: ﴿وَتَجْعَلُونَ رِزْقَكُمْ أَنَّكُمْ تُكَذِّبُونَ﴾ [الواقعة: 75، 82]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (73) عن عباس بن عبدالعظيم العنبريّ، حدثنا النضر بن محمد، حدثنا عكرمة (وهو ابن عمار)، حدثنا أبو زُميل، حدثني ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان إطلاق اسم الكفر على من قال: مُطرنا بالنوء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (73).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Use of the Term Disbelief for One Who Says, “We Were Given Rain by Such-and-Such Star”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: Rain fell upon the people during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This morning some of the people became grateful and some became disbelievers. Some said, ‘This is the mercy of Allah,’ while others said, ‘Such-and-such nawʾ has proven true.’” Then these verses were revealed: “Then I swear by the positions of the stars — and indeed, it is a tremendous oath, if you only knew — indeed, this is truly a noble Qurʾān, in a well-preserved Book, touched by none except the purified, a revelation from the Lord of all worlds. Is it this message that you take lightly, and do you make your provision that you deny it?” [Sūrat al-Wāqiʿah 56:75–82]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (73)."},{"num":170,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الدَّرْدَاءِ قَالَ: قَحَطَ الْمَطَرُ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَسَأَلْنَا نَبِيَّ اللهِ أَنْ يَسْتَسْقِيَ لَنَا، فَاسْتَسْقَى، فَغَدَا نَبِيُّ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَإِذَا هُوَ بِقَوْمٍ يَتَحَدَّثُونَ، قَالُوا: سُقِينَا اللَّيْلَةَ بِنَوْءِ كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَقَالَ نَبِيُّ اللهِ: مَا أَنْعَمَ اللهُ عَلَى قَوْمٍ نِعْمَةً إِلَّا أَصْبَحُوا بِهَا كَافِرِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (4102)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (1102) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل بن عياش، عن راشد بن داود الصنعاني، عن أبي عثمان الصنعاني، عن أبي الدرداء قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان إطلاق اسم الكفر على من قال: مُطرنا بالنوء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (4102) and al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (1102).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Use of the Term Disbelief for One Who Says, “We Were Given Rain by Such-and-Such Star”","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: Rain became scarce during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we asked the Prophet of Allah ﷺ to pray for rain for us, and he did so. The next morning, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ came upon some people who were speaking together. They said: “We were given rain last night because of such-and-such nawʾ.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a people except that some of them enter the morning disbelieving in that blessing.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (4102)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (1102)."},{"num":171,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اثْنَتَانِ فِي النَّاسِ هُمَا بِهِمْ كُفْرٌ، الطَّعْنُ فِي النَّسَبِ، وَالنِّيَاحَةُ عَلَى الْمَيِّتِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (67) من طرق عن الأعمش، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إطلاق اسم الكفر على الطعن في النسب والنياحة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (67).","chapter_en":"Applying the Term Disbelief to Attacking Lineage and Wailing Over the Dead","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":48,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two practices found among people are acts of disbelief: attacking people’s lineage and wailing over the dead.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[3558],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (67)."},{"num":172,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: ثَلَاثٌ مِنْ عَمَلِ أَهْلِ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ لَا يَتْرُكُهُنَّ أَهْلُ الْإِسْلَامِ: النِّيَاحَةُ، وَالِاسْتِسْقَاءُ بِالْأَنْوَاءِ، وَكَذَا . قُلْتُ لِسَعِيدٍ: وَمَا هُوَ؟ قَالَ: دَعْوَى الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ يَا آلَ فُلَانٍ، يَا آلَ فُلَانٍ، يَا آلَ فُلَانٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (7560) عن ربعي بن إبراهيم، حدثنا عبدالرحمن، يعني ابن إسحاق، ، عن سعيد المقبريّ، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إطلاق اسم الكفر على الطعن في النسب والنياحة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (7560), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (3141).","chapter_en":"Applying the Term Disbelief to Attacking Lineage and Wailing Over the Dead","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":48,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three practices from the deeds of the pre-Islamic period will not be abandoned by the people of Islam: wailing over the dead, seeking rain through attribution to the anwāʾ, and such-and-such.” The narrator said: I asked Saʿīd: “What is the other practice?” He replied: “The tribal call of the pre-Islamic period: ‘O family of so-and-so! O family of so-and-so!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (7560)، وصححه ابن حبان (3141)."},{"num":173,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: أَنَّ نَاسًا مِنْ أَهْلِ الشِّرْكِ كَانُوا قَدْ قَتَلُوا وَأَكْثَرُوا، وَزَنَوْا وَأَكْثَرُوا، فَأَتَوْا مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: إِنَّ الَّذِي تَقُولُ وَتَدْعُو إِلَيْهِ لَحَسَنٌ لَوْ تُخْبِرُنَا أَنَّ لِمَا عَمِلْنَا كَفَّارَةً، فَنَزَلَ ﴿وَالَّذِينَ لَا يَدْعُونَ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَهًا آخَرَ وَلَا يَقْتُلُونَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِي حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا يَزْنُونَ﴾ [الفرقان: 68]، وَنَزَلَ ﴿قُلْ يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَى أَنْفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا مِنْ رَحْمَةِ اللَّهِ﴾ [الزمر: 53]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4810)، ومسلم في الإيمان (122) كلاهما عن ابن جريج، قال: أخبرني يعلى بن مسلم، أنّه سمع سعيد بن جبير يحدّث عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الإسلام يهدم ما كان قبله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4810) and Muslim (122).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Islam Erases What Came Before It","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: Some people from among the polytheists had committed much killing and had repeatedly committed unlawful sexual relations. They came to Muḥammad ﷺ and said: “What you say and call people toward is certainly good, if only you could tell us whether there is any expiation for what we have done.” Then Allah revealed: “And those who do not invoke another deity alongside Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except with legal right, nor commit unlawful sexual intercourse…” [Sūrat al-Furqān 25:68] And He revealed: “Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah.” [Sūrat al-Zumar 39:53]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4810)، ومسلم (122)."},{"num":174,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَجُلٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَنُؤَاخَذُ بِمَا عَمِلْنَا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ ؟ قَالَ: مَنْ أَحْسَنَ فِي الْإِسْلَامِ لَمْ يُؤَاخَذْ بِمَا عَمِلَ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، وَمَنْ أَسَاءَ فِي الْإِسْلَامِ أُخِذَ بِالْأَوَّلِ وَالْآخِرِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في استتابة المرتدين (6921)، ومسلم في الإيمان (120) كلاهما من حديث منصور، عن الأعمش، عن أبي وائل، عن ابن مسعود، فذكر الحديث، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الإسلام يهدم ما كان قبله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6921) and Muslim (120).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Islam Erases What Came Before It","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we did during the pre-Islamic period?” He replied: “Whoever does well after embracing Islam will not be held accountable for what he did during the pre-Islamic period. But whoever does evil after embracing Islam will be held accountable for both the former and the latter.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The meaning of “does evil” here is disbelief and polytheism. Thus, whoever returns to associating partners with Allah and disbelieving in Him after embracing Islam will be held accountable for what he did both before and after Islam. Otherwise, he will not.","Allah Most High says:","“Say to those who disbelieve that if they cease, what has previously occurred will be forgiven for them.”","[Sūrat al-Anfāl 8:38]","And in the following ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ:","“Islam erases what came before it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12380],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6921)، ومسلم (120)."},{"num":175,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ شِمَاسَةَ الْمَهْرِيِّ قَالَ: حَضَرْنَا عَمْرَو بْنَ الْعَاصِ وَهُوَ فِي سِيَاقَةِ الْمَوْتِ، فَبَكَى طَوِيلًا وَحَوَّلَ وَجْهَهُ إِلَى الْجِدَارِ، فَجَعَلَ ابْنُهُ يَقُولُ: يَا أَبَتَاهُ أَمَا بَشَّرَكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِكَذَا؟ أَمَا بَشَّرَكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِكَذَا؟ قَالَ: فَأَقْبَلَ بِوَجْهِهِ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ أَفْضَلَ مَا نُعِدُّ، شَهَادَةُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، إِنِّي قَدْ كُنْتُ عَلَى أَطْبَاقٍ ثَلَاثٍ، لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي وَمَا أَحَدٌ أَشَدَّ بُغْضًا لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنِّي، وَلَا أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ أَنْ أَكُونَ قَدِ اسْتَمْكَنْتُ مِنْهُ فَقَتَلْتُهُ، فَلَوْ مُتُّ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، لَكُنْتُ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَلَمَّا جَعَلَ اللَّهُ الإِسْلَامَ فِي قَلْبِي، أَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: ابْسُطْ يَمِينَكَ فَلأُبَايِعْكَ، فَبَسَطَ يَمِينَهُ، قَالَ: فَقَبَضْتُ يَدِي، قَالَ: مَا لَكَ يَا عَمْرُو؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: أَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَشْتَرِطَ، قَالَ: تَشْتَرِطُ بِمَاذَا؟ قُلْتُ: أَنْ يُغْفَرَ لِي، قَالَ: أَمَا عَلِمْتَ أَنَّ الإِسْلَامَ يَهْدِمُ، مَا كَانَ قَبْلَهُ وَأَنَّ الْهِجْرَةَ تَهْدِمُ مَا كَانَ قَبْلِهَا، وَأَنَّ الْحَجَّ يَهْدِمُ مَا كَانَ قَبْلَهُ، وَمَا كَانَ أَحَدٌ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلَا أَجَلَّ فِي عَيْنِي مِنْهُ، وَمَا كُنْتُ أُطِيقُ أَنْ أَمْلَأَ عَيْنَيَّ مِنْهُ إِجْلَالًا لَهُ، وَلَوْ سُئِلْتُ أَنْ أَصِفَهُ مَا أَطَقْتُ، لِأَنِّي لَمْ أَكُنْ أَمْلَأُ عَيْنَيَّ مِنْهُ، وَلَوْ مُتُّ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، لَرَجَوْتُ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، ثُمَّ وَلِينَا أَشْيَاءَ مَا أَدْرِي مَا حَالِي فِيهَا، فَإِذَا أَنَا مُتُّ، فَلَا تَصْحَبْنِي نَائِحَةٌ، وَلَا نَارٌ، فَإِذَا دَفَنْتُمُونِي، فَشُنُّوا عَلَيَّ التُّرَابَ شَنًّا، ثُمَّ أَقِيمُوا حَوْلَ قَبْرِي قَدْرَ مَا تُنْحَرُ جَزُورٌ، وَيُقْسَمُ لَحْمُهَا حَتَّى أَسْتَأْنِسَ بِكُمْ، وَأَنْظُرَ مَاذَا أُرَاجِعُ بِهِ رُسُلَ رَبِّي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (121) من طرق عن أبي عاصم الضّحاك، قال: أخبرنا حيدة بن شريح، قال: حدثني يزيد بن أبي حبيب، عن ابن شُماسة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الإسلام يهدم ما كان قبله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (121).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported That Islam Erases What Came Before It","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Shumāsah al-Mahrī reported: We were present with ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ may Allah be pleased with him while he was in the throes of death. He wept for a long time and turned his face toward the wall. His son began saying: “Father, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not give you glad tidings of such-and-such? Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not give you glad tidings of such-and-such?” ʿAmr turned toward them and said: “The best thing we have prepared is the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah. I passed through three different stages. I remember a time when no one was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was nothing I desired more than to gain power over him and kill him. Had I died in that state, I would certainly have been among the people of the Fire. Then when Allah placed Islam within my heart, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ‘Extend your right hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you.’ He extended his right hand, but I drew my hand back. He asked: ‘What is the matter with you, O ʿAmr?’ I replied: ‘I wish to stipulate a condition.’ He asked: ‘What condition do you wish to stipulate?’ I replied: ‘That I be forgiven.’ He said: ‘Do you not know that Islam erases what came before it, that migration erases what came before it, and that ḥajj erases what came before it?’ Thereafter, no one was more beloved to me than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor was anyone greater in my eyes than he was. I could not fill my eyes with looking at him because of my reverence for him. If I were asked to describe him, I would be unable to do so because I never gazed fully at him. Had I died in that state, I would have hoped to be among the people of Paradise. Then we were entrusted with various affairs, and I do not know what my condition in them has been. When I die, let no wailing woman accompany me and let no fire accompany me. When you bury me, pour the earth over me, then remain around my grave for the length of time it takes to slaughter a camel and distribute its meat, so that I may feel comforted by your presence and consider how I should answer the messengers of my Lord.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His words, “I passed through three stages,” mean three successive conditions and phases, as in the words of Allah Most High:","“You will surely pass from one stage to another.”","[Sūrat al-Inshiqāq 84:19]","That is: from one condition to another.","His words, “pour the earth over me,” have been narrated with two closely related Arabic pronunciations. It has been said that both carry the meaning of pouring. It has also been said that one refers to pouring gently, while the other refers to scattering it.","ʿIyāḍ stated that this describes the practice of pouring soil over the deceased in the grave.","Al-Qurṭubī, al-Mufhim (1/330)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10295],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (121)."},{"num":176,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حَكِيمِ بْنِ حِزَامٍ قَالَ: قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَرَأَيْتَ أَشْيَاءَ كُنْتُ أَتَحَنَّثُ بِهَا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ مِنْ صَدَقَةٍ أَوْ عَتَاقَةٍ وَصِلَةِ رَحِمٍ، فَهَلْ فِيهَا مِنْ أَجْرٍ؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَسْلَمْتَ عَلَى مَا سَلَفَ مِنْ خَيْرٍ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: أَنَّ حَكِيمَ بْنَ حِزَامٍ، أَعْتَقَ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ مِائَةَ رَقَبَةٍ، وَحَمَلَ عَلَى مِائَةِ بَعِيرٍ، ثُمَّ أَعْتَقَ فِي الإِسْلَامِ مِائَةَ رَقَبَةٍ، وَحَمَلَ عَلَى مِائَةِ بَعِيرٍ، ثُمَّ أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَذَكَرَ نَحْوَ حَدِيثِه."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الزكاة (1436)، ومسلم في الإيمان (123) كلاهما من حديث ابن شهاب الزهريّ، قال: أخبرني عروة بن الزبير، أنّ حكيم بن حزام، فذكر مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من عمل خيراً في الكفر ثم أسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1436) and Muslim (123).","chapter_en":"Whoever Performed Good Deeds While in Disbelief and Then Embraced Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about the things I used to perform as acts of devotion during the pre-Islamic period — such as charity, freeing slaves, and maintaining ties of kinship? Is there any reward for them?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You embraced Islam upon the good that you had already sent forth.”","In another narration: Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām had freed one hundred slaves during the pre-Islamic period and provided one hundred camels. Then, after embracing Islam, he freed another one hundred slaves and provided another one hundred camels. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ and related the matter as in the narration above."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration he said:","“By Allah, I will not leave any good deed that I used to perform during the pre-Islamic period except that I will perform its equivalent in Islam.”","The word «التحنث» means worship and devotional practice.","Regarding the words:","“You embraced Islam upon the good that you had already sent forth,”","most scholars interpreted their meaning.","Al-Ḥarbī said:","“The good deeds you previously performed remain for you, just as one might say, ‘He embraced Islam while possessing one thousand dirhams,’ meaning that he retained them for himself.”","Al-Qurṭubī said:","“What al-Ḥarbī stated is the interpretation that most closely resembles the wording and is the most appropriate.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1436)، ومسلم (123)."},{"num":177,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا أَسْلَمَ الْعَبْدُ فَحَسُنَ إِسْلَامُهُ كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَهُ كُلَّ حَسَنَةٍ كَانَ أَزْلَفَهَا، وَمُحِيَتْ عَنْهُ كُلُّ سَيِّئَةٍ كَانَ أَزْلَفَهَا، ثُمَّ كَانَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ الْقِصَاصُ، الْحَسَنَةُ بِعَشْرَةِ أَمْثَالِهَا إِلَى سَبْعِ مِائَةِ ضِعْفٍ، وَالسَّيِّئَةُ بِمِثْلِهَا إِلَّا أَنْ يَتَجَاوَزَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَنْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائيّ (4998) من طريق الوليد (هو ابن مسلم)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (24) من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي أويس، كلاهما قالا: حدثنا مالك، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن عطاء بن يسار، عن أبي سعيد الخدريّ، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء. إلاّ أنّ البيهقي قال: أسنده مالك وأرسله ابنُ عيينة، ثم روى الحديث من طريقه مرسلاً.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من عمل خيراً في الكفر ثم أسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Nasāʾī (4998) and al-Bayhaqī in Shuʿab al-Īmān (24).","chapter_en":"Whoever Performed Good Deeds While in Disbelief and Then Embraced Islam","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a servant embraces Islam and perfects his Islam, Allah records for him every good deed that he had previously sent forth and erases from him every bad deed that he had previously sent forth. After that comes recompense: a good deed is multiplied tenfold up to seven hundred times, while a bad deed is recorded as only one like it, unless Allah, Mighty and Majestic, pardons it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī mentioned it in the Book of Faith (41) as a suspended narration from Mālik and did not provide its connected chain elsewhere. However, he omitted the words:","“Allah records for him every good deed that he had previously sent forth.”","The reason this wording was considered difficult according to certain general principles is that a disbeliever is not ordinarily rewarded for righteous deeds performed while in disbelief and polytheism, since an act of drawing near requires recognition of the One to whom the person draws near.","Al-Māzarī and others discussed this difficulty, and al-Qāḍī ʿIyāḍ likewise presented it.","Al-Nawawī responded:","“The correct view held by the verifying scholars — and some have even transmitted consensus upon it — is that if a disbeliever performs virtuous deeds such as giving charity and maintaining ties of kinship, then embraces Islam and dies upon Islam, the reward of those deeds is recorded for him.”","Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar mentioned several other possibilities in Fatḥ al-Bārī (1/99). Among the strongest is his statement:","“The correct position is that Allah’s graciously recording reward for a Muslim after his Islam does not necessarily mean that the deed he performed while in disbelief had already been accepted at that time. The ḥadīth speaks only of recording the reward and does not explicitly state acceptance. It is possible that acceptance was made conditional upon his later Islam: if he embraces Islam, the deed is accepted and rewarded; otherwise, it is not.”","The preceding ḥadīth of Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām supports this interpretation.","The expression «أزلفها» means: he sent it forth and put it forward."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[143],"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (4998)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (24)."},{"num":178,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! ابْنُ جُدْعَانَ كَانَ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ يَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ وَيُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِينَ فَهَلْ ذَاكَ نَافِعُهُ؟ قَالَ: لَا يَنْفَعُهُ، إِنَّهُ لَمْ يَقُلْ يَوْمًا: رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي خَطِيئَتِي يَوْمَ الدِّينِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (214) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا حفص بن غياث، عن داود، عن الشعبي، عن مسروق، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من لم يؤمن لم ينفعه عمل صالح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (214).","chapter_en":"Whoever Does Not Believe Will Not Benefit From a Righteous Deed","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her reported: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Judʿān used to maintain ties of kinship and feed the poor during the pre-Islamic period. Will that benefit him?” He replied: “It will not benefit him, for he never once said: ‘My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Recompense.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (214)."},{"num":179,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَدِيَّ بْنَ حَاتِمٍ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِنَّ أَبِي كَانَ يَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ، وَيَفْعَلُ كَذَا وَكَذَا. قَالَ: إِنَّ أَبَاكَ أَرَادَ أَمْرًا فَأَدْرَكَهُ . يَعْنِي: الذِّكْرَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه احمد (18262)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 250)، وابن حبان (332) كلهم من طريق شعبة، عن سماك بن حرب، قال: سمعت مري بن قطري قال: سمعت عدي بن حاتم فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من لم يؤمن لم ينفعه عمل صالح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (18262), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (17/104), and Ibn Ḥibbān (332).","chapter_en":"Whoever Does Not Believe Will Not Benefit From a Righteous Deed","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain ties of kinship and perform such-and-such good deeds.” He replied: “Your father sought something, and he attained it.” That is, he sought mention and reputation."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (18262)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 250)، وابن حبان (332)."},{"num":180,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَدَأَ الإِسْلَامُ غَرِيبًا، وَسَيَعُودُ كَمَا بَدَأَ غَرِيبًا، فَطُوبَى لِلْغُرَبَاءِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (145) من طرق عن مروان الفزاريّ، عن يزيد بن كيسان، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإسلام بدأ غريباً وسيعود غريباً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (145).","chapter_en":"Islam Began as Something Strange and Will Return to Being Strange","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange just as it began. So glad tidings are for the strangers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (145)."},{"num":181,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، عَن النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ الإِسْلَامَ بَدَأَ غَرِيبًا، وَسَيَعُودُ غَرِيبًا، كَمَا بَدَأَ وَهُوَ يَأْرِزُ بَيْنَ الْمَسْجِدَيْنِ، كَمَا تَأْرِزُ الْحَيَّةُ فِي جُحْرِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (146) من طرق عن شبابة بن سوّار، حدثنا عاصم (وهو ابن محمد العمريّ)، عن أبيه، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإسلام بدأ غريباً وسيعود غريباً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (146).","chapter_en":"Islam Began as Something Strange and Will Return to Being Strange","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange just as it began. It will retreat between the two mosques just as a snake retreats into its hole.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[10581],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (146)."},{"num":182,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ الْإِيمَانَ بَدَأَ غَرِيبًا، وَسَيَعُودُ غَرِيبًا كَمَا بَدَأَ، فَطُوبَى يَوْمَئِذٍ لِلْغُرَبَاءِ إِذَا فَسَدَ النَّاسُ. وَالَّذِي نَفْسُ أَبِي الْقَاسِمِ بِيَدِهِ لَيَأْرِزَنَّ الْإِيمَانُ إِلَى بَيْنِ هَذَيْنِ الْمَسْجِدَيْنِ كَمَا تَأْرِزُ الْحَيَّةُ إِلَى جُحْرِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (1604)، وأبو يعلى (756)، والبزار في البحر الزّخّار (1119) كلهم من طرق عن عبدالله بن وهب، قال: أخبرني أبو صخر، عن أبي حازم، عن ابن سعد، عن سعد، قال البزار: أحسبه عامراً.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإسلام بدأ غريباً وسيعود غريباً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (1604), Abū Yaʿlā (756), and al-Bazzār in al-Baḥr al-Zakhkhār (1119).","chapter_en":"Islam Began as Something Strange and Will Return to Being Strange","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Faith began as something strange, and it will return to being strange just as it began. So glad tidings on that day are for the strangers when the people become corrupt. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Abū al-Qāsim, faith will retreat between these two mosques just as a snake retreats into its hole.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The two mosques are the mosque of Makkah and the mosque of Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (1604)، وأبو يعلى (756)، والبزار في البحر الزخار (1119)."},{"num":183,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ الإِسْلَامَ بَدَأَ غَرِيبًا، وَسَيَعُودُ غَرِيبًا كَمَا بَدَأَ، فَطُوبَى لِلْغُرَبَاءِ، قِيلَ: مَن هُمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: الَّذِينَ يُصْلِحُونَ إِذَا فَسَدَ النَّاسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الآجريّ في الغرباء (1) عن عبدالله بن أبي داود، حدثنا محمد ابن آدم المصيصيّ، حدثنا حفص بن غياث، عن الأعمش، عن أبي إسحاق، عن أبي الأحوص، عن عبدالله، يعني ابن مسعود، ، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإسلام بدأ غريباً وسيعود غريباً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Ājurrī in al-Ghurabāʾ (1).","chapter_en":"Islam Began as Something Strange and Will Return to Being Strange","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange just as it began. So glad tidings are for the strangers.” It was asked: “Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Those who set things right when the people become corrupt.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الآجري في الغرباء (1)."},{"num":184,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عَمْرِو بْنِ العاص قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ وَنَحْنُ عِنْدَهُ: طُوبَى لِلْغُرَبَاءِ، فَقِيلَ: مَنِ الْغُرَبَاءُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: أُنَاسٌ صَالِحُونَ فِي أُنَاسِ سُوءٍ كَثِيرٍ، مَنْ يَعْصِيهِمْ أَكْثَرُ مِمَّنْ يُطِيعُهُمْ.","ثُمَّ ذَكَرَ فُقَرَاءُ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ الَّذِينَ تُتَّقَى بِهِمُ الْمَكَارِهُ...الْحَدِيثَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6650) عن حسن بن موسى، حدثنا ابن لهيعة، حدثنا الحارث بن يزيد، عن جندب بن عبدالله، أنه سمع سفيان بن عوف يقول: سمعت عبدالله بن عمرو، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الإسلام بدأ غريباً وسيعود غريباً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ḥasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (6650), ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak in al-Zuhd (775), and al-Bayhaqī in al-Zuhd (203).","chapter_en":"Islam Began as Something Strange and Will Return to Being Strange","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: One day, while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Glad tidings are for the strangers.” It was asked: “Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Righteous people among a great number of corrupt people; those who disobey them are more numerous than those who obey them.”","He then mentioned the poor among the Muhājirūn, through whom hardships are warded off…"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6650)، وعبد الله بن المبارك في الزهد (775)، والبيهقي في الزهد (203)."},{"num":185,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: نَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِالشَّكِّ مِنْ إِبْرَاهِيمَ إِذْ قَالَ: ﴿رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِ الْمَوْتَى قَالَ أَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ قَالَ بَلَى وَلَكِنْ لِيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِي﴾ [البقرة: 260]، وَيَرْحَمُ اللَّهُ لُوطًا لَقَدْ كَانَ يَأْوِي إِلَى رُكْنٍ شَدِيدٍ وَلَوْ لَبِثْتُ فِي السِّجْنِ طُولَ مَا لَبِثَ يُوسُفُ لَأَجَبْتُ الدَّاعِيَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأنبياء (3372)، ومسلم في الفضائل (2370: 152) كلاهما من حديث ابن وهب، قال: أخبرني يونس، عن ابن شهاب، عن أبي سلمة بن عبدالرحمن، وسعيد بن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب زيادة طمأنينة القلب بتظاهر الأدلة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3372) and Muslim (2370:152).","chapter_en":"Increasing the Heart’s Reassurance Through the Manifestation of Proofs","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":53,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We have more right to doubt than Ibrāhīm, when he said: ‘My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.’ He said, ‘Do you not believe?’ He replied, ‘Yes, but so that my heart may be reassured.’ [Sūrat al-Baqarah 2:260] May Allah have mercy upon Lūṭ; indeed, he used to seek refuge in a strong support. And if I had remained in prison for as long as Yūsuf remained, I would have answered the caller.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī said:","The Prophet’s statement:","“We have more right to doubt than Ibrāhīm”","is not an admission of doubt either on his own part or on the part of Ibrāhīm. Rather, it negates doubt from both of them. Its meaning is: if I do not doubt or waver concerning Allah’s power, Mighty and Majestic, to bring the dead to life, then Ibrāhīm is even more deserving of not doubting or wavering.","The Prophet ﷺ said this out of humility and self-effacement.","It also clarifies that Ibrāhīm’s request did not arise from doubt, but from seeking an increase in knowledge, for direct observation gives a degree of knowledge and reassurance beyond that obtained through inference alone.","His words:","“So that my heart may be reassured”","mean: through the certainty produced by direct observation.","This is abridged. See Aʿlām al-Ḥadīth (3/1545–1546).","The Prophet’s statement:","“I would have answered the caller”","means: I would have hastened to respond and leave the prison rather than first requesting formal vindication. Yūsuf, peace be upon him, was thus described as possessing tremendous patience because he did not hasten to leave.","The Prophet ﷺ said this by way of humility. Humility does not diminish the rank of a great person; rather, it increases him in elevation and dignity.","It has also been said that this is similar to his statement:","“Do not prefer me over Yūnus.”","See Fatḥ al-Bārī (6/413)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3372)، ومسلم (2370: 152)."},{"num":186,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَقُومُ السَّاعَةُ حَتَّى تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ مِنْ مَغْرِبِهَا، فَإِذَا رَآهَا النَّاسُ آمَنَ مَنْ عَلَيْهَا، فَذَاكَ حِينَ ﴿لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ آمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ﴾ [سورة الأنعام: 158]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4635)، ومسلم في الإيمان (157) كلاهما من حديث عمارة بن القعقاع، عن أبي زرعة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان الزمن الذي لا يقبل فيه الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4635) and Muslim (157).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Time When Faith Will No Longer Be Accepted","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":54,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from the west. When it rises and the people see it, everyone upon the earth will believe. That will be the time when: ‘No soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before.’” [Sūrat al-Anʿām 6:158]"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī (4636) and Muslim also narrated:","“When it rises from the west, all the people will believe altogether. On that day:","‘No soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned any good through its faith.’”","[Sūrat al-Anʿām 6:158]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4635)، ومسلم (157)."},{"num":187,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ثَلَاثٌ إِذَا خَرَجْنَ ﴿لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ آمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ، أَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِي إِيمَانِهَا خَيْرًا﴾ [سورة الأنعام: 158] طُلُوعُ الشَّمْسِ مِنْ مَغْرِبِهَا، وَالدَّجَّالُ، وَدَابَّةُ الأَرْضِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (158) من طرق عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، قال: فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان الزمن الذي لا يقبل فيه الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (158).","chapter_en":"Explaining the Time When Faith Will No Longer Be Accepted","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":54,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are three things which, when they appear, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith: the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjāl, and the Beast of the Earth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (158)."},{"num":188,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ أَنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ يَوْمًا: أَتَدْرُونَ أَيْنَ تَذْهَبُ هَذِهِ الشَّمْسُ؟ قَالُوا: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: إِنَّ هَذِهِ تَجْرِي حَتَّى تَنْتَهِيَ إِلَى مُسْتَقَرِّهَا تَحْتَ الْعَرْشِ، فَتَخِرُّ سَاجِدَةً، وَلاَ تَزَالُ كَذَلِكَ حَتَّى يُقَالَ لَهَا: ارْتَفِعِي، ارْجِعِي مِنْ حَيْثُ جِئْتِ، فَتَرْجِعُ فَتُصْبِحُ طَالِعَةً مِنْ مَطْلِعِهَا، ثُمَّ تَجْرِي حَتَّى تَنْتَهِيَ إِلَى مُسْتَقَرِّهَا تَحْتَ الْعَرْشِ فَتَخِرُّ سَاجِدَةً، وَلَا تَزَالُ كَذَلِكَ، حَتَّى يُقَالَ لَهَا: ارْتَفِعِي، ارْجِعِي مِنْ حَيْثُ جِئْتِ، فَتَرْجِعُ فَتُصْبِحُ طَالِعَةً مِنْ مَطْلِعِهَا، ثُمَّ تَجْرِي لَا يَسْتَنْكِرُ النَّاسَ مِنْهَا شَيْئًا، حَتَّى تَنْتَهِيَ إِلَى مُسْتَقَرِّهَا ذَاكَ تَحْتَ الْعَرْشِ، فَيُقَالُ لَهَا: ارْتَفِعِي، أَصْبِحِي طَالِعَةً مِنْ مَغْرِبِكِ، فَتُصْبِحُ طَالِعَةً مِنْ مَغْرِبِهَا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَتَى ذَاكُمْ؟ ذَاكَ حِينَ ﴿لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ آمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ أَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِي إِيمَانِهَا خَيْرًا﴾ [سورة الأنعام: 158]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في بدء الخلق (3199)، ومسلم في الإيمان (159) كلاهما من حديث إبراهيم بن يزيد التيميّ، عن أبيه، عن أبي ذرّ، فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.وفي رواية لهما: فذلك قوله تعالى ﴿وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَهَا ذَلِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ﴾ [يس: 38].","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان الزمن الذي لا يقبل فيه الإيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3199) and Muslim (159), with the wording of Muslim.","chapter_en":"Explaining the Time When Faith Will No Longer Be Accepted","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":54,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said one day: “Do you know where this sun goes?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “It travels until it reaches its resting place beneath the Throne. It then falls down in prostration and remains that way until it is said to it: ‘Rise and return from where you came.’ It returns and rises from its usual place of rising. Then it travels until it reaches its resting place beneath the Throne, falls in prostration, and remains that way until it is said to it: ‘Rise and return from where you came.’ It returns and rises from its usual place of rising. Then it continues traveling, while the people notice nothing unusual about it, until it reaches that resting place beneath the Throne. Then it will be said to it: ‘Rise and emerge from your place of setting.’ So it will rise from the west.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Do you know when that will occur? It will be when: ‘No soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned any good through its faith.’” [Sūrat al-Anʿām 6:158]"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وفي رواية لهما:","«فذلك قوله تعالى:","﴿وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَهَا ذَلِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ﴾»","[يس: ٣٨]"],"en":["In another narration found in both collections:","“That is the meaning of Allah’s statement:","‘And the sun runs to its resting place. That is the decree of the Almighty, the All-Knowing.’”","[Sūrat Yā Sīn 36:38]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3199)، ومسلم (159)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":189,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْمَعْرُورِ قَالَ: لَقِيتُ أَبَا ذَرٍّ بِالرَّبَذَةِ وَعَلَيْهِ حُلَّةٌ وَعَلَى غُلَامِهِ حُلَّةٌ، فَسَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ: إِنِّي سَابَبْتُ رَجُلًا فَعَيَّرْتُهُ بِأُمِّهِ، فَقَالَ لِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ، أَعَيَّرْتَهُ بِأُمِّهِ، إِنَّكَ امْرُؤٌ فِيكَ جَاهِلِيَّةٌ إِخْوَانُكُمْ خَوَلُكُمْ جَعَلَهُمُ اللَّهُ تَحْتَ أَيْدِيكُمْ، فَمَنْ كَانَ أَخُوهُ تَحْتَ يَدِهِ فَلْيُطْعِمْهُ مِمَّا يَأْكُلُ وَلْيُلْبِسْهُ مِمَّا يَلْبَسُ، وَلَا تُكَلِّفُوهُمْ مَا يَغْلِبُهُمْ، فَإِنْ كَلَّفْتُمُوهُمْ فَأَعِينُوهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الإيمان (30)، ومسلم في الأيمان والنذور (1661) كلاهما من حديث شعبة، عن واصل بن الأحدب، عن المعرور بن سويد، فذكره، واللفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم قريب منه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب المعاصي من أمر الجاهلية، ولا يكفر صاحبها بارتكابها إلا بالشرك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (30) and Muslim (1661).","chapter_en":"Sins Are From the Ways of the Pre-Islamic Era, and One Does Not Become a Disbeliever by Committing Them Except Through Polytheism","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Maʿrūr reported: I met Abū Dharr may Allah be pleased with him at al-Rabadhah. He was wearing a set of clothing, and his servant was wearing a similar set. I asked him about this, and he said: “I once exchanged insults with a man and reproached him concerning his mother. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: ‘O Abū Dharr, did you reproach him concerning his mother? You are a man in whom there remains a trait of Jāhiliyyah. Your servants are your brothers whom Allah has placed under your authority. Whoever has his brother under his authority should feed him from what he himself eats, clothe him from what he himself wears, and not burden him with work beyond his ability. If you do burden him, then help him.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words:","“You reproached him concerning his mother”","refer to the fact that the man’s mother was non-Arab."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12153],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (30)، ومسلم (1661)."},{"num":190,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي أُمَامَةَ قَالَ: سَأَلَ رَجُلٌ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَا الْإِثْمُ؟ فَقَالَ: إِذَا حَكَّ فِي نَفْسِكَ شَيْءٌ فَدَعْهُ، قَالَ: فَمَا الْإِيمَانُ؟ قَالَ: إِذَا سَاءَتْكَ سَيِّئَتُكَ، وَسَرَّتْكَ حَسَنَتُكَ، فَأَنْتَ مُؤْمِنٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (22159)، والطبراني في الكبير (7539)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (176) كلهم من طرق عن يحيى بن أبي كثير، عن زيد بن سلام، عن جده ممطور، قال: سمعتُ أبا أمامة (فذكر الحديث).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المعاصي من أمر الجاهلية، ولا يكفر صاحبها بارتكابها إلا بالشرك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (22159) and al-Ṭabarānī (7539), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (176).","chapter_en":"Sins Are From the Ways of the Pre-Islamic Era, and One Does Not Become a Disbeliever by Committing Them Except Through Polytheism","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “What is sin?” He replied: “When something troubles you inwardly, then leave it.” The man asked: “What is faith?” He replied: “When your bad deed saddens you and your good deed pleases you, then you are a believer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (22159)، والطبراني (7539)، وصححه ابن حبان (176)."},{"num":191,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: خَطَبَنَا عُمَرُ بِالْجَابِيَةِ، فَقَالَ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، إِنِّي قُمْتُ فِيكُمْ كَمَقَامِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِينَا، فَقَالَ: أُوصِيكُمْ بِأَصْحَابِي، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ يَفْشُو الْكَذِبُ، حَتَّى يَحْلِفَ الرَّجُلُ وَلَا يُسْتَحْلَفُ وَيَشْهَدَ الشَّاهِدُ وَلَا يُسْتَشْهَدُ، أَلَا لَا يَخْلُوَنَّ رَجُلٌ بِامْرَأَةٍ إِلَّا كَانَ ثَالِثَهُمَا الشَّيْطَانُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْجَمَاعَةِ وَإِيَّاكُمْ وَالْفُرْقَةَ فَإِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ مَعَ الْوَاحِدِ وَهُوَ مِنَ الِاثْنَيْنِ أَبْعَدُ، مَنْ أَرَادَ بُحْبُوحَةَ الْجَنَّةِ فَلْيَلْزَمْ الْجَمَاعَةَ، مَنْ سَرَّتْهُ حَسَنَتُهُ وَسَاءَتْهُ سَيِّئَتُهُ فَذَلِكَ الْمُؤْمِنُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذيّ (2165) عن أحمد بن منيع، حدثنا النّضر بن إسماعيل أبو المغيرة، عن محمد بن سوقة، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن ابن عمر، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المعاصي من أمر الجاهلية، ولا يكفر صاحبها بارتكابها إلا بالشرك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2165) and Aḥmad (114), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7254).","chapter_en":"Sins Are From the Ways of the Pre-Islamic Era, and One Does Not Become a Disbeliever by Committing Them Except Through Polytheism","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with him delivered a sermon to us at al-Jābiyah and said: “O people, I have stood among you just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stood among us, and he said: ‘I instruct you to hold fast to my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then lying will become widespread, until a man will swear an oath without being asked to swear, and a witness will testify without being asked to testify. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for Satan will be the third of them. You must remain with the united community, and beware of division, for Satan is with one person and is farther away from two. Whoever desires the central and spacious part of Paradise should adhere to the united community. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed — that person is the believer.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2165)، وأحمد (114)، وصححه ابن حبان (7254)."},{"num":192,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ مِنَ الشَّجَرِ شَجَرَةً لَا يَسْقُطُ وَرَقُهَا وَإِنَّهَا مَثَلُ الْمُسْلِمِ، فَحَدِّثُونِي مَا هِيَ؟ فَوَقَعَ النَّاسُ فِي شَجَرِ الْبَوَادِي، قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: وَوَقَعَ فِي نَفْسِي أَنَّهَا النَّخْلَةُ، ثُمَّ قَالُوا: حَدِّثْنَا مَا هِيَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: هِيَ النَّخْلَةُ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ: أَخْبِرُونِي بِشَجَرَةٍ مَثَلُهَا مَثَلُ الْمُسْلِمِ تُؤْتِي أُكُلَهَا كُلَّ حِينٍ بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهَا وَلَا تَحُتُّ وَرَقَهَا، فَوَقَعَ فِي نَفْسِي أَنَّهَا النَّخْلَةُ فَكَرِهْتُ أَنْ أَتَكَلَّمَ، وَثَمَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ فَلَمَّا لَمْ يَتَكَلَّمَا، قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هِيَ النَّخْلَةُ فَلَمَّا خَرَجْتُ مَعَ أَبِي قُلْتُ: يَا أَبَتَاهُ وَقَعَ فِي نَفْسِي أَنَّهَا النَّخْلَةُ، قَالَ: مَا مَنَعَكَ أَنْ تَقُولَهَا؟ لَوْ كُنْتَ قُلْتَهَا كَانَ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ كَذَا وَكَذَا، قَالَ: مَا مَنَعَنِي إِلَّا أَنِّي لَمْ أَرَكَ وَلَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ تَكَلَّمْتُمَا فَكَرِهْتُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في العلم (61)، ومسلم في صفات المنافقين (2811) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن ابن عمر، قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب مثل المؤمن كشجرة تؤتي أكلها كل حين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (61) and Muslim (2811). The second wording is narrated by al-Bukhārī (6144).","chapter_en":"The Believer Is Like a Tree That Gives Its Fruit at All Times","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":56,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the trees there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it resembles the Muslim. Tell me which tree it is.” The people began thinking of the trees of the desert. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: It occurred to me that it was the date palm, but I felt shy to speak. They then asked: “Tell us which tree it is, O Messenger of Allah.” He replied:","“It is the date palm.” In another narration: “Tell me of a tree whose likeness is that of the Muslim: it gives its fruit at all times by the permission of its Lord, and its leaves do not fall.” It occurred to me that it was the date palm, but I disliked speaking while Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were present. When neither of them spoke, the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is the date palm.” When I later went out with my father, I said: “Father, it occurred to me that it was the date palm.” He replied: “What prevented you from saying it? Had you said it, that would have been more beloved to me than such-and-such.” I said: “Nothing prevented me except that I did not see you or Abū Bakr speak, so I disliked speaking.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1140],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (61)، ومسلم (2811). والرواية الثانية عند البخاري (6144)."},{"num":193,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَدِيِّ بْنِ الْخِيَارِ أَخْبَرَهُ، أَنَّ الْمِقْدَادَ بْنَ عَمْرٍو الْكِنْدِيَّ، وَكَانَ حَلِيفًا لِبَنِي زُهْرَةَ وَكَانَ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخْبَرَهُ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَرَأَيْتَ إِنْ لَقِيتُ رَجُلًا مِنَ الْكُفَّارِ فَاقْتَتَلْنَا، فَضَرَبَ إِحْدَى يَدَيَّ بِالسَّيْفِ فَقَطَعَهَا، ثُمَّ لَاذَ مِنِّي بِشَجَرَةٍ، فَقَالَ: أَسْلَمْتُ لِلَّهِ، أَأَقْتُلُهُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ بَعْدَ أَنْ قَالَهَا؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَقْتُلْهُ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّهُ قَطَعَ إِحْدَى يَدَيَّ، ثُمَّ قَالَ ذَلِكَ بَعْدَ مَا قَطَعَهَا؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَقْتُلْهُ فَإِنْ قَتَلْتَهُ فَإِنَّهُ بِمَنْزِلَتِكَ قَبْلَ أَنْ تَقْتُلَهُ وَإِنَّكَ بِمَنْزِلَتِهِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَقُولَ كَلِمَتَهُ الَّتِي قَالَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازي (4019)، ومسلم في الإيمان (95) من حديث ابن شهاب الزهريّ، عن عطاء بن يزيد، عن عبيد الله بن عدي بن الخياريّ، به، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم قتل الكافر بعد أن قال لا إله إلا الله، وإن كان أوجع في المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4019) and Muslim (95).","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Killing a Disbeliever After He Says “There Is No Deity Worthy of Worship Except Allah,” Even If He Had Severely Harmed the Muslims","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":57,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khiyār reported that al-Miqdād ibn ʿAmr al-Kindī may Allah be pleased with him — an ally of Banū Zuhrah and one of those who participated in Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Suppose I encounter a man from among the disbelievers and we fight. He strikes one of my hands with his sword and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: ‘I have submitted to Allah.’ May I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Do not kill him.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands and only said that after cutting it off!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him. If you kill him, he will be in the position you were in before you killed him, and you will be in the position he was in before he uttered the statement that he said.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4019)، ومسلم (95)."},{"num":194,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ يَقُولُ: بَعَثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى الْحُرَقَةِ، فَصَبَّحْنَا الْقَوْمَ فَهَزَمْنَاهُمْ، وَلَحِقْتُ أَنَا وَرَجُلٌ مِنْ الْأَنْصَارِ رَجُلًا مِنْهُمْ فَلَمَّا غَشِينَاهُ قَالَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، فَكَفَّ الْأَنْصَارِيُّ فَطَعَنْتُهُ بِرُمْحِي حَتَّى قَتَلْتُهُ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا بَلَغَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا أُسَامَةُ، أَقَتَلْتَهُ بَعْدَ مَا قَالَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ ؟، قُلْتُ: كَانَ مُتَعَوِّذًا فَمَا زَالَ يُكَرِّرُهَا حَتَّى تَمَنَّيْتُ أَنِّي لَمْ أَكُنْ أَسْلَمْتُ قَبْلَ ذَلِكَ الْيَوْمِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازيّ (4269)، ومسلم في الإيمان (96: 159) كلاهما من طريق هشيم، أخبرنا حصين، حدثنا أبو ظبيان، قال: سمعتُ أسامة بن زيد بن حارثة يحدّث، قال (فذكره)، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم قتل الكافر بعد أن قال لا إله إلا الله، وإن كان أوجع في المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4269) and Muslim (96:159).","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Killing a Disbeliever After He Says “There Is No Deity Worthy of Worship Except Allah,” Even If He Had Severely Harmed the Muslims","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":57,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us against al-Ḥuraqah. We attacked the people at dawn and defeated them. A man from the Anṣār and I caught up with one of them. When we overtook him, he said: “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.” The Anṣārī man held back from him, but I stabbed him with my spear until I killed him. When we returned, news of this reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “O Usāmah, did you kill him after he said, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah’?” I replied: “He only said it to seek protection!” The Prophet ﷺ continued repeating the question until I wished that I had not embraced Islam before that day."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated through another route from Usāmah ibn Zayd may Allah be pleased with them:","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on an expedition. We attacked al-Ḥuraqāt of Juhaynah at dawn.","I caught up with a man who said:","“There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.”","But I stabbed him.","The matter troubled me, so I mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:","“He said, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ and you killed him?!”","I replied:","“O Messenger of Allah, he only said it out of fear of the weapon.”","He said:","“Why did you not split open his heart so that you could know whether he said it or not?!”","He continued repeating this to me until I wished that I had only embraced Islam on that very day.","Saʿd said:","“By Allah, I will not kill a Muslim until the man with the broad belly kills him” — meaning Usāmah.","A man asked:","“Did Allah not say:","‘Fight them until there is no persecution and religion is entirely for Allah’?”","[Sūrat al-Anfāl 8:39]","Saʿd replied:","“We fought until there was no persecution, whereas you and your companions wish to fight until there is persecution.”","The name «الحرقات» is formed like ʿArafāt and Adhruʿāt and refers to a place in the territory of Juhaynah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6822,7870],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4269)، ومسلم (96: 159)."},{"num":195,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جُنْدَبِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الْبَجَلِيِّ أَنَّهُ بَعَثَ إِلَى عَسْعَسِ بْنِ سَلَامَةَ زَمَنَ فِتْنَةِ ابْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ، فَقَالَ: اجْمَعْ لِي نَفَرًا مِنْ إِخْوَانِكَ حَتَّى أُحَدِّثَهُمْ، فَبَعَثَ رَسُولًا إِلَيْهِمْ، فَلَمَّا اجْتَمَعُوا، جَاءَ جُنْدَبٌ وَعَلَيْهِ بُرْنُسٌ أَصْفَرُ، فَقَالَ: تَحَدَّثُوا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَحَدَّثُونَ بِهِ حَتَّى دَارَ الْحَدِيثُ، فَلَمَّا دَارَ الْحَدِيثُ إِلَيْهِ، حَسَرَ الْبُرْنُسَ عَنْ رَأْسِهِ، فَقَالَ: إِنِّي أَتَيْتُكُمْ وَلَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أُخْبِرَكُمْ عَنْ نَبِيِّكُمْ، إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعَثَ بَعْثًا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ إِلَى قَوْمٍ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، وَإِنَّهُمُ الْتَقَوْا فَكَانَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، إِذَا شَاءَ أَنْ يَقْصِدَ إِلَى رَجُلٍ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ قَصَدَ لَهُ فَقَتَلَهُ، وَإِنَّ رَجُلًا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ قَصَدَ غَفْلَتَهُ، قَالَ: وَكُنَّا نُحَدَّثُ أَنَّهُ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ، فَلَمَّا رَفَعَ عَلَيْهِ السَّيْفَ، قَالَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهَ، فَقَتَلَهُ، فَجَاءَ الْبَشِيرُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَسَأَلَهُ، فَأَخْبَرَهُ حَتَّى أَخْبَرَهُ خَبَرَ الرَّجُلِ كَيْفَ صَنَعَ، فَدَعَاهُ فَسَأَلَهُ، فَقَالَ: لِمَ قَتَلْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهَ، أَوْجَعَ فِي الْمُسْلِمِينَ، وَقَتَلَ فُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا، وَسَمَّى لَهُ نَفَرًا، وَإِنِّي حَمَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا رَأَى السَّيْفَ، قَالَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَقَتَلْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَكَيْفَ تَصْنَعُ بِلَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، إِذَا جَاءَتْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، اسْتَغْفِرْ لِي، قَالَ: وَكَيْفَ تَصْنَعُ بِلَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، إِذَا جَاءَتْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ قَالَ: فَجَعَلَ لَا يَزِيدُهُ عَلَى أَنْ يَقُولَ: كَيْفَ تَصْنَعُ بِلَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، إِذَا جَاءَتْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ؟."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (97) عن أحمد بن الحسن بن خراش، حدثنا عمرو بن عاصم، حدثنا معمر، قال: سمعتُ أبي يحدّث أنّ خالداً الأثْبَجَ ابن أخي صفوان بن محرز، حدّث عن صفوان بن محرز، أنّه حدّث أن جندب بن عبدالله بعث، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم قتل الكافر بعد أن قال لا إله إلا الله، وإن كان أوجع في المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by Muslim (97).","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Killing a Disbeliever After He Says “There Is No Deity Worthy of Worship Except Allah,” Even If He Had Severely Harmed the Muslims","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":57,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jundub ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bajalī may Allah be pleased with him sent for ʿAsʿas ibn Salāmah during the turmoil of Ibn al-Zubayr and said: “Gather a group of your brothers for me so that I may speak to them.” He sent for them, and when they had gathered, Jundub came wearing a yellow hooded cloak. He said: “Continue speaking about what you were discussing until the conversation comes around.” When the discussion reached him, he uncovered his head and said: “I have come to you, and I intend to narrate to you from your Prophet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a detachment of Muslims against a group of polytheists, and the two sides met. There was a man among the polytheists who, whenever he targeted a Muslim, would attack and kill him. Then one of the Muslims waited for an opportunity to attack him — and we used to say that this Muslim was Usāmah ibn Zayd. When he raised his sword over the man, the man said: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.’ But he killed him. When the bearer of good news returned to the Prophet ﷺ, the Prophet asked him about what had happened. He informed him of the man’s story and what he had done. The Prophet ﷺ called him and asked: ‘Why did you kill him?’ He replied: ‘O Messenger of Allah, he had severely harmed the Muslims and killed so-and-so and so-and-so,’ and he named several people. ‘I attacked him, and when he saw the sword he said: “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.”’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: ‘Did you kill him?’ He replied: ‘Yes.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Then what will you do with “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah” when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?’ He said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.’ The Prophet ﷺ replied: ‘And what will you do with “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah” when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?!’ He continued saying nothing to him except: ‘What will you do with “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah” when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[9089],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (97)."},{"num":196,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ أَنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أَيُّمَا رَجُلٍ قَالَ لِأَخِيهِ يَا كَافِرُ فَقَدْ بَاءَ بِهَا أَحَدُهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الكلام (1) عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن عبدالله بن عمر، قال: فذكره. ورواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6104) من طريق مالك، به، مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء من التحذير في تكفير المسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (1), al-Bukhārī (6104), and Muslim (60).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Warning Against Declaring a Muslim to Be a Disbeliever","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":58,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says to his brother, ‘O disbeliever,’ then one of the two has incurred it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim added:","“If he is as the speaker said, then so it is; otherwise, it returns upon the one who said it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (1)، والبخاري (6104)، ومسلم (60)."},{"num":197,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِذَا قَالَ الرَّجُلُ لِأَخِيهِ يَا كَافِرُ فَقَدْ بَاءَ بِهِ أَحَدُهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6103) عن محمد وأحمد بن سعيد، قالا: حدثنا عثمان بن عمر، أخبرنا علي بن المبارك، عن يحيى بن أبي كثير، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء من التحذير في تكفير المسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Ṣaḥīḥ: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6102).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Warning Against Declaring a Muslim to Be a Disbeliever","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":58,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man says to his brother, ‘O disbeliever,’ then one of the two has incurred it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6103)."},{"num":198,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ثَابِتِ بْنِ الضَّحَّاكِ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ حَلَفَ بِمِلَّةٍ غَيْرِ الْإِسْلَامِ كَاذِبًا فَهُوَ كَمَا قَالَ، وَمَنْ قَتَلَ نَفْسَهُ بِشَيْءٍ عُذِّبَ بِهِ فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ، وَلَعْنُ الْمُؤْمِنِ كَقَتْلِهِ، وَمَنْ رَمَى مُؤْمِنًا بِكُفْرٍ فَهُوَ كَقَتْلِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6105)، ومسلم في الإيمان (110) كلاهما من حديث أبي قلابة، عن ثابت بن الضّحّاك، فذكر الحديث، واللفظ للبخاريّ، ولفظ مسلم مختصراً، ولم يذكر قوله: ولعن المؤمن...الخ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء من التحذير في تكفير المسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6105) and Muslim (110), with the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Warning Against Declaring a Muslim to Be a Disbeliever","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":58,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever falsely swears by a religion other than Islam is as he has said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it in the Fire of Hell. Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[6829],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6105)، ومسلم (110)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":199,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: لَا يَرْمِي رَجُلٌ رَجُلًا بِالْفُسُوقِ وَلَا يَرْمِيهِ بِالْكُفْرِ، إِلَّا ارْتَدَّتْ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ صَاحِبُهُ كَذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الأدب (6045)، ومسلم في الإيمان (61) كلاهما من حديث عبدالوارث، عن الحسين المعلم، عن عبدالله بن بريدة، حدثني يحيى بن يعمر، أنّ أبا الأسود الدّيليّ حدّثه، عن أبي ذر، فذكر الحديث،","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء من التحذير في تكفير المسلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الإيمان","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6045) and Muslim (61).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Concerning the Warning Against Declaring a Muslim to Be a Disbeliever","part_en":"The Book of Faith","group_ar":"مجموع أبواب خصال الإيمان","group_en":"Collection of Chapters on the Characteristics of Faith","part_no":2,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":58,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr may Allah be pleased with him reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No man accuses another of sinful wickedness or accuses him of disbelief except that the accusation returns upon him if the other person is not as he said.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14879],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6045)، ومسلم (61)."}]);